const ANSWERS_EN={"019fa1bc-8512-4253-b278-c9a7dd74c2be": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric producer. Its notable facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP with 582.1 MW, and the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant with 500 MW. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   It operates 15 active power plants with 526.2 MWe of installed capacity. Through its hydroelectric, wind and geothermal investments, the company contributes to Türkiye's transition to a low-carbon economy. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://www.turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   With 36 plants and 4,500+ MW of installed capacity, it is one of Türkiye's largest private sector electricity producers. Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants. ([enerjisauretim.com.tr](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Merge Enerji**\n   Developing hydroelectric, wind and solar energy projects since 2005, the company operates the Duru-1 and Duru-2 hydroelectric plants in Amasya, with installed capacities of 5.29 MW and 5.40 MW. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n   Founded in 2000, the company contributes to environmentally friendly power generation with 8 hydroelectric plants, 1 wind farm and 6 solar plants with a capacity of 205 MW. ([tektug.com](https://www.tektug.com/enerji-uretimi-ve-satisi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Kurtsuyu Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n   With 68.74 MW of installed capacity through the Daran Hydroelectric Plant, the company generates an average of 278 million kWh of energy per year. ([kurtsuyu.com.tr](https://kurtsuyu.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Enova Enerji Şirketi**\n   Founded by Özaltın İnşaat and Nurol Yatırım Şirketleri, Enova Enerji is the owner and operator of the Berkman Dam and HPP in Osmaniye, with 39 MW of installed capacity. ([ozaltin.com](https://www.ozaltin.com/tr/tum-projeler/baraj-ve-hes-projeleri/berkman-dam-and-hepp/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Energo Pro**\n   With a total of 5 hydroelectric plants in Sivas, Tokat, Ankara and Artvin and around 100 MW of installed capacity, the company aims to meet the electricity needs of 610 thousand households by the end of 2020. ([turkiyegazetesi.com.tr](https://www.turkiyegazetesi.com.tr/ekonomi/energo-pro-610-bin-haneyi-aydinlatacak-610351?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and contribute to environmentally friendly energy production by increasing the use of renewable energy sources.", "0214448c-fa70-45ec-8edd-dd7ca940a360": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers are determined according to the \"MW100 Türkiye's Largest 100 Electricity Producers Survey\" reports, prepared in cooperation between the international consulting firm Kearney and Enerji Günlüğü. These reports are based on the installed capacity companies held as of 31 December 2024. Although the public entity EÜAŞ ranks first in total installed capacity, there are many important companies that stand out in the private sector.\n\nHere are some of Türkiye's leading private electricity producers:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - It is the largest electricity producer in Türkiye's private sector. As of 31 December 2024, it has 3,978 MWe of installed capacity. This capacity represents approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. Although the installed capacity of ENKA's plants is high, generation at its natural gas plants may at times decline due to market conditions.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks third with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity as of 31 December 2024 and is closing in on ENKA with new plants. The company has a variety of sources, including hydroelectric, wind and solar power plants.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Standing out with 3,161 MWe of installed capacity as of 31 December 2024, Cengiz Enerji has a balanced source mix. According to Enerji Atlası data, it has 16 plants and 4,480 MW of installed capacity.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It rose to fifth place with 3,033 MWe of installed capacity as of 31 December 2024. Limak Enerji's G4 Erzin 1 SPP, with 100 MWe of installed capacity, is among the important investments commissioned in 2024. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 16 plants and 3,638 MW of installed capacity.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - It is one of the companies in the top 10 according to the MW100 survey. According to 2019 data, it has 2,824 MWe of installed capacity. In Enerji Atlası, it is listed as Eren Holding Enerji Grubu with 3 plants and 2,810 MW of installed capacity.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - It is in the top 10 according to the MW100 survey. According to 2019 data, it has 2,713 MWe of installed capacity. In Enerji Atlası, it is listed as Çelikler Holding Enerji Grubu with 12 plants and 2,769 MW of installed capacity.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - Having seen significant increases in its total installed capacity in 2024, Aydem Enerji has 1,965 MWe of installed capacity according to 2019 data. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji, which also operates in renewable energy, has 19 plants and 1,121 MW of installed capacity.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - It is one of the companies in the top 10 according to the MW100 survey. According to 2019 data, it has 1,665 MWe of installed capacity. As IC İçtaş Enerji Üretim ve Ticaret A.Ş., it has 4 plants and 1,131 MW of installed capacity. IC İçtaş Enerji's G4 Erzin 2 SPP, with 78 MWe of installed capacity, was also commissioned in 2024.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - It is in the top 10 according to the MW100 survey. According to 2019 data, it has 1,580 MWe of installed capacity. Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding A.Ş. has 12 plants and 1,733 MW of installed capacity.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - It is one of the companies that achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024. It has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio with its solar power plant (SPP) investment in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ. Kalyon Holding Enerji Grubu has 6 plants and 1,399 MW of installed capacity.\n11. **Aksa Enerji** - With more than 3,000 MW of installed capacity, it aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity by making approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments under its 2030 strategy. In addition to Türkiye, it has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n12. **Zorlu Enerji** - It stands out as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers. Its total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW belongs to domestic plants. The company has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in Türkiye. In Enerji Atlası, Zorlu Enerji Grubu is listed with 14 plants and 612 MW of installed capacity.\n\nThese companies make up a significant portion of the private sector's share in Türkiye's electricity generation and stand out particularly for their investments in renewable energy sources.", "040e8259-9ebf-46c6-877e-e22a61d01af5": "The main companies that build, operate or lead the sector in large-scale solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n- **Kalyon Holding** : With the [Kalyon Karapınar Solar Power Plant](https://kalyonholding.com/enerji/ges/karapinar-ges), which it built in Karapınar, Konya, with **1,350 MWp** of installed capacity, it has delivered one of the largest SPP projects in Türkiye and Europe.[[1]](https://kalyonholding.com/enerji/ges/karapinar-ges)\n- **CW Enerji** : It is one of the leading firms carrying out large rooftop and ground-mounted SPP projects in various provinces of Türkiye and at factories, while also manufacturing solar panels.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4UGDCTGL8OWVNaaCEquYVcyGfXA3HxGceBOGFBM3LD6RI989pT4)[[2]](https://tr.linkedin.com/posts/enerji-life_ges-ile-elektrik-%C3%BCretimi-yayg%C4%B1nla%C5%9F%C4%B1yor-t%C3%BCrkiye-activity-7161652584825528321-upzu)\n- **Limak Yenilenebilir Enerji** : With the Erzin-1 SPP project, which it built in Erzin, Hatay, and which reached **140 MW** of installed capacity, it has brought one of Türkiye's largest solar plants to life.[[1]](https://www.haberturk.com/turkiye-nin-ikinci-en-buyuk-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kismi-olarak-devreye-alindi-3715547-ekonomi)\n- **Esenboğa Elektrik** : By incorporating numerous SPP projects belonging to Kinesis AŞ, it has become one of Türkiye's largest solar portfolio owners.[[1]](https://www.ntv.com.tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-solar-portfoy-sahibi-esenboga-elektrik-oldu,izEkk95hBkKUAzcB00MOqA)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** : With the *Solentegre SPP* it built in Elazığ, it brought one of Türkiye's first licensed solar power plants to life.[[1]](https://www.patronlardunyasi.com/turkiyenin-ilk-lisansli-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-enerji-uretmeye-basladi)\n- **Tekno Ray Solar** : It has developed large-scale solar plant projects with high capacity and advanced technological infrastructure, such as the Konya Kızören SPP.[[1]](http://www.enerjimagazin.com/haber-4549-Turkiyenin-En-Buyuk-Gunes-Enerjisi-Santrali-Resmen-Aciliyor.html)\n- **Alfa Solar Enerji & Naturel Enerji** : They are among the important energy players carrying out both panel manufacturing and large-scale plant installations across Türkiye.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4UGDCTGL8OWVNaaCEquYVcyGfXA3HxGceBOGFBM3LD6RI989pT4)\n\nIf you are curious about **a specific region**, **a company's financial/technical details** or **the differences between rooftop and ground-mounted installations** in solar energy investments, I can go into more detail.", "04dff98d-0659-402e-994e-dfe6e1492c86": "There are many large energy companies installing solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye. These companies play a critical role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are some of the large energy companies that stand out in this field:\n\n1.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in Istanbul in 2014, the company is an R&D-focused technology firm. It offers solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells, and aims to reach 2,000 MW of cell production by the end of 2025.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is one of the pioneers of Türkiye's renewable energy sector. A significant portion of the company's total installed capacity comes from renewable sources. While it has seven hydroelectric, one wind, four geothermal and two natural gas plants in Türkiye, it also carries out various energy projects abroad, including solar power plants.\n3.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is one of Türkiye's leading companies in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. Within Enerjisa Üretim, there are two solar power plants in operation in Bandırma and Karabük with a total installed capacity of 9 MW. It is also carrying out hybrid plant conversions in which generation with solar technology will start at its existing plants.\n4.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, it has been traded on Borsa İstanbul since 2010. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity by making approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments. In addition to Türkiye, it has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n5.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - One of Türkiye's leading renewable energy companies, Akfen generates power at 59 plants with more than 774 MW of installed capacity. Its portfolio covers hydroelectric, wind, solar and hybrid plants. The company has solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed).\n6.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Founded in 2011, Alfa Solar Enerji offers reliable and efficient solutions to Türkiye's growing energy needs. At its facility in the Kırıkkale Organised Industrial Zone, with 40,000 m² of indoor space, it manufactures high-efficiency solar panels with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW.\n7.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - Thanks to its solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp, it has become one of the notable players in the sector. It has also completed a 61 MWp SPP installation abroad on a turnkey basis and taken on the operation and maintenance of these facilities.\n8.  **Aydem Enerji** - Known as the founder of our country's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind farms, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant. The company also keeps renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects.\n9.  **Göktekin Enerji** - Founded in Adana in 2015 by Abdullah Göktekin, Göktekin Enerji is an EPC (Engineering, Procurement and Construction) engineering firm. It carries out industrial-scale sustainable energy projects and investments across Türkiye and has delivered many ground-mounted and rooftop SPP projects.\n10. **Liva Enerji** - Closely following developments in the solar power generation sector, Liva Enerji has achieved important reference projects in turnkey Solar Power Plant (SPP) installation, in both rooftop and ground-mounted applications. It serves all of Türkiye with offices in Istanbul, Gaziantep, Ankara and Bursa.\n11. **IBT Solar** - As one of Türkiye's pioneering firms in photovoltaic systems since 2013, it provides services across the country with standards-compliant applications and expert teams.", "06b938d1-ade9-44a6-81be-72f1ada9cc1b": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers vary according to their installed capacity. Although the public entity EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.) ranks first in total installed capacity, there are many large players that stand out in the private sector.\n\nSome of Türkiye's leading private electricity producers are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA Enerji Elektrik Üretim** - It is Türkiye's largest private electricity producer. As of the end of 2024, it has 3,978 MWe of installed capacity, which represents approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. ENKA's plants are mostly natural gas based.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim is one of the important players in the sector with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity as of the end of 2024. The company has a balanced source mix with hydroelectric, wind and solar power plants. Enerjisa Üretim has 12 hydroelectric, five wind and two solar power plants.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji San. ve Tic. A.Ş.** - It stands out with 3,161 MWe of installed capacity as of the end of 2024. The company has 16 plants and is notable for its balanced source mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji A.Ş.** - It reached 3,033 MWe of installed capacity as of the end of 2024. Limak Enerji operates with various energy projects across Türkiye. The company has 16 plants.\n5.  **Eren Holding Enerji Grubu** - With 2,810 MWe of installed capacity, it is one of the important private producers. The group has 3 plants.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding Enerji Grubu** - It has 2,769 MWe of installed capacity and generates electricity with 12 plants.\n7.  **Özaltın İnşaat Enerji A.Ş.** - It is on the list with 1,888 MWe of installed capacity. The company has 7 plants.\n8.  **OYAK - Ordu Yardımlaşma Kurumu** - It operates in the energy sector with 1,789 MWe of installed capacity. OYAK has 11 plants.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding A.Ş.** - It has 1,733 MWe of installed capacity and generates power with 12 plants.\n10. **İÇDAŞ Elektrik Enerjisi Üretim A.Ş.** - It has 1,665 MWe of installed capacity and operates 3 plants.\n11. **Akenerji** - It is in the sector with 1,221 MWe of installed capacity and has 9 plants.\n12. **Aydem Enerji** - Focused on renewable energy sources, Aydem Enerji operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind farms, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant. In 2024, its total installed capacity increased by 179 megawatts. According to Enerji Atlası data, Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji AŞ has 1,121 MW of installed capacity and 19 plants.", "083c275e-0a50-4c7c-bf95-fff1a8bdbd1f": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Zorlu Enerji**\n   It is one of the companies with the largest renewable energy investments in Türkiye. It has a broad portfolio in solar, wind and geothermal. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Enerji**\n   It is an important renewable energy producer with its wind and hydroelectric plants. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aksa Enerji**\n   It contributes to renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   It contributes to Türkiye's energy generation with its solar, wind and hydroelectric power plants. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Borusan EnBW Enerji**\n   It stands out especially for its wind energy projects. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Kalyon Enerji**\n   It is making significant investments in solar energy. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Aydem Enerji**\n   It contributes to renewable energy generation with its hydroelectric, wind and geothermal power plants. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Eksim Enerji**\n   It is one of the companies rapidly expanding its renewable energy portfolio. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Polat Enerji**\n   It is strengthening its position in the sector with its wind and solar energy projects. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Akenerji Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n    It contributes to renewable energy generation with its hydroelectric and wind plants. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies play an important role in Türkiye's renewable energy sector and contribute to sustainable energy generation.", "08b67f3a-ece6-4006-8011-21ca166f2868": "The leading private sector companies that generate the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye and hold large HPP (Hydroelectric Power Plant) portfolios include **Enerjisa Üretim**, **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji**, **Cengiz Enerji**, **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** and **Akenerji**.[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[3]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)[[4]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n\n### Leading Private Companies and Their Projects\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It is among Türkiye's largest private electricity producers, and its portfolio includes a significant share of renewable energy and hydroelectric plants.[[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** The [Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji) in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, is the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector in Türkiye.[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n- **[Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr):** In its portfolio, made up entirely of renewable sources, it operates many hydroelectric plants, including high-capacity HPPs such as Göktaş I-II in Adana.[[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)[[2]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** With numerous HPPs in different regions, it is one of the prominent players in Türkiye's renewable and hydroelectric generation.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Akenerji:** With important hydroelectric assets such as the Uluabat HPP and the Feke projects, it has a strong HPP portfolio in the sector.[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)\n\nIf you wish, we can look in more detail at:\n\n- The **total installed capacity ranking** of these companies\n- Which company **operates which large dam**\n\nHow would you like to continue?", "0c3ba192-c657-4f4d-9c4e-ea127178fc95": "Among Türkiye's largest private electricity producers, **Eren Enerji**, **ENKA** and **Enerjisa Üretim** rank at the top.[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)Other large private sector electricity producers that stand out by overall generation volume and size are as follows:\n\n- **Eren Enerji**\n- **ENKA**\n- **Enerjisa Üretim**\n- **İÇDAŞ**\n- **Limak Enerji**\n- **Cengiz Enerji**\n- **EMBA Power**\n- **Çelikler Holding**\n- **Aydem Enerji** [](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[3]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)\n\n*(Note: The largest overall player in electricity generation in Türkiye is the public entity Elektrik Üretim AŞ - EÜAŞ, but the companies above are the leaders in the private sector.)* [](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)Would you like more detailed information about these companies' **generation types (coal, natural gas, renewables)** or **installed capacities**?", "0d53134a-566e-4139-ac54-03a918642b79": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies contribute to the country's sustainable energy targets by investing in different renewable energy sources such as wind, solar, hydroelectric and geothermal. Here are some important companies operating in this field:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji** - One of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji is the country's largest producer, particularly in geothermal energy. A significant portion of the company's total installed capacity comes from renewable sources, and it has hydroelectric, wind and geothermal plants.\n\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim (Enerjisa Enerji)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa makes significant investments in renewable energy generation in addition to electricity distribution and retail sales. With various renewable energy plants, the company is among Türkiye's leading energy companies.\n\n3.  **Aydem Enerji** - The founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind farms, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant. The company also keeps renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects.\n\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Focused on renewable energy investments, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji has significant installed capacity with both hydroelectric and wind plants. The company generates renewable energy at a capacity able to meet a significant portion of Türkiye's energy needs.\n\n5.  **Aksa Enerji** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji aims to increase its renewable energy investments under its 2030 strategy. The company has completed the licensing processes for wind farms with storage and also has energy investments abroad in addition to Türkiye.\n\n6.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - With 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity, it is one of Türkiye's leading wind generation companies. It also has hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 50.3 MW.\n\n7.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji owns large wind farms such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP and Göktepe WPP. Geycek WPP in particular is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n\n8.  **Gürmat Elektrik Üretim A.Ş. (GÜRİŞ)** - It is one of the companies that stand out in geothermal energy generation. By building and operating geothermal power plants in Germencik, Aydın, it is among the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy.\n\n9.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and has geothermal, hydroelectric and wind power plants. The company also plays an active role in carbon emissions trading.\n\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - With its solar power plant (SPP) investment in Viranşehir, Şanlıurfa, together with its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ, it has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio.\n\nThese companies play a key role in meeting Türkiye's growing energy needs and achieving environmental sustainability targets.", "0df461d2-6de0-423a-ab32-1e7a036b9b2e": "**ENKA**, **Enerjisa Üretim** and **Eren Enerji** stand out among Türkiye's largest private electricity producers. After the public entity EÜAŞ, the main private sector companies with the highest electricity generation and installed capacity are as follows:[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** It is one of the largest producers, at the top of the private sector in both installed capacity and total generation rankings.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** Through the partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, it has a large installed capacity and portfolio.\n- **Eren Enerji:** With its thermal power plants in Zonguldak, it is a leader among the private sector companies generating the most electricity in Türkiye.\n- **İÇDAŞ:** In addition to iron and steel production, it also has a large share in the energy sector.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** It is among the leading producers with its natural gas and hydroelectric plants.\n- **Limak Enerji and EMBA Power:** They rank high on the list with large thermal/energy investments such as Çatalağzı and Hunsun.\n- Explore the comprehensive analysis on [Anadolu Ajansı](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590).\n- Read the detailed industry report from [Enerji Günlüğü](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm).[[1]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)[[4]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[5]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)\n\nIf you wish, I can provide more detailed information about these companies' **installed capacities (MW)** or **renewable energy investments**.", "13f56170-f764-47e0-b0ae-cac267180c7e": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies contribute to the country's sustainable energy targets by generating energy from various sources such as solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal. Here are some important companies operating in this field:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's leading domestic energy companies, Zorlu Enerji generates power from solar, wind and geothermal sources. In particular, it is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy producer. The company has hydroelectric, wind, geothermal and solar plants both in Türkiye and abroad.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA) / Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is an important player in renewable energy generation in addition to electricity distribution and retail sales. Enerjisa Üretim has 12 hydroelectric plants, five wind farms and two solar power plants.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji is focusing on renewable energy investments under its 2030 strategy. The company has completed the licensing processes for wind farms with storage in locations such as Mersin and Balıkesir.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - With a 100 percent renewable energy portfolio, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji stands out with its hydroelectric and wind plants. The company has 12 HPPs in different regions of Türkiye, with a total installed capacity of 228.7 MW.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji / Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - The founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji also keeps renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects. The company has 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind farms, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant.\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. The company has production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa, with a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n7.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Offering reliable and efficient solutions to Türkiye's growing energy needs, Alfa Solar Enerji manufactures high-efficiency solar panels at its facility in Kırıkkale with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW.\n8.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is one of the important companies operating in the renewable energy sector.\n9.  **Kalyon Enerji** - Known as Türkiye's largest solar energy company, Kalyon Enerji operates Türkiye's largest solar power plant in Karapınar, with 1,350 MW of installed capacity. It also established Türkiye's first domestic solar panel factory in Ankara.\n10. **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji has important wind farms such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP, Göktepe WPP, Poyraz WPP, Ege WPP and Seyitali WPP. Soma WPP in particular, with 328.9 MWm of installed capacity, is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe. Geycek WPP is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n11. **Sanko Enerji** - Part of Sanko Holding, which began energy investments in 1997, Sanko Enerji has a broad portfolio in renewable energy.\n12. **Cengiz Enerji** - With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is the largest private sector producer in this field in Türkiye. The Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP is Türkiye's largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector. In addition, the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant is Türkiye's first and Europe's largest hybrid power plant.\n13. **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - Operating within IC Holding, the company has a total installed capacity of approximately 388 MW with 9 hydroelectric plants.\n14. **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding (MOGAN)** - One of the new energy companies to start trading on Borsa İstanbul, it has a hydroelectric plant portfolio.", "159f3268-9680-4588-9f16-c029033c969b": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies generally invest in different renewable energy sources such as wind, solar, hydroelectric and geothermal. Here are some important companies operating in this field:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy producer and also generates power from solar, wind and hydroelectric sources.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - In addition to electricity distribution and retail, it offers customer solutions such as solar systems, e-mobility (Eşarj) and energy efficiency. Its generation portfolio also includes hydroelectric and wind plants.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - It is one of Türkiye's largest publicly traded independent power producers and has renewable energy investments.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - It is a company with significant investments in renewable energy.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, and a significant portion of its total installed capacity consists of HPPs.\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - It is an important company operating in solar energy and manufacturing solar panels.\n7.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - It is one of the firms that stand out among domestic solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye.\n8.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind energy investments.\n9.  **Akenerji (AKENR)** - Its operating hydroelectric plant (HPP) portfolio is around 289 MW, and its portfolio also includes wind and natural gas plants.\n10. **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding (MOGAN)** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul with hydroelectric plants in its renewable energy portfolio.\n11. **Eksim Enerji** - With its wind power plant (WPP) investments, it is one of the few private sector WPP producers in Türkiye to exceed the 1 GW threshold.\n12. **Kalyon Holding** - It is among the domestic solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye.\n13. **CW Enerji** - It is one of the firms that stand out among the many domestic solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye.\n14. **Naturel Enerji** - It is among the domestic solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye.\n15. **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - It is one of the companies that started trading on Borsa İstanbul and operates in renewable energy.\n\nAmong the international and domestic firms manufacturing wind turbines or providing services in this field in Türkiye are companies such as TPI Composites Türkiye, Siemens Gamesa Türkiye, Nordex Türkiye, GE Renewable Energy and Enercon Türkiye. Solar panel manufacturers such as Daxler Energy also contribute to Türkiye's renewable energy sector.", "16898208-308e-411d-a17e-8715d7043945": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)**\n   It is one of the companies with the largest renewable energy investments in Türkiye. It has a broad portfolio in solar, wind and geothermal. It is one of Türkiye's largest players, particularly in geothermal energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)**\n   Operating in electricity generation, distribution and retail sales, Enerjisa Enerji contributes to renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants. By investing in sustainable energy projects, it aims to reduce its carbon footprint. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)**\n   With a broad portfolio in energy generation and trading, Aksa Enerji focuses on renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants. It is strengthening its position in the sector by offering innovative solutions in energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)**\n   Contributing to Türkiye's energy generation with its solar, wind and hydroelectric power plants, Akfen is known for its environmentally friendly energy projects and continues to meet Türkiye's energy needs by increasing energy efficiency. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Borusan EnBW Enerji (BRMEN)**\n   An important player in Türkiye's renewable energy sector, Borusan EnBW Enerji stands out especially for its wind energy projects. It owns some of Türkiye's largest wind farms and is continuously increasing its renewable energy investments. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Aydem Enerji (AYDEM)**\n   Operating in electricity generation, distribution and retail with more than 40 years of experience, Aydem Enerji focuses on renewable energy and generates power from hydroelectric, wind and geothermal sources. With more than 12 thousand employees, it adopts an approach that is sensitive to society and the environment. ([a1capital.com.tr](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Kalyon Enerji**\n   Operating in solar energy, Kalyon Enerji owns one of Türkiye's largest solar energy projects with the 1,000 MW Karapınar Solar Power Plant. It is also increasing its presence in the sector with local panel manufacturing and storage projects. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Polat Enerji**\n   Operating with wind and solar energy projects, Polat Enerji has 500+ MW of wind capacity. It is increasing its renewable energy investments through technology partnerships. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Say Yenilenebilir Enerji Ekipmanları A.Ş. (SAYAS)**\n   Designing and manufacturing equipment such as wind turbine tower internal/external components and blade, generator and rotor transport fixtures, SAYAS is one of the first firms in Türkiye to offer integrated solutions. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)**\n    Founded in Istanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, the company has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies play an important role in Türkiye's renewable energy sector and contribute to the country's energy transition.", "1801438a-8882-4f98-9f91-3623b6a21b33": "There are many private companies generating hydroelectric power in Türkiye. Here are some of the private companies that stand out in this field and their key features:\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric power producers. It generates clean energy with six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity. It stands out in particular with the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl, which, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, is the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector in Türkiye. It also owns Türkiye's second largest private sector hydroelectric plant, the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP, with 582.1 MW of installed capacity. The company's Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant, with 500 MW of installed capacity, is Türkiye's first and Europe's largest hybrid power plant and generates energy from water and the sun.\n2.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants. The total installed capacity of these HPPs is 852.1 MWm, representing 71.1% of the company's total installed capacity of 1,198 MWm. The company is known as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The Bereket 1 and 2 Hydroelectric Plants (3.15 MW in total) and the Dereli Hydroelectric Plant (49.2 MW) are among its notable HPPs.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - It is one of the companies with a 100% renewable energy portfolio. Its hydroelectric portfolio includes 12 HPPs operating in different regions of Türkiye. The total installed capacity of these plants is 228.7 MW, and their annual generation capacity is approximately 895 GWh. The HPP facilities are located in different basins such as the Sakarya, Kızılırmak and Çoruh rivers.\n4.  **Akenerji (AKENR)** - Its operating HPP portfolio has around 289 MW of hydroelectric installed capacity. The Yamula HPP on the Kızılırmak River, with 100 MW of installed capacity, and the Büyükdüz HPP in Gümüşhane, with 68.9 MW of installed capacity, are among the company's notable hydroelectric assets. The company has a total of 388 MWe of installed capacity.\n5.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is a company focused on the use of clean energy that prioritises domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation. It currently has 12 hydroelectric plants. The company's total installed capacity is around 3,901 MWe.\n6.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It continues its operations with seven hydroelectric plants. The company supports Türkiye in reaching its renewable energy targets.\n7.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding (MOGAN)** - The company directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and has Geothermal, Hydroelectric and Wind Power Plants. Following the public offerings in the 2024-2025 period, the company was added to the list of Borsa İstanbul HPP stocks.\n8.  **Ayen Enerji (AYEN)** - In addition to its hydroelectric assets in Türkiye, it also has HPP investments in Albania. In Türkiye, the Yamula HPP on the Kızılırmak River, with 100 MW of installed capacity, and the Büyükdüz HPP in Gümüşhane, with 68.9 MW of installed capacity, are among the company's notable hydroelectric assets.\n9.  **Hun Yenilenebilir Enerji (HUNER)** - Its hydroelectric portfolio consists of two HPPs in the Tortum district of Erzurum: Büyükbahçe HPP (12.10 MW) and Bağbaşı HPP (14.00 MW).\n10. **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - Following the public offerings in the 2024-2025 period, it was added to the list of Borsa İstanbul HPP stocks.\n11. **Enda Enerji Holding (ENDAE)** - Following the public offerings in the 2024-2025 period, it was added to the list of Borsa İstanbul HPP stocks.", "1a18f479-a986-458e-b481-f3cca194f942": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers stand out for their investments in various energy sources and their installed capacity. Although the public entity EÜAŞ ranks first in total installed capacity, the major players in the private sector also make a large contribution to the country's electricity generation capacity.\n\nAccording to the \"MW100, Türkiye's Largest 100 Electricity Producers Survey\" conducted as of 31 December 2024, Türkiye's leading private electricity producers are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - It is one of the largest companies in the private sector in terms of installed capacity. With 3,978 MWe of installed capacity, it represents 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. Although the installed capacity of ENKA's plants is high, generation at its natural gas plants may decline due to market conditions.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim holds an important place in the private sector with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity. It continues to increase its installed capacity with newly commissioned plants. The company also plays a major role in renewable energy.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with 3,161 MWe of installed capacity, Cengiz Enerji stands out for its balanced source mix. According to Enerji Atlası data, it has 16 plants and 4,480 MW of installed capacity.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - With 3,033 MWe of installed capacity, it is one of the leading firms in the private sector. It stands out with investments such as the G4 Erzin 1 SPP, with 100 MWe of installed capacity, commissioned in 2024. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 16 plants and 3,638 MW of installed capacity.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - According to the MW100 2022 survey, it is among the companies generating the most electricity. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 3 plants and 2,810 MW of installed capacity.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - According to the MW100 2022 survey, it is among the top 10 electricity producers. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 12 plants and 2,769 MW of installed capacity.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is known as the founder of our country's first private hydroelectric plant and focuses on renewable energy. In 2024, its total installed capacity increased by 179 megawatts. According to Enerji Atlası, Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji AŞ has 19 plants and 1,121 MW, and Aydem Enerji has 2 plants and 981 MW of installed capacity.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - According to the MW100 2022 survey, it is among the companies generating the most electricity. It has investments such as the G4 Erzin 2 SPP, with 78 MWe of installed capacity, commissioned in 2024. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 3 plants and 1,665 MW of installed capacity.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - Although it is in the top 10 of the installed capacity list, it did not make the top 10 in electricity generation. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 12 plants and 1,733 MW of installed capacity.\n10. **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, it is traded on Borsa İstanbul. In total, it has 11 plants in 7 countries and more than 3,000 MW of installed capacity. Under its 2030 strategy, it aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity by making approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 2 plants and 1,170 MW of installed capacity.\n11. **Zorlu Enerji** - It continues its operations with seven hydroelectric and three wind power plants and supports Türkiye's renewable energy targets. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW.\n12. **Kalyon Enerji** - It achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024. Thanks to its solar power plant (SPP) in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ, it has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 6 plants and 1,399 MW of installed capacity.\n13. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates with diversified modern power plants commissioned in many regions of Türkiye over the last five years. Excluding its projects currently at the permitting stage, it is stated to have 699 MWe of installed capacity. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 31 plants and 638 MW of installed capacity.\n14. **Sanko Enerji** - According to Enerji Atlası, it has 17 plants and 977 MW of installed capacity.\n15. **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - According to Enerji Atlası, it has 18 plants and 949 MW of installed capacity.\n16. **Polat Enerji** - According to Enerji Atlası, it has 13 plants and 872 MW of installed capacity.\n\nThese companies play an important role in meeting Türkiye's energy needs and in building a sustainable future, particularly through their investments in renewable energy sources.", "1b5807a9-42aa-40b0-b904-49443846db7f": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye make significant contributions to the country's renewable energy targets. According to January 2026 data, Türkiye's largest wind investors include many established and new companies.\n\nThe main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of Türkiye's largest wind energy investors. As of January 2026, it has 1,035 MW of installed capacity. The company generates electricity at a total of 18 wind farms in Akhisar, Akköy, Armutçuk, Arturna, Aydos, Balıkesir, Çanakkale, Çeşme, Dağpazarı, Dampınar, Dikili, Erciyes, Hacıhıdırlar, Harmancık, Ihlamur, Kestanederesi, Ovacık and Uygar. It will also continue its 1,000 MW of wind energy investments under the YEKA 2 tenders.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - It is one of the important wind energy players in Türkiye and has 773 MW of installed capacity as of January 2026.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy. As of January 2026, it has reached 772 MW of installed capacity. The company has plants such as Seyitali WPP (İzmir).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - Although it is not traded on Borsa İstanbul, Eksim Enerji, part of Eksim Holding, is among Türkiye's largest private sector wind energy players. As of January 2026, it has 733 MW of installed capacity.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It is another firm with significant investments in the wind energy sector. As of January 2026, it has 702 MW of installed capacity. It has projects such as Kocatepe WPP and Fatma WPP.\n6.  **Galata Wind** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind energy investments.\n7.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the important companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that also include wind energy in their renewable energy portfolio.\n8.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the firms traded on Borsa İstanbul that are notable for their wind energy investments.\n9.  **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind energy investments.\n10. **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of the large energy companies that also have wind power plants in their renewable energy portfolio.\n11. **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates various wind farms such as Düzova WPP, Ziyaret WPP and Salman WPP.\n\nIn addition to these firms, companies such as Akenerji (with Ayyıldız WPP in Balıkesir) and Ayen Enerji also operate in the wind energy sector. Türkiye is one of the few countries that has built its own supply chain in wind energy and holds an important position in terms of industry thanks to its domestic manufacturing capacity.", "1cfa3b0c-f436-4c3a-9a5e-997f5747dc08": "According to data from the [Turkish Wind Energy Association (TÜREB)](https://tureb.tr/), the leader among the main firms operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye is **Enerjisa Üretim, with installed capacity exceeding 1,119 MW**. While installed wind power capacity across Türkiye is approaching the 16,000 MW mark, the largest share of the sector is held by five large domestic energy giants.[](https://tureb.tr/) [[1]](https://tureb.tr/)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)[[3]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)Türkiye's Largest Wind Energy Investors\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It is the clear leader of Türkiye's wind energy market. The company is among the first producers to exceed the 1 GW mark in wind.\n- **Borusan EnBW Enerji:** With approximately 775 MW of capacity, it is the second largest wind energy operator in the market.\n- **Eksim Enerji:** With WPP investments in important regions such as Geyve and Yozgat, it has 774 MW of installed capacity.\n- **Polat Enerji:** As one of the most established players in the sector, it operates 771 MW of wind capacity.\n- **GÜRİŞ Holding:** With 702 MW of installed capacity, it is among the top 5 investors in wind energy.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-kurulu-gucu-14-gwi-asti-yatirim-portfoyu-26-gw-seviyesine-ulasti/)[[3]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)\n\nOther Major WPP Companies Traded on Borsa İstanbul In addition to these large-scale leaders, other prominent publicly traded firms on Borsa İstanbul (BIST) with direct wind power plant portfolios and hybrid projects are as follows:[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\n- **Galata Wind Enerji (GWIND):** A Doğan Holding affiliate, the company is entirely focused on clean energy and operates large plants such as Şah WPP and Mersin WPP.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji (AYDEM):** It is an important renewable energy player that allocates a large share of its portfolio to wind energy.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It has a mixed green energy portfolio made up of wind, solar and hydroelectric plants.\n- **Tatlıpınar Enerji (TATEN):** It is growing with its wind investments in the Balıkesir region and its WPP projects with storage.\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** In addition to its geothermal investments, it also generates wind energy.[](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) [[1]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)[[2]](https://www.hocaileborsa.com/haber/borsadaki-ruzgar-enerjisi-sirketleri-hangileri)[[3]](https://www.hisse.net/haber/ruzgar-enerjisinde-2026-beklentisi-borsada-hangi-sirketler-one-cikabilir-47554)[[4]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\nWhich are the largest wind farms in the sector?Leading Türkiye's largest wind farms operated as a single unit are **Soma WPP** (İş Enerji) in Manisa and **Karaburun WPP** (Alto Holding) in İzmir.[](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/) [[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)Would you like to look at **projects in a specific region** in wind energy investments, or would you like details on these listed companies' **WPP projects with storage**?", "20925623-43fc-4669-b173-5f15b67d4293": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers stand out for their investments in various energy sources and their installed capacity. Despite the weight of the public entity EÜAŞ in the sector, private sector companies make up a significant portion of total electricity generation capacity.\n\nAccording to data announced by the MW100 Türkiye's Largest 100 Electricity Producers Survey as of 31 December 2024, Türkiye's leading private electricity producers are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - The largest player among private sector companies in terms of installed capacity, ENKA represents approximately 3.4 percent of Türkiye's total generation capacity with 3,978 MWe of installed capacity. The company's plants are mostly natural gas based, but generation activity may vary due to market conditions.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim is the third largest electricity producer with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity and has come very close to ENKA. Enerjisa's areas of activity include business lines such as distribution, retail and customer solutions (solar systems, e-mobility, energy efficiency).\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with 3,161 MWe of installed capacity, Cengiz Enerji stands out for its balanced source mix. According to Enerji Atlası data, it has 16 plants and 4,480 MW of installed capacity.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - Rising to fifth place with 3,033 MWe, Limak Enerji has increased its capacity with investments such as the G4 Erzin 1 SPP commissioned in 2024. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 16 plants and 3,638 MW of installed capacity.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - With 2,824 MWe of installed capacity, Eren Enerji is one of Türkiye's important private electricity producers.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - On the list with 2,713 MWe of installed capacity, Çelikler Holding Enerji Grubu stands out with 12 plants and 2,769 MW of installed capacity.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji / Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Having seen a 179 megawatt increase in its total installed capacity compared to 2023, Aydem Enerji is one of Türkiye's pioneering energy companies. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji has reached 1,216 MW of installed capacity with hydroelectric, wind, geothermal and hybrid plants. It has also put into operation the Uşak Hybrid SPP, Türkiye's largest hybrid solar power plant (SPP) with a capacity of 82.15 MW.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - Standing out with 1,665 MWe of installed capacity, İÇDAŞ is among Türkiye's large private electricity producers.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - With 1,580 MWe of installed capacity, Bilgin Enerji is one of the important private players in the sector. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 12 plants and 1,733 MW of installed capacity.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - Having achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024, Kalyon Enerji has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio thanks to its solar power plant (SPP) investment in Şanlıurfa and other wind power plant (WPP) projects. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 6 plants and 1,399 MW of installed capacity.\n11. **Zorlu Enerji** - Standing out as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji generates power from solar, wind and geothermal sources and is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy producer. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 14 plants and 612 MW of installed capacity.\n12. **Aksa Enerji** - With 2 plants and 1,170 MW of installed capacity according to Enerji Atlası, Aksa Enerji is also one of Türkiye's important private electricity producers.", "20acdefc-5668-475d-a515-1c04240bff9f": "Large players such as `Enerjisa Üretim, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE) and Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)` stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye.Prominent Companies\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its large renewable portfolio, it is among the sector leaders in electricity generation.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It is one of the large producers focused entirely on renewable sources (HPP, WPP, SPP).\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** It stands out with its geothermal, wind and solar energy investments.\n- **Aydem Enerji:** Most of its portfolio consists of renewable energy sources.\n- **Galata Wind:** It is one of the publicly traded companies that generate only renewable (wind and solar) energy.\n- **Solar and Equipment Manufacturers:** Firms such as Margün Enerji , Smart Güneş Enerjisi (SMRTG) and Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS) stand out in solar energy and equipment.[](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri) [[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[3]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[4]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[5]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)[[6]](https://www.gcmyatirim.com.tr/egitim/makaleler/gelecegin-enerji-sektoru-ve-hisseleri-genel-gorunum-ve-yatirim-araclari)\n\nWould you like to focus on a specific branch of renewable energy (**solar**, **wind** or **geothermal** ), or would you like to look at the companies' **stock market status**?", "239500bd-76c1-4303-81e9-c157a2c90f11": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)**\n   It is one of the companies with the largest renewable energy investments in Türkiye. It has a broad portfolio in solar, wind and geothermal. It is one of Türkiye's largest players, particularly in geothermal energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)**\n   Operating in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions, Enerjisa Enerji contributes to renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants. By investing in sustainable energy projects, it aims to reduce its carbon footprint. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)**\n   Focusing on renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants, Aksa Enerji is strengthening its position in the sector by offering innovative solutions in energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)**\n   Contributing to Türkiye's energy needs with its solar, wind and hydroelectric power plants, Akfen prioritises sustainability and environmentally friendly projects in energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Borusan EnBW Enerji (BRMEN)**\n   An important player in Türkiye's renewable energy sector, Borusan EnBW Enerji stands out especially for its wind energy projects. The company owns some of Türkiye's largest wind farms and is continuously increasing its renewable energy investments. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji (AYDEM)**\n   With its solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants, it generates electricity in Türkiye exclusively from renewable energy sources. The plants of the company, which has more than 1,000 MW of installed capacity, are located in strategic regions across the country. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Say Yenilenebilir Enerji Ekipmanları A.Ş. (SAYAS)**\n   Designing and manufacturing equipment such as wind turbine tower internal/external components and blade, generator and rotor transport fixtures, SAYAS is one of the first firms in Türkiye to offer integrated solutions in equipment supply for renewable energy plants. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)**\n   Founded in Istanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, the company has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)**\n   Founded in 2011, Alfa Solar Enerji manufactures high-efficiency solar panels with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW at its facility in the Kırıkkale Organised Industrial Zone, with 40,000 m² of indoor space. Combining more than 40 years of manufacturing experience with advanced technology and robotic systems, it serves Türkiye's leading solar energy producers. ([a1capital.com.tr](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Galata Wind (GWIND)**\n    Operating in wind energy, Galata Wind operates wind farms in various regions of Türkiye. The company maintains its presence in the sector by increasing its renewable energy generation capacity. ([gedik.com](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to environmentally friendly energy generation by making significant investments in Türkiye's renewable energy sector.", "25862f0d-a02d-4198-a1c2-48db3741b1eb": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric producer. Its notable facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, and the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP in Elazığ, with 582.1 MW. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Energo-Pro Türkiye**\n   It operates in Türkiye with eight hydroelectric plants totalling 475 MW of installed capacity. These plants include Reşadiye 1-2-3 HPP, Aralık HPP, Hamzalı HPP, Meydancık EKO HPP, Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP, and Karakurt Dam and HPP. ([energo-pro.com.tr](https://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Merge Enerji**\n   It has been contributing to clean energy generation for 21 years with hydroelectric, wind and solar energy projects. It operates the Duru-1 hydroelectric plant in Amasya with 5.29 MW of installed capacity and the Duru-2 plant with 5.40 MW. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   It operates across Türkiye with 15 active power plants with 526.2 MWe of installed capacity. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://www.turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n   It generates 100% renewable energy with eight hydroelectric plants, one wind farm and six solar power plants with 205 MW of installed capacity. ([tektug.com](https://www.tektug.com/yesil-projeler/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **IC İçtaş Enerji**\n   It continues to generate renewable energy with nine hydroelectric plants totalling 388 MWe of installed capacity. ([icholding.com.tr](https://www.icholding.com.tr/TR/enerji/page/hidroelektrik-santralleri-28?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and contribute to increasing the use of renewable energy sources.", "26be0cae-2316-4382-ba06-3eabbb6f0d95": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   A leader in Türkiye's private sector electricity generation, Enerjisa Üretim has more than 4,600 MW of installed capacity in total, approximately 1,500 MW of which comes from wind energy. The company aims to raise its total installed capacity to 5,000 MW by 2026 and to source 60% of it from renewable energy sources. ([sirkulerekonomi.com](https://sirkulerekonomi.com/haberler/t%C3%BCrkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-yat%C4%B1r%C4%B1mlar%C4%B1-2025-raporu-2/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Zorlu Enerji**\n   Zorlu Enerji has a total installed capacity of approximately 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW is in Türkiye and 348.4 MW is abroad. The company's electricity generation in Türkiye comes entirely from renewable sources. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   Holding one of Türkiye's largest wind energy portfolios, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji is actively involved in YEKA projects and has goals of expanding abroad. ([sirkulerekonomi.com](https://sirkulerekonomi.com/haberler/t%C3%BCrkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-yat%C4%B1r%C4%B1mlar%C4%B1-2025-raporu-2/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Bereket Enerji**\n   A leader in wind energy, Bereket Enerji is one of the winning companies in the YEKA-1 tender. ([sirkulerekonomi.com](https://sirkulerekonomi.com/haberler/t%C3%BCrkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-yat%C4%B1r%C4%B1mlar%C4%B1-2025-raporu-2/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Shell & Turcas**\n   With the \"Derince Solar Project\" it implemented at the Derince Lubricant and Grease Production Facility, it received the \"2025 Low Carbon Hero\" award at the Istanbul Carbon Summit. This project contributes to reducing carbon emissions by meeting 25% of the facility's electricity needs from solar energy. ([petroturk.com](https://www.petroturk.com/akaryakit-haberleri/shell-turcas-derince-solar-projesi-ile-dusuk-karbon-kahramani-oldu?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **TEMSAN**\n   Developed by engineers at Türkiye Elektromekanik AŞ (TEMSAN), which is affiliated with the Ministry of Energy and Natural Resources, HİDROTEM is a compact mini hydroelectric plant with up to 1 MW of installed capacity, and thanks to its portable and compact structure it can be transported in a short time. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/temsan-muhendisleri-kompakt-mini-hes-gelistirdi/3181309?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to the country's energy transition by making significant investments in Türkiye's renewable energy sector.", "28ac917e-c9a6-4234-a930-b6c264664cb5": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **RT Enerji**\n   It operates in the development, installation and operation of power plant projects based on 100% renewable energy sources. The company's current capacity is 377.4 MWe, and its 2027 target is 1,351.1 MWe. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   It operates 7 wind farms with 451.1 MW of installed capacity. Its notable projects include Sarıtepe WPP (57 MWm/50 MWe) and Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe). ([akfenren.com.tr](https://www.akfenren.com.tr/varliklarimiz/res/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Polat Enerji**\n   It operates large-scale wind farms such as Soma WPP (328.9 MWm) and Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe). Soma WPP is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Demirer Holding**\n   It operates the Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in the Şarköy district of Tekirdağ province. With 30.5 MW of installed capacity, this plant generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eksim Enerji**\n   It operates 17 wind farms with 1,257.1 MW of installed capacity. It has projects such as Silivri WPP (108.8 MW) and Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe). ([eksimenerji.com.tr](https://eksimenerji.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-enerjisi-santralleri?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Medyol Enerji**\n   It operates wind farms such as Çerkeş WPP (50 MW), Kırklareli Yeni WPP (30 MW) and Çandarlı WPP (26 MW). ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://www.medyolenerji.com.tr/projelerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Çalık Enerji**\n   It operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant (40 MW) in the Urla district of İzmir province. This plant generates approximately 155 GWh of electricity per year. ([demirciliruzgar.com](https://www.demirciliruzgar.com/index.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Boydak Enerji**\n   It operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant (47.5 MW) in the Silivri district of Istanbul province. This plant generates approximately 151 GWh of electricity per year. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese firms operate wind farms in different regions of Türkiye and make significant contributions to renewable energy generation.", "28dcfd9c-375b-459a-b150-c1a28b3b3d66": "There are many important firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye. These firms play a critical role in helping Türkiye reach its renewable energy targets. Here are the main firms:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of Türkiye's largest wind energy investors. With 1,035.5 MW of installed wind capacity as of January 2026, it is one of the first players in the private sector to exceed this threshold. It operates a total of 18 wind farms in Akhisar, Akköy, Armutçuk, Arturna, Aydos, Balıkesir, Çanakkale, Çeşme, Dağpazarı, Dampınar, Dikili, Erciyes, Hacıhıdırlar, Harmancık, Ihlamur, Kestanederesi, Ovacık and Uygar.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - It is one of the important wind energy investors in Türkiye and has 773 MW of installed capacity. It owns large plants such as Saros WPP.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It stands out with high-capacity WPP projects and long-term energy investments. It has 772 MW of installed capacity. It operates plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP, Göktepe WPP, Poyraz WPP and Ege WPP.\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - It is among Türkiye's largest wind energy investors. It has a total installed capacity of 733 MW. With 428 MW of active installed capacity, it generates 1.2 million MWh of electricity per year and has 8 wind farm investments.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It is an important player in the wind energy sector with 702 MW of installed capacity. It has projects such as the Kocatepe Wind Power Plant (100 MW), Fatma WPP (80 MW), Zeliha WPP (25 MW) and Kanije WPP (64 MW).\n6.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind investments. It has the Uşak WPP, Armutlu WPP and Söke WPP investments. In March 2026, with the Uşak WPP capacity increase, its wind energy capacity rose to approximately 268.5 MW.\n7.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that give wind investments a significant place in their renewable energy portfolio. It owns important WPPs such as the Şah Wind Power Plant.\n8.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is a company traded on Borsa İstanbul with wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n9.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of the important wind power plant operators in Türkiye. It owns large plants such as Osmaniye Gökçedağ WPP (135 MW).\n10. **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - It is a firm traded on Borsa İstanbul that stands out for its wind energy investments. It has plants such as Tatlıpınar WPP (127 MW) in Balıkesir.\n11. **RT Enerji** - It is among the leading investors in the Turkish energy market and develops, builds and operates power plant projects based on 100% renewable energy sources. It has a total of 377.4 MWe of installed capacity in operation.\n12. **Türkerler Holding** - It owns wind farms such as Barbaros WPP, Gelibolu WPP, Kalfaköy WPP, Meryem WPP, Şapdağı WPP, Tire WPP, Yenihisar WPP and Zonguldak WPP. A significant portion of its total installed capacity of 527 MWe comes from wind energy.", "295c8cb6-e645-4b0a-94b8-359270f82331": "The leading private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye are listed below. These companies make significant contributions to Türkiye's security of energy supply.\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is the largest private sector producer in this field in Türkiye. The company's important HPP projects include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector; the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP with 582.1 MW of installed capacity; and the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant with 500 MW of installed capacity, Türkiye's first hybrid power plant.\n2.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW. The company stands out for its investments in renewable energy sources.\n3.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It owns the Bereket 1 and 2 Hydroelectric Plants, the first private sector plants built outside the state in Türkiye. The company also has important hydroelectric plants such as the Aksu HPP with 46.2 MW of installed capacity, the Gökyar HPP with 63 MW and the Akıncı HPP with 99 MW.\n4.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is a large renewable energy company operating seven hydroelectric plants. It plays an important role in helping Türkiye reach its renewable energy targets.\n5.  **ENKA** - With 3,978 megawatts of installed capacity, it is one of the largest electricity generation companies in the private sector, and its portfolio also includes hydroelectric plants.\n6.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim is one of Türkiye's leading electricity producers with 3,901 megawatts of installed capacity and also operates hydroelectric plants.\n7.  **Limak Enerji** - Rising to fifth place with 3,033 megawatts of installed capacity, Limak Enerji also has a share in hydroelectric power generation.\n8.  **Çalık Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's largest private sector energy companies and generates electricity using various energy sources such as hydroelectric, wind and solar power plants.\n9.  **Kolin Enerji** - It operates hydroelectric plants such as the Doğankent HPP (75 MW).\n10. **Alarko Enerji** - It has hydroelectric plants such as the Karakuz Dam and HPP (76 MW).", "2995aafb-b0cf-4dd3-8247-f66e7c551ac7": "Some of the private sector companies that stand out in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric producer. Its notable facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, and the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP in Elazığ, with 582.1 MW of installed capacity. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Merge Enerji**\n   Developing hydroelectric, wind and solar energy projects since 2005, Merge Enerji has a total hydroelectric plant capacity of 1,300 MW. It has projects such as the Duru-1 and Duru-2 hydroelectric plants in Amasya. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   Operating 15 active power plants with 526.2 MW of installed capacity, Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji contributes to Türkiye's transition to a low-carbon economy with its hydroelectric investments. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n   Founded in 2000, Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş. contributes to environmentally friendly power generation with 8 hydroelectric plants, 1 wind farm and 6 solar power plants with a total capacity of 205 MW. ([tektug.com](https://www.tektug.com/enerji-uretimi-ve-satisi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Enova Enerji Şirketi**\n   Founded by Özaltın İnşaat and Nurol Yatırım Şirketleri, Enova Enerji Şirketi is the owner and operator of the Berkman Dam and HPP in Osmaniye, with 39 MW of installed capacity. ([ozaltin.com](https://www.ozaltin.com/tr/tum-projeler/baraj-ve-hes-projeleri/berkman-dam-and-hepp/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies are private sector players holding a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation.", "2ed8e622-b76c-4bb0-9469-263e78b6ea6b": "The leading private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye stand out for the installed capacity of their hydroelectric plants (HPP) and their energy generation portfolios. Here are some of these companies:\n\n1.  **Aydem Enerji** - Known as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji focuses on renewable energy. The company's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, with a total installed capacity of 852.1 MWm. 71.1% of its total installed capacity consists of HPPs.\n2.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - One of the companies with a 100% renewable energy portfolio, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji has 12 HPPs operating in different regions of Türkiye in its hydroelectric portfolio. The total installed capacity of these plants is 228.7 MW, and their annual generation capacity is stated as approximately 895 GWh.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Focusing on the use of domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation, Enerjisa Üretim currently has 12 hydroelectric plants. The company states that it will continue its investments in this field in the coming years. According to the MW100 survey, Enerjisa Üretim, a partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, is one of the leading companies in the private sector with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity.\n4.  **ENERGO-PRO** - Entering the Turkish market in 2010, ENERGO-PRO generates 1.7 TWh of energy in Türkiye with 8 hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW. The company's Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP has 280 MW of installed capacity and an annual generation of 850 GWh.\n5.  **Akenerji** - Starting its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji has a total of 388 MWe of installed capacity with hydroelectric and wind plants. The company is stated to have the capacity to meet 3% of Türkiye's energy needs on its own.\n6.  **Zorlu Enerji** - Zorlu Enerji Elektrik Üretim Anonim Şirketi, the only publicly traded company of the Zorlu Enerji Group, continues its operations with seven hydroelectric and three wind power plants.\n7.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and has Geothermal Power Plants, Hydroelectric Power Plants and Wind Power Plants. Mogan Enerji's HPP capacity of 81.37 MW is a direct part of its portfolio.\n8.  **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul with hydroelectric plants in their portfolio. ENTRA's operating HPP portfolio has an installed capacity of approximately 388 MW.\n9.  **Enda Enerji Holding (ENDAE)** - Among the companies with hydroelectric plants in their portfolio, ENDAE has 104.08 MWe of hydroelectric installed capacity consisting of 4 HPPs.\n10. **Bilgin Enerji** - Among Türkiye's largest electricity producers according to the MW100 survey, Bilgin Enerji's total installed capacity is stated as 1,580 MW. The company's portfolio also includes hydroelectric plants.", "2edec8f0-1f6b-4e5a-b6ae-f3bfbf23126d": "The main large firms and energy producers operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye are as follows:[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\n- [Enerjisa Üretim](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-santrallerimiz/) : With numerous WPP projects across the country, it is one of the largest renewable energy producers.\n- [Galata Wind](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) : It is one of the leading listed energy companies focused directly on renewable sources such as wind and solar.\n- Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji : It has wind farm investments and operations in different regions.\n- Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji : Its portfolio includes a significant share of wind and hydroelectric plants.\n- Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji : It generates electricity with wind farms in various provinces.\n- [GÜRİŞ](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html) : It owns large-scale wind projects such as Kocatepe WPP.\n- Tatlıpınar Enerji : It is among the companies that stand out for their wind power plant investments.[[1]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-santrallerimiz/)[[2]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[3]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[4]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)[[5]](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html)[[6]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)\n\nIf you are curious about a specific **region** (for example the Aegean or Marmara) or a **company's installed capacity**, I can provide detailed information.", "31aa96c7-607a-4ee0-be7d-26986b2bdb96": "There are many private companies generating hydroelectric power in Türkiye. These companies play an important role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are some of the leading private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's largest private sector producers of hydroelectric energy. It generates clean energy with six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity. Its notable HPPs include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP, the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector with 626.85 MW of installed capacity; the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP, the second largest with 582.1 MW of installed capacity; and the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant with 500 MW of installed capacity.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Sabancı Holding and Germany's E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim is one of Türkiye's important electricity producers. It currently has 12 hydroelectric plants and focuses on the use of domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation. According to the MW100 survey, it has 3,901 MWe of installed capacity as of 2024, with a significant hydroelectric share within this capacity.\n3.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is known as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji includes important plants such as the Göktaş Dam and HPP with 276 MW of installed capacity. It also includes many HPPs such as the Adıgüzel HPP (62 MW), Kemer HPP (48 MW) and Akköprü HPP (115 MW).\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a total capacity of 228.7 MW. The company stands out for its investments in renewable energy.\n5.  **Akenerji** - Starting its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji has a total of 388 MWe of installed capacity with hydroelectric and wind plants. The company states that it has the capacity to meet a significant portion of Türkiye's energy needs.\n6.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It continues its operations with seven hydroelectric and three wind power plants. Supporting Türkiye in reaching its renewable energy targets, the company continues its work with new projects nationally and internationally.\n7.  **Limak Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's leading energy companies and also holds an important place in hydroelectric power generation. The company operates large hydroelectric plants such as the Çetin Dam and HPP (420 MW) and the Alkumru Dam and HPP (276 MW). According to the MW100 survey, it is among the top five electricity producers with 3,033 MWe of installed capacity as of 2024.\n8.  **Sanko Enerji** - It owns important hydroelectric plants such as the Yedigöze Sanibey Dam (311 MW). By investing in renewable energy sources, the company contributes to Türkiye's security of energy supply.\n9.  **Doğuş Enerji** - It operates large hydroelectric plants such as the Artvin Dam and HPP (332 MW).\n10. **Kolin Enerji** - It owns hydroelectric plants such as the Akköy 2 Dam and HPP (230 MW).", "325ae353-ab89-451e-9af3-9253ff9916e0": "The main energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and delivering important projects are as follows:\n\n1. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two giant solar power plants with a total capacity of 5,000 MW in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **OYAK Çimento** - It has commissioned Türkiye's largest solar power plant for self-consumption in Beypazarı, Ankara, with 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp of installed capacity. ([enerjiekonomisi.com](https://www.enerjiekonomisi.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oztuketim-gunes-santralini-devreye-aldi/41773?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - With its solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants, it has more than 1,000 MW of installed capacity. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Operating in the installation and operation of solar power plants, this company carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Margün Enerji** - Working in solar power generation and project development, this company has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Zorlu Enerji** - As one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, it has a total installed capacity of approximately 991 MW, a significant portion of which consists of solar power plants. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Enerjisa Enerji** - One of Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions companies, Enerjisa Enerji also invests in renewable energy projects. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies have made significant contributions to the development of the solar energy sector in Türkiye and continue their presence in the sector with various projects.", "345e53e2-8b13-494a-8a85-518fcca04b61": "There are many large energy companies installing solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye. These companies play an important role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are some prominent large energy companies and their activities in solar energy:\n\n1.  **Kalyon Enerji (Kalyon PV)** - Known as Türkiye's largest solar energy company, Kalyon Enerji operates Türkiye's largest solar power plant, in Karapınar, Konya in particular, with 1,350 MW of installed capacity. Kalyon PV also has an integrated structure, producing ingots, wafers, cells and panels. It established Türkiye's first domestic solar panel factory in Ankara.\n2.  **CW Enerji** - Founded in 2010, CW Enerji is a manufacturing and services firm operating in the photovoltaic energy generation sector. It has an annual solar panel production capacity of 1.8 GW. It offers a wide range of services such as turnkey SPP installation, engineering, maintenance and sales of solar equipment. It has important SPP projects in many provinces such as Kayseri, İzmir, Elazığ, Batman and Balıkesir.\n3.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in Istanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri offers solar panel manufacturing and solar energy solutions with an R&D-focused approach. It has two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, with a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells. The company serves customers in more than 20 countries worldwide.\n4.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji obtains a significant portion of its total installed capacity from renewable sources. The company also maintains its presence in this field with solar power plants.\n5.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is a leader in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. The company also invests in solar systems as part of its customer solutions. Enerjisa Üretim currently has two solar power plants.\n6.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - The Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji Group has solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed) in its portfolio. The company operates with modern power plants in many regions of Türkiye.\n7.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş. (MAGEN)** - Operating since 2014, Margün Enerji offers project development, turnkey installation (EPC) and Operation and Maintenance services in renewable energy and climate technologies. It stands out in the sector with solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp. It has also completed SPP installations with a capacity of 61 MWp abroad.\n8.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Operating in photovoltaic panel manufacturing and SPP investments, Alfa Solar Enerji is one of Türkiye's leading solar panel manufacturers.\n9.  **Aydem Enerji** - The founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji also keeps renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects. In addition to a hybrid plant, the company's portfolio also includes solar power plants.\n10. **Liva Enerji** - Offering fast, flexible and high-quality service across Türkiye with offices in Istanbul, Gaziantep, Ankara and Bursa, Liva Enerji has important reference projects in turnkey Solar Power Plant (SPP) installation, in both rooftop and ground-mounted applications.\n11. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji (NATEN)** - Standing out on the SPP development and electricity generation side, Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji operates in solar plant investment and project development.", "371e322a-a408-4824-98c5-6c04c295643e": "Among the main firms operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye, [Galata Wind](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri), Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji, Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji and [Polat Enerji](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz) stand out.[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[2]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)\n\n### Main WPP Operators\n\n- **Galata Wind:** It generates purely renewable electricity with wind and solar plants across Türkiye.\n- **Polat Enerji:** It manages large projects such as Soma WPP, one of Türkiye's largest wind portfolios.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is one of the important producers whose portfolio is weighted towards wind farms.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Among its renewable energy facilities across the country, it is also active with wind farms.\n- **Eksim Enerji:** With licensed wind energy projects and high installed capacity, it holds a strong position in the sector.\n- **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It operates many wind farms such as Ziyaret, Salman and Düzova.\n- **Tatlıpınar Enerji:** It is one of the companies on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind investments.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** In addition to its broad energy portfolio, it also has wind energy investments.[[1]](https://www.instagram.com/p/DF5SheotIz0/)[[2]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)[[3]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)[[4]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[5]](https://eksimenerji.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-enerjisi-santralleri)[[6]](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html)\n\nWould you like more information about the **regional distribution** or **installed capacities** of these operating plants?", "3938e1de-bc14-481d-a326-6fe9914fa903": "Among the large energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, Kalyon Enerji, [Zorlu Enerji](https://www.zorluenerji.com.tr/), [Enerjisa Enerji](https://www.enerjisa.com.tr/), Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and [Alarko Holding](https://www.alarko.com.tr/) stand out.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://ceyrekmuhendis.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-santralleri/)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)Leading Energy Companies\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** With the huge YEKA SPP project it built in Karapınar, Konya, it brought one of the largest solar plants in Türkiye and Europe to life.[](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/) [[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOoouJDuf0PV5vQDaPA_h51eHMimfIVPRnL40gg8ar3eJn1F969FT)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/)[[3]](https://ceyrekmuhendis.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-santralleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** By adding renewable energy investments to its portfolio, it has built solar plant projects in different regions and developed licensed/unlicensed SPP projects.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji:** Through the partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, it makes rooftop SPP projects in particular and large-scale renewable energy investments.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** In addition to wind and hydroelectric projects, it holds a significant share of solar energy capacity in its portfolio in various provinces of Türkiye.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[3]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Alarko Holding (Altek Alarko):** In line with its growth strategy in the energy sector, it continues its solar power plant investments and project design.[[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n\nIs there **a specific region**, **a company's financial information** or **installed capacity details** you would like?", "3bd41bf0-5617-4e53-b4c0-90c701ce7a4e": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers are ranked by installed capacity as follows:\n\n1. **ENKA** - With 3,978 MWe of installed capacity, it is Türkiye's largest private electricity producer. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim** - It ranks second with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji** - It ranks third with 3,147 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji** - It ranks fourth with 2,576 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji** - It ranks fifth with 2,818 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant portion of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity.", "3fad5c6d-252f-4dcc-9682-4b21669f408a": "There are many large energy companies building solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye. These companies operate both in solar panel manufacturing and in developing and implementing turnkey SPP projects. Here are some of the prominent ones:\n\n1.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in Istanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa, the company has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells. The company aims to reach 2,000 MW of cell production by the end of 2025. It also exports energy and solar panels.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji obtains most of its total installed capacity from renewable sources. The company has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in Türkiye, and 1 wind, 1 solar and 2 natural gas plants abroad. It generates power from solar, wind and geothermal sources.\n3.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is one of the leading companies in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. Enerjisa Üretim currently has two solar power plants.\n4.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity by making approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments under its 2030 strategy. The company is Türkiye's largest publicly traded independent power producer.\n5.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - The Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji Group's portfolio includes solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed).\n6.  **CW Enerji Mühendislik Ticaret ve Sanayi Anonim Şirketi** - Actively operating in the photovoltaic energy generation sector since 2010, it is one of Türkiye's leading solar panel manufacturing companies.\n7.  **GES Enerji San. ve Tic. Ltd. Şti.** - It is the firm named GES (Gelecek Enerji Sistemleri) that was the first to start operating in renewable energy in Türkiye in 2005. It carries out work on many SPP projects, the installation and commissioning of biodiesel and biogas facilities, and related consulting, in our country and abroad.\n8.  **Entegre Solar** - Founded in 2013 by combining the strengths of Germany's established solar energy company Entegro GMBH and Türkiye's experienced engineering firm Akademi Mühendislik, Entegro Enerji Sistemleri offers world-class solar energy solutions to our country. It offers solutions for ground-mounted, industrial-commercial rooftop and solar carport projects. It has completed successful SPP projects all over Türkiye.\n9.  **Göktekin Enerji** - It carries out clean, renewable energy projects and investments in every corner of Türkiye. It has both ground-mounted SPP and rooftop SPP projects.\n10. **TURECO Enerji** - Installing ground-mounted and rooftop turnkey solar energy systems in Türkiye since 2014, it is one of the strong organisations in the photovoltaic energy sector.", "41e3bf3e-ab57-4b75-a9b3-7d6b03f749f9": "The largest and leading investor firm operating **wind power plants (WPP)** in Türkiye is **Enerjisa Üretim** . According to data from the Turkish Wind Energy Association ([TÜREB](https://tureb.tr/) ), the country's total installed wind capacity has exceeded **16,200 MW**.[[1]](https://yatirimlar.com/haber/tureb-temmuz-2026-turkiye-ruzgar-enerjisi-istatistik-raporunu-yayimladi_254968)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)The main wind energy investors and operators that stand out in the sector in terms of installed capacity (MW) are as follows:\n\n### Main Wind Energy Operators\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With approximately **1,119 MW** of installed capacity in operation, it is the **undisputed leader** of Türkiye's wind energy market . Its portfolio includes some of the country's largest plants, such as Balıkesir WPP and Çanakkale WPP.[[1]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)[[2]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-santrallerimiz/)\n- **Borusan EnBW Enerji:** With approximately **776 MW** of installed capacity, it is the second largest player in the sector. It has extensive investments particularly in the Bursa, Balıkesir and Çanakkale regions.[[1]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)\n- **Eksim Enerji:** It ranks third with approximately **774 MW** of wind capacity. **Soma WPP** (288 MW) in Manisa, one of Türkiye's largest wind farms, is also among this group's notable investments (in partnership with İş Enerji).[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)\n- **Polat Enerji:** It operates in fourth place in the sector with installed capacity of **771 MW**.[[1]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)\n- **GÜRİŞ Holding:** Completing the top 5 with approximately **702 MW** of capacity, it is one of the established investors focused on renewable energy.[[1]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)\n\n### Other Important Investors in the Sector\nIn addition to these leading firms, large groups such as **Akfen Enerji**, **Zorlu Enerji**, **Ayen Enerji**, **Limak Enerji** and **Türkerler Holding** also operate wind farms on a significant scale in different regions of Türkiye.[[1]](https://t24.com.tr/gundem/ruzgar-pazarinin-yuzde-90ini-elinde-bulunduran-8-sirket-turkiyede-yarisacak,416653)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/olds/upload/Turkiye_Ruzgar_Enerjisi_istatistik_raporu_ocak_2014.pdf)\n\n---\n\n### Direct Comparison Table\n| Operator Firm | Approximate Installed Wind Capacity | Notable Plant Locations |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Enerjisa Üretim** | ~1,119 MW | Balıkesir, Çanakkale, İzmir, Kayseri |\n| **Borusan EnBW Enerji** | ~776 MW | Balıkesir, Bursa, Çanakkale |\n| **Eksim Enerji** | ~774 MW | Manisa (Soma), Tokat, Amasya |\n| **Polat Enerji** | ~771 MW | İzmir, Manisa, Kırşehir |\n| **GÜRİŞ** | ~702 MW | Aydın, Dinar, Muğla, Hatay |\n\n*(Note: The installed capacity data above reflects existing capacity in operation; projects under construction and in the licensing process are not included.)* [[1]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)[[2]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)If you are interested, I can also share details on the following topics:\n\n- Which **turbine manufacturers** (Nordex, Vestas, Enercon, etc.) do these firms prefer most for their plants?\n- Which are the **geographic regions and cities** with the most intensive wind investments in Türkiye?[[1]](https://cdn.tureb.tr/storage/20260206/019c330f-13ea-71f1-829c-691608beb434.pdf)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/turkiyenin-insa-asamasindaki-ruzgar-gucu-45-gwa-ulasti/)[[3]](https://t24.com.tr/gundem/ruzgar-pazarinin-yuzde-90ini-elinde-bulunduran-8-sirket-turkiyede-yarisacak,416653)", "45cc7c3a-7103-45b9-b3de-780bc1ef97f0": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Polat Enerji A.Ş.** - It operates the Soma Wind Power Plant, one of Türkiye's largest wind farms. With 328.9 MWm of installed capacity, Soma WPP is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **RT Enerji** - It owns many wind farms. Its notable projects include Adapazarı WPP (92.8 MWm), Bozüyük WPP (98 MWm), Çandır WPP (11.4 MWm) and Kandıra WPP (58 MWm). ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Çalık Enerji** - It is known for projects such as Demircili WPP and Sarpıncık WPP. Demircili WPP in Urla, İzmir has 40 MW of installed capacity, while Sarpıncık WPP in Karaburun, İzmir has 32 MW of installed capacity. ([momentumenerji.com.tr](https://momentumenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **EOLOS Rüzgar Enerjisi Üretim A.Ş.** - It operates the Şenköy WPP within the provincial borders of Hatay. With a total capacity of 36 MW, this plant aims to generate approximately 110 million kWh of electricity per year. ([santralmadencilik.com](https://www.santralmadencilik.com/eolos-ruzgar.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Demirer Holding** - It operates the Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in Şarköy, Tekirdağ. With 30.5 MW of installed capacity, this plant generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Livera Enerji** - It plans to build the Germiyan Wind Power Plant in Çeşme, İzmir. With a total capacity of 10 MWm, this plant will consist of 4 wind turbines of 2.5 MWm each. ([liveraenergy.com](https://liveraenergy.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Medyol Enerji** - It has projects such as İzmir Ala WPP, Bayburt Kalyon YEKA WPP and Trabzon Kalyon YEKA WPP. ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://www.medyolenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Arsen Elektrik** - It has undertaken the construction of wind farms such as Emres WPP (2 MW), Adares WPP EXT. (14.4 MW), Taşpınar WPP (60 MW) and Ovacık WPP (26 MW). ([arsenelektrik.com.tr](https://www.arsenelektrik.com.tr/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri-proje?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Boydak Enerji** - It operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant in Silivri, Istanbul. With 47.5 MW of installed capacity, this plant generates approximately 151 GWh of electricity per year. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Güral Porselen** - It plans to build the Germiyan Wind Power Plant in Çeşme, İzmir. With a total capacity of 10 MWm, this plant will consist of 4 wind turbines of 2.5 MWm each. ([liveraenergy.com](https://liveraenergy.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese firms operate wind farms in different regions of Türkiye and make significant contributions to renewable energy generation.", "48c26071-228e-4e0a-8f9f-389a68776336": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers are ranked by the installed capacity they held as of 31 December 2024 as follows:\n\n1. **ENKA**: The leader in the private sector with 3,978 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim**: It ranks second with 3,901 MWe of installed capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji**: It ranks third with 3,147 MWe of installed capacity. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji**: It ranks fourth with 3,033 MWe of installed capacity. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji**: It ranks fifth with 2,818 MWe of installed capacity. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant portion of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity and are among the largest private producers in the sector.", "4d77fcbe-a5b8-4dab-86b3-af81f6651362": "There are many important firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye. These firms play a critical role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are the main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of the largest wind energy investors in Türkiye. As of January 2026, it has 1,035 MW of installed capacity. The company operates a total of 19 wind farms in different locations such as Akhisar, Balıkesir and Çanakkale, and continues to invest in domestic and renewable sources.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's leading wind generation companies. It stands out with 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy. With 772 MW of installed capacity as of January 2026, it operates Türkiye's first licensed wind power plant with storage (DRES) whose acceptance has been completed (Soma WPP).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - It is among Türkiye's large wind energy investors and has 733 MW of installed capacity as of January 2026.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It is an important player in the wind energy sector and has 702 MW of installed wind capacity as of January 2026.\n6.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It has a broad renewable energy portfolio and stands out with its wind farms and capacity expansion investments. It is also known as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant.\n7.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is one of the companies on Borsa İstanbul directly linked to wind energy. It operates plants such as Şah WPP, Mersin WPP and Taşpınar WPP.\n8.  **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - At the centre of its operations is the Tatlıpınar Wind Power Plant in Balıkesir, and it is one of the companies on Borsa İstanbul most directly linked to the wind energy theme.\n9.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates in the renewable energy sector with wind farms and significant WPP capacity expansion projects.\n10. **Zorlu Enerji** - It is an integrated energy company with wind investments within its broad energy portfolio. It stands out with its existing and planned/storage-backed wind investments. It owns large plants such as Osmaniye Gökçedağ WPP.\n\nThese firms continue to develop wind energy capacity to meet Türkiye's growing energy needs and build a sustainable future.", "4d8dd457-4fd3-4fe0-ac61-071c44da8cc6": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies invest in various renewable sources such as solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal in order to meet the country's growing energy needs and reduce external dependence.\n\nSome of the prominent companies operating in Türkiye's renewable energy sector are as follows:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is recognised as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW comes from domestic plants. Obtaining all of its electricity generation in Türkiye from renewable sources, Zorlu Enerji has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind and 4 geothermal plants in the country. It is one of Türkiye's largest companies, particularly in geothermal energy generation, and meets 20% of the country's geothermal energy needs.\n\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions company. In addition to electricity infrastructure investments, the company also has customer solutions business lines such as solar systems, e-mobility (Eşarj) and energy efficiency. Within Enerjisa Üretim, there are 12 hydroelectric plants, 5 wind farms and 2 solar power plants.\n\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji is Türkiye's largest publicly traded independent power producer. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity with approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments. It has completed the licensing processes for wind farms with storage in locations such as Mersin and Balıkesir, and in addition to Türkiye, it has investments in Africa and Central Asia.\n\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - Founded by Akfen Holding in 2007, the company has a 100% renewable energy portfolio. Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW. Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji's HPP facilities are located in different basins such as the Sakarya, Kızılırmak and Çoruh rivers.\n\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is known as the founder of our country's first private hydroelectric plant. Aydem Enerji operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind farms, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant. 71.1% of the company's total installed capacity of 1,198 MWm consists of HPPs.\n\n6.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is a company traded on Borsa İstanbul that stands out for its wind energy investments. With a total installed capacity of 297 MW, Galata Wind is increasing sustainable energy through its projects. The company's investments include Mersin WPP, Şah WPP, Çorum SPP, Erzurum SPP and Taşpınar WPP.\n\n7.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in Istanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, the company has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n\n8.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - It is one of the leading domestic firms manufacturing solar panels in Türkiye. The company is present in the sector with solar panel projects in various regions of Türkiye.\n\n9.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - Thanks to its solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp, it has become one of the notable players in the sector. As part of its work abroad, it has also completed the installation of a solar power plant with a capacity of 61 MWp on a turnkey basis and taken on the operation and maintenance of these facilities.\n\n10. **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - Operating in geothermal energy, GÜRMAT operates Türkiye's largest geothermal power plant, with 260 MW of installed capacity, by utilising the high-enthalpy geothermal resources in the Aydın-Germencik region. It generates electricity by using the domestic, renewable, low-cost and environmentally friendly advantages of geothermal energy.\n\nBy utilising Türkiye's renewable energy potential, these companies both contribute to the country's security of energy supply and play an important role in reaching its environmental sustainability targets.", "4e4c0926-1e2d-4c9d-82db-49785874ddaa": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers can be ranked by installed capacity as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - With 3,978 megawatts of installed capacity in the private sector, it is Türkiye's largest private electricity producer. It represents 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim follows ENKA with 3,901 megawatts of installed capacity. The company stands out for its balanced source mix.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with 3,161 megawatts of installed capacity, Cengiz Enerji has a balanced source mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It ranks fifth with 3,033 megawatts of installed capacity.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - According to 2019 data, it has 2,824 MWe of installed capacity.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - According to 2019 data, it has 2,713 MWe of installed capacity.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - Having seen significant increases in its total installed capacity, the company invests in renewable energy.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - According to 2019 data, it is in the top 10 and has 1,665 MWe of installed capacity.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - According to 2019 data, it stands out with 1,580 MWe of installed capacity.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - Particularly in 2024, it is one of the companies that achieved the largest capacity increase with its solar power plant (SPP) in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in different provinces.\n\nThese companies cover a significant portion of Türkiye's electricity generation capacity and also stand out for their investments in renewable energy sources.", "504a5499-8621-4980-83b2-a19f3d332f36": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers are ranked in terms of installed capacity and generation capacity as follows:\n\n1. **ENKA**\n   Installed capacity: 3,978 MWe. ENKA owns natural gas plants and represents approximately 4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/2852564?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   Installed capacity: 3,901 MWe. Enerjisa Üretim has a balanced portfolio of hydroelectric, natural gas and wind power plants. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/2852564?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   Installed capacity: 3,147 MWe. Cengiz Enerji owns natural gas and coal plants and has a significant share in Türkiye's energy generation. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/2852564?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji**\n   Installed capacity: 3,033 MWe. Limak Enerji stands out in renewable energy generation with its hydroelectric and wind power plants. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/2852564?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji**\n   Installed capacity: 2,818 MWe. Eren Enerji holds an important position in electricity generation with its natural gas and coal plants. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/2852564?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant portion of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity and play a strategic role in the energy sector.", "50f62979-5628-4b6d-a509-19ffa12533d5": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **RT Enerji**\n   Among the leading investors in the Turkish energy market, RT Enerji develops, installs and operates power plant projects based on 100% renewable energy sources. The company's existing plants include Adapazarı WPP, Bozüyük WPP, Çandır WPP and Kandıra WPP. For example, Adapazarı WPP, with 16 turbines and 92.8 MWm of installed capacity, has the capacity to generate 280 million kWh of electricity per year. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Polat Enerji**\n   Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji operates plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP, Göktepe WPP, Poyraz WPP, Ege WPP and Seyitali WPP. For example, Soma WPP, built in 2009 with 328.9 MWe of installed capacity, is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **EOLOS Rüzgar Enerjisi Üretim A.Ş.**\n   Founded in 2010, EOLOS operates with the Şenköy WPP, located within the provincial borders of Hatay. With a total installed capacity of 36 MW, the plant aims to generate approximately 110 million kWh of electricity per year. ([santralmadencilik.com](https://www.santralmadencilik.com/eolos-ruzgar.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Medyol Enerji**\n   Specialising in wind power plant infrastructure and high-voltage electrical works, Medyol Enerji has taken part in projects such as İzmir Ala WPP, Bayburt Kalyon YEKA WPP, Trabzon Kalyon YEKA WPP, Kırşehir Geycek WPP and Karaman WPP. For example, İzmir Ala WPP has a total installed capacity of 12 MW with 2 ENERCON model turbines. ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://www.medyolenerji.com.tr/projelerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Demirer Holding**\n   Operating in the wind energy sector since 1998, Demirer Holding operates the Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in the Şarköy district of Tekirdağ province. With 30.5 MW of installed capacity, the plant generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Arsen Elektrik Elektromekanik İnşaat Taahhüt San. ve Tic.**\n   Operating in renewable energy projects since 2007, Arsen Elektrik has undertaken the construction of wind farms such as Emres WPP, Adares WPP EXT., Taşpınar WPP, Ovacık WPP and Ayvalık-1 WPP. For example, Taşpınar WPP is a plant completed in 2020 with 60 MW of installed capacity. ([arsenelektrik.com.tr](https://www.arsenelektrik.com.tr/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri-proje?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Momentum Enerji**\n   An affiliate of Çalık Enerji, Momentum Enerji operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant, commissioned in 2016 in the Urla district of İzmir province. The plant generates 155 GWh of electricity per year. ([momentumenerji.com.tr](https://momentumenerji.com.tr/index.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese firms hold a significant share of Türkiye's wind energy sector and contribute to renewable energy generation.", "51353839-7f9d-46f3-80cc-f88e1f8a94c0": "The main energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1. **Kalyon Enerji** - It built Türkiye's largest solar power plant in the Karapınar district of Konya, with 1,350 MW of installed capacity. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/iste-turkiyenin-yesil-enerji-devleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **OYAK Çimento** - It has commissioned Türkiye's largest solar power plant for self-consumption in Beypazarı, Ankara, with 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp of installed capacity. ([enerjiekonomisi.com](https://www.enerjiekonomisi.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oztuketim-gunes-santralini-devreye-aldi/41773?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two large solar power plants with a total installed capacity of 5,000 MW in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Zorlu Enerji** - With a total installed capacity of approximately 991 MW, the company operates 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in Türkiye. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Enerjisa Enerji** - One of Türkiye's leading electricity distribution and retail sales companies, Enerjisa makes significant investments in renewable energy projects. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Operating solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants, the company has more than 1,000 MW of installed capacity and generates electricity exclusively from renewable energy sources. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Operating in the installation and operation of solar power plants, the company carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Margün Enerji** - Working in solar power generation and project development, the company has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **CW Enerji** - Installing on-grid solar power plants in Türkiye that use CW Enerji brand solar panels, the company is involved in various projects. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/cw-enerji-solar-panel/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Jinko Solar** - Installing on-grid solar power plants in Türkiye that use Jinko Solar brand solar panels, the company is involved in various projects. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/jinko-solar/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in Türkiye's solar energy sector.", "558b42b3-2f06-4712-b9db-8e2b89f346b4": "Renewable energy generation in Türkiye has become a rapidly growing strategic sector in line with growing energy needs, goals to reduce import dependence and global environmental policies. Many companies operating in this field stand out for both their generation capacity and their technology investments. Here are some of the companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji has a total installed capacity of approximately 991 MW. Of this, 642.8 MW belongs to domestic plants and 348.4 MW to plants abroad. All of the company's electricity generation in Türkiye comes from renewable sources, and it has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind and 4 geothermal plants. It is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy producer.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is one of Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions companies. It has distribution, retail and customer solutions business lines such as solar systems, e-mobility (Eşarj) and energy efficiency.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji aims to reach 5,297 MW of installed capacity by making approximately USD 4.9 billion of renewable energy investments under its 2030 strategy. In addition to Türkiye, it has renewable energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - Operating with diversified modern power plants in many regions of Türkiye over the last five years, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji has 699 MWe of installed capacity. Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - The founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji holds an important place in renewable energy. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji AŞ has 1,121 MW of installed capacity with 19 plants.\n6.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It is one of the companies that stand out in the renewable energy sector. Its portfolio includes 81.37 MW of hydroelectric plant (HPP) capacity. In total, it has 949 MW of installed capacity with 18 plants.\n7.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - It is one of the prominent domestic companies operating in solar energy technologies.\n8.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Among the solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye and an important player in the sector, Alfa Solar Enerji contributes to renewable energy generation.\n9.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is among the companies with a renewable energy portfolio traded on Borsa İstanbul.\n10. **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - It is among Türkiye's large renewable energy companies.\n11. **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - It was founded in 1999 by GÜRİŞ İnşaat ve Mühendislik A.Ş. to build and operate the Aydın Germencik geothermal power plant. It is one of the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy and owns many geothermal plants.\n12. **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji Holding A.Ş.** - It has investments in wind and solar power plants and hybrid power plants. It operates many wind farms.\n13. **GMK Enerji** - It works on geothermal energy investments such as exploration activities within geothermal licences, drilling new geothermal wells, greenhouse farming, district heating and power plants. It aims to combine the power of geothermal with innovation and technology.\n14. **Enda Enerji Holding A.Ş.** - It undertakes initiatives in sustainable, renewable and clean energy generation with solar (SPP), wind (WPP), geothermal (GPP) and hydroelectric power plants (HPP). Its portfolio has 104.08 MWe of hydroelectric installed capacity consisting of 4 HPPs.\n15. **Akenerji (AKENR)** - A partnership of Akkök Holding and the Czech energy company ČEZ, Akenerji's operating HPP portfolio corresponds to around 289 MW of hydroelectric installed capacity. In addition to hydroelectric assets, its portfolio also includes wind and natural gas plants. In total, it has 1,221 MW of installed capacity with 9 plants.\n\nIn addition, in wind turbine manufacturing, firms such as TPI Composites Türkiye, Siemens Gamesa Türkiye, Nordex Türkiye, GE Renewable Energy and Enercon Türkiye support wind energy projects in Türkiye. In solar panel manufacturing, domestic manufacturers such as CW Enerji, Kalyon Holding and Naturel Enerji stand out. HT Solar is Türkiye's largest solar panel manufacturer in terms of both production capacity and export volume. In the hydroelectric sector, Voith Hydro Türkiye is one of the leading firms with more than a hundred projects and offers turnkey solutions.", "57b47cdd-f3a8-45dd-835c-e7c76daf5105": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are followed by institutions such as [Gedik Yatırım](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) because of their large installed capacity and publicly traded structure.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n\n### ✅ Leading Renewable Energy Companies\n\n- ###🔋 Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)\n\t- It is focused entirely on renewable sources.\n\t- It has HPP, WPP and SPP projects.\n\t- It is traded on Borsa İstanbul.[[1]](https://www.gcmyatirim.com.tr/borsa/endeks/bist-elektrik-xelkt)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- ###⚡ Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)\n\t- It stands out with its geothermal and HPP projects.\n\t- It has a broad renewable portfolio.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- ###💡 Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)\n\t- It is a giant in green energy and distribution.\n\t- It is rapidly increasing its renewable investments.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- ###📊 Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)\n\t- It is active globally and domestically.\n\t- It has a diversified energy portfolio.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- ###☀️ Margün Enerji\n\t- It is a leader in solar energy (SPP) investments.\n\t- It builds plants in Türkiye and abroad.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://tr.investing.com/stock-screener/tuerkiye/energy/renewable-energy)\n\nIf you tell me which **energy type** (Solar, Wind, Geothermal) or **company size** you would like to focus on for investment or sector analysis, I can narrow down the details.", "58f7344f-e9ee-4e17-b1fc-0656084af724": "There are many important firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye. These firms play a critical role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. According to January 2026 TÜREB data, the leading names among Türkiye's largest wind investors and other important players are listed below:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - One of Türkiye's leading energy companies, Enerjisa Üretim is one of the largest investors in the sector with 1,035 MW of installed wind energy capacity. The company has a broad portfolio and stands out for the diversity of its energy generation.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - A partnership of Germany-based EnBW and Borusan Holding, the company has 773 MW of wind energy capacity. It operates important wind farms in various regions of Türkiye.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios, Polat Enerji has 772 MW of installed capacity. The company owns plants such as Seyitali WPP that have been operating for many years with high efficiency. It also owns one of Türkiye's first facilities whose acceptance has been completed as a licensed wind power plant with storage (DRES).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - Operating within Eksim Holding, Eksim Enerji is among Türkiye's important private sector players with 733 MW of wind energy capacity.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - With 702 MW of installed wind energy capacity, it is one of the large players in the sector. GÜRİŞ also undertakes the construction, mechanical and electrical installation work of various wind farms.\n6.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - A Doğan Holding affiliate, Galata Wind is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that are strongly associated with wind energy. It has important wind investments such as Şah WPP, Mersin WPP and Taşpınar WPP, and reached a total installed capacity of approximately 354 MW as of the end of 2025. The company also stands out with hybrid solar investments and battery storage projects.\n7.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its renewable energy portfolio includes wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW. Together with its hydroelectric and solar power plants, the company has a broad range of renewable energy.\n8.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - Standing out for many years with its renewable energy investments, Zorlu Enerji maintains assets such as Demirciler WPP in Türkiye in addition to its wind investments in Pakistan. The company completed the process of transferring Gökçedağ WPP at the end of 2025.\n9.  **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates many wind farms such as Düzova WPP, Ziyaret WPP and Salman WPP. It has plants in different provinces such as İzmir, Hatay, Kırklareli, Tekirdağ, Balıkesir, Muğla and Istanbul.\n10. **Akenerji (AKENR)** - Also including wind energy in its renewable energy portfolio, Akenerji has the Ayyıldız WPP investment in Balıkesir with approximately 28.2 MW of installed capacity. The company has a mixed renewable energy portfolio, mostly together with hydroelectric and other generation sources.\n11. **Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It has important wind energy investments such as the Bandırma Wind Power Plant (BARES). BARES is one of Türkiye's largest wind energy investments and, with 50 MW of installed capacity, can meet the electricity needs of a settlement of 80,000 people.\n12. **Mogan Enerji** - It operates large wind farms such as Albay Çiğiltepe WPP (173 MW) and the Ulu Wind Farm (120 MW).\n\nIn addition to these firms, companies such as İş Enerji, Alto Holding, Universal Wind Enerji, Yıldızlar Enerji, Enerjisa Elektrik, RES Anatolia Holding, Ece Tur İnşaat, Aydem Enerji, Tatlıpınar Enerji, Fernas Enerji, Türkerler Holding and Ulusoy Enerji are also among the operators of important wind farms in Türkiye.", "5e2c94ff-9b54-4d37-99a1-ea060a02465f": "The leading companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://tr.investing.com/stock-screener/tuerkiye/energy/renewable-energy)[[3]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n\n- **Elektrik Üretim AŞ (EÜAŞ):** With its high-capacity public hydroelectric and renewable plants, it is Türkiye's largest electricity producer.[[1]](https://www.capital.com.tr/haberler/tum-haberler/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-aciklandi)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji:** With its broad renewable and conventional portfolio, it is one of the largest private players in the sector.[[1]](https://www.capital.com.tr/haberler/tum-haberler/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-aciklandi)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It has a broad portfolio made up of hydroelectric (HPP), solar (SPP), wind (WPP) and hybrid plants.[[1]](https://www.akfen.com.tr/yatirimlar/yenilenebilir-enerji/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It manages a large portfolio focused entirely on renewable sources (hydro, wind, etc.).[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** It is among Türkiye's pioneering companies, particularly in geothermal energy generation.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** It stands out with its huge investments and plants in solar energy (for example the Konya Karapınar SPP).[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n- **Galata Wind Enerji (GWIND):** It is one of the important listed companies focused on wind and renewable energy generation.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n- **CW Enerji and Alfa Solar Enerji:** They are the main manufacturers that stand out in solar panel production and renewable energy engineering.[[1]](https://tr.investing.com/stock-screener/tuerkiye/energy/renewable-energy)[[2]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/)\n\nWould you like more detailed information about these companies' **stock market performance**, **installed capacity breakdown** or **a specific energy type (solar, wind, geothermal)**?", "606acbb0-4269-4f94-a98c-db7e67538adf": "The main firms operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye include both large players traded on Borsa İstanbul and those that stand out in the private sector. Türkiye has significant potential in wind energy, and many firms continue their investments in this field.\n\nThe main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios, Polat Enerji stands out in particular for its large-scale plants. The company's notable projects include Soma WPP, which with 328.9 MW of installed capacity is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe; Geycek WPP, Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant (combining wind, solar and energy storage systems); and Ege WPP, the first facility whose acceptance has been completed as a licensed wind power plant with storage (DRES).\n2.  **Eksim Enerji** - Although it is not traded on Borsa İstanbul, Eksim Enerji, part of Eksim Holding, is among Türkiye's largest private sector wind energy players. The company is also known for accelerating its hybrid plant investments.\n3.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of the firms that give wind energy an important place in their renewable energy portfolio. Gökçedağ WPP in Osmaniye, with 135 MW of installed capacity, is among Türkiye's large wind farms.\n4.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind energy investments. The company has projects such as the Şah Wind Farm in Balıkesir.\n5.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Cited among the largest renewable energy companies in Türkiye, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji also has significant investments in wind energy.\n6.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the important wind energy investors traded on Borsa İstanbul. It stands out with projects such as the Uşak Wind Farm. The company is taking steps to increase its installed capacity.\n7.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - As one of Türkiye's largest renewable energy companies, it also owns wind power plants. It currently operates five wind farms. The Balıkesir Wind Farm, with 143 MW of installed capacity, is operated by Enerjisa Elektrik.\n8.  **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out for their wind energy investments. Tatlıpınar WPP in Balıkesir, with 127 MW of installed capacity, is one of the important plants.\n9.  **Akenerji** - It is one of the companies that also include wind energy in their renewable energy portfolio. Its Ayyıldız WPP investment operating in Balıkesir has approximately 28.2 MW of installed capacity.\n10. **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - An investor member of the Turkish Wind Energy Association, Borusan EnBW Enerji operates important wind farms such as Saros WPP. Saros WPP operates in Çanakkale with 138 MW of installed capacity.\n11. **GÜRİŞ** - It is one of the firms that undertake construction, mechanical and electrical installation work in wind power plant projects and also operate plants. It has projects such as Kocatepe WPP.\n12. **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates various wind farms such as Düzova WPP, Ziyaret WPP and Salman WPP.", "6199c19d-71a2-49e1-98a4-4d3b93eedcc8": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Polat Enerji A.Ş.**\n   Polat Enerji operates the Soma Wind Power Plant (WPP), which with 328.9 MWm of installed capacity is among the top ten onshore wind farms in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   It operates a total of 7 wind farms: İmbat WPP, Derbent WPP, Isıder WPP, Korda WPP, Kovancı WPP, Kanat WPP and Pruva WPP. The total installed capacity of these plants is 451.1 MW. ([akfenren.com.tr](https://www.akfenren.com.tr/varliklarimiz/res/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Çalık Enerji**\n   Çalık Enerji operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant (WPP) in Urla, İzmir, which generates 155 GWh of electricity per year. ([demirciliruzgar.com](https://www.demirciliruzgar.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Boydak Enerji**\n   Boydak Enerji operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant in the Silivri district of Istanbul, which generates 151 GWh of electricity per year. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Demirer Holding**\n   Demirer Holding operates the Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in Şarköy, Tekirdağ, which generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Enercon GmbH**\n   There are 651 Enercon turbines at 24 plants in Türkiye, with a total installed capacity of 964.50 MW. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar-turbini/enercon/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **RT Enerji**\n   Operating plants such as Adapazarı WPP, Bozüyük WPP, Çandır WPP and Kandıra WPP, RT Enerji has a total of 377.4 MWe of installed capacity. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Livera Elektrik**\n   Operating plants such as Poyraz WPP and Gülpınar WPP, Livera Elektrik is active in the wind energy sector. ([liveraenergy.com](https://liveraenergy.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Eawind**\n   Specialising in wind turbine blade manufacturing and repair, Eawind holds an important position in the wind energy sector in Türkiye. ([eawind.com](https://www.eawind.com/references/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Medyol Enerji**\n    Offering wind power plant infrastructure solutions, Medyol Enerji provides services such as power transmission lines, substations and switchyard works. ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://www.medyolenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese firms hold a significant share of Türkiye's wind energy sector and contribute to renewable energy generation through various plants.", "63ffa08c-2db8-4a51-a5a8-a84ce555d637": "There are many large energy companies and specialised firms installing solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye. These companies are delivering important projects to meet the country's growing energy needs and diversify its renewable energy sources. Here are some of the prominent large energy companies and firms building solar power plants in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **CW Enerji** - One of Türkiye's leading solar panel manufacturers, CW Enerji also carries out turnkey SPP projects. It has an annual solar panel production capacity of 1.8 GW and has SPP projects of different sizes in many provinces of Türkiye.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji** - One of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, Zorlu Enerji obtains a significant portion of its total installed capacity from renewable sources. In addition to hydroelectric, wind and geothermal plants in Türkiye, the company also has solar power plants.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Operating within Akfen Holding, the company has built various modern power plants in many regions of Türkiye over the last five years. Its portfolio includes solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW.\n4.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim focuses on domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation. The company currently has two solar power plants.\n5.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel manufacturing and renewable energy solutions. With production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, the company has a total production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n6.  **Ersis Enerji** - It is an organisation specialising in solar panel solutions and SPP projects. Having carried out successful work in solar panel installation, Ersis Enerji holds an important place in the renewable energy sector.\n7.  **Entegre Solar** - Founded in 2019 as an Entegre Grup affiliate, Entegre Solar provides engineering, procurement and construction (EPC) services for rooftop and ground-mounted solar energy systems. It develops turnkey projects for buildings with high energy consumption such as schools, business centres, warehouses, hospitals, hotels, shopping malls, fuel stations and factories.\n8.  **Teknik Solar Enerji Aydınlatma Sanayi Limited Şirketi** - Founded in 2014, it is a manufacturing and services firm operating in the photovoltaic energy generation sector. With an annual solar panel production capacity of 40 MW, it is one of Türkiye's leading solar panel manufacturers. It offers a wide range of services such as SPP investment and technical consulting, project design, system design, and licensed and unlicensed plant installations.\n9.  **IBT Solar** - As one of Türkiye's pioneering firms in photovoltaic systems since 2013, it provides services across the country with standards-compliant applications and expert teams.\n10. **TURECO Enerji** - Installing ground-mounted and rooftop turnkey solar energy systems in Türkiye since 2014, it is one of the strong organisations in the photovoltaic energy sector.\n11. **GES Enerji San. ve Tic. Ltd. Şti.** - It is the energy firm that started operating in renewable energy in 2005 and was the first to carry the name GES. It carries out work on many SPP projects and on the installation and commissioning of biodiesel and biogas facilities, in our country and abroad.\n12. **Powergie (a Tunçmatik affiliate)** - A subsidiary of Tunçmatik, Powergie built one of Türkiye's largest solar power plants, with a capacity of 8 MW, in Kızören, Konya.\n\nBy utilising Türkiye's solar energy potential, these companies both contribute to sustainable energy generation and play an important role in helping the country reach its energy independence goals.", "64fe679d-b91b-4d28-a51b-b013c16546c3": "The leading private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye are listed below:\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is the largest private sector producer in this field in Türkiye. The company's notable plants include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP, the largest HPP operated by the private sector with 626.85 MW of installed capacity; the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP, the second largest with 582.1 MW; and the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant with 500 MW of installed capacity. The Oymapınar HPP, with 540 MW of installed capacity, is also part of Cengiz Enerji.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim owns a total of 12 hydroelectric plants with 1,350 MW of installed capacity. With plants in Adana, Kahramanmaraş, Artvin and Trabzon, the company is one of the market leaders in private sector electricity generation.\n3.  **ENERGO-PRO Türkiye** - The Turkish arm of Czech Republic-based ENERGO-PRO, established in 2010, generates 1.7 TWh of energy with 8 hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 475 MW. Its important plants include the Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP with 280 MW of installed capacity and the Karakurt Dam and HPP with 97 MW of installed capacity.\n4.  **Akenerji** - Starting its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji has around 289 MW of hydroelectric installed capacity. In addition to its hydroelectric assets, the company also owns wind and natural gas plants.\n5.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Founded by Akfen Holding in 2007, the company has a 100% renewable energy portfolio. Its hydroelectric portfolio includes 12 HPPs operating in different regions of Türkiye. The total installed capacity of these plants is 228.7 MW, and their annual generation capacity is approximately 895 GWh.\n6.  **Aydem Enerji** - The founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants. The company's Bereket 1 and 2 HPPs have 3.15 MW of installed capacity, Toros HPP 49 MW and Mentaş HPP 49.6 MW.\n7.  **Zorlu Enerji** - Operating seven hydroelectric plants, Zorlu Enerji supports Türkiye in reaching its renewable energy targets.\n8.  **Enda Enerji Holding (ENDAE)** - Enda Enerji, which owns 13 power plants based entirely on renewable sources, has 4 hydroelectric plants in its portfolio, with a total installed capacity of 104.08 MWe. Among these plants, the Çaygören HPP in Balıkesir, the Akçay HPP in Aydın and the Eğlence I and Eğlence II HPPs in Adana stand out.\n9.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and has Geothermal Power Plants, Hydroelectric Power Plants and Wind Power Plants.", "67746f00-4d47-4e10-b0bd-94218a965471": "There are many leading private companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye. These companies play an important role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are some of the private companies in Türkiye that generate the most hydroelectric power or have important hydroelectric plants in their portfolio:\n\n1.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is known as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants (HPP), with a total installed capacity of 852.1 MWm. 71.1% of Aydem Enerji's total installed capacity consists of HPPs.\n2.  **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - Operating within IC Holding, the company has an HPP portfolio of 9 hydroelectric plants with approximately 388 MW of installed capacity. Its plants are located in cities such as Trabzon, Erzincan, Tokat, Mersin and Giresun.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - The company's portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a total capacity of 228.7 MW. These plants are located in different basins such as the Sakarya, Kızılırmak and Çoruh rivers and have an annual generation capacity of approximately 895 GWh.\n4.  **Akenerji** - Starting its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji's operating HPP portfolio has approximately 289 MW of hydroelectric installed capacity. In addition to HPPs, the company's portfolio also includes wind and natural gas plants.\n5.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim currently operates 12 hydroelectric plants. The company focuses on the use of domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation.\n6.  **ENKA** - One of the largest electricity generation companies in the private sector, ENKA has a total installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, representing 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. The company's power plants also include hydroelectric plants.\n7.  **Zorlu Enerji** - An important player in Türkiye's energy sector, Zorlu Enerji continues its operations with seven hydroelectric and three wind power plants.\n8.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and has Geothermal Power Plants, Hydroelectric Power Plants and Wind Power Plants. HPP capacity of 81.37 MW is part of the portfolio.\n9.  **Enda Enerji Holding (ENDAE)** - It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul with hydroelectric plants in their portfolio. ENDAE has 104.08 MWe of hydroelectric installed capacity consisting of 4 HPPs.\n10. **ENERGO-PRO Türkiye** - Entering the Turkish market in 2010, ENERGO-PRO generates 1.7 TWh of energy per year in Türkiye with 8 hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW. The HPPs it operates include Reşadiye 1-2-3 HPP, Aralık HPP, Hamzalı HPP, Meydancık Eko HPP, Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP, and Karakurt Dam and HPP.", "69a12740-d076-4b2c-a57d-ea06e6a7171d": "The main firms operating wind power plants in Türkiye and other companies playing an important role in this field are listed below:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - With 1,035 MW of installed wind energy capacity as of January 2026, it is one of Türkiye's largest wind investors.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - With 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity, it is one of Türkiye's leading wind energy companies.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It has 772 MW of installed wind energy capacity as of January 2026. The company has important plants such as Seyitali WPP (İzmir) and Geycek WPP (Kırşehir).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - Although it is not traded on Borsa İstanbul, Eksim Enerji, part of Eksim Holding, is among Türkiye's largest private sector wind energy players with 733 MW of installed capacity.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - With 702 MW of installed wind energy capacity as of January 2026, it holds an important place in the sector. It has projects such as Kocatepe WPP (Afyon) and Fatma WPP.\n6.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its renewable energy portfolio includes wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n7.  **Galata Wind** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul and operating in the wind energy sector.\n8.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's large renewable energy companies and also has wind energy investments.\n9.  **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates various wind farms such as Düzova WPP (İzmir), Ziyaret WPP (Hatay) and Salman WPP (İzmir).\n10. **Akenerji (AKENR)** - It is one of the companies that also include wind energy within their renewable energy portfolio. Its Ayyıldız WPP investment in Balıkesir has approximately 28.2 MW of installed capacity.", "6a7b957f-422a-4219-b6a6-30269f1a4cc2": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers are the private sector firms that, apart from the public entity EÜAŞ, generate the most electricity and have the most installed capacity.[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[3]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)According to current data, the largest private electricity producers are as follows:\n\n- **ENKA Enerji** : It is one of the main producers at the top of the private sector in both installed capacity and total generation rankings.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim** : With its broad portfolio and its wind, solar, hydroelectric and natural gas plants, it is among the largest in the sector.\n- **Eren Enerji** : It stands out among the companies with the highest electricity generation in the private sector, particularly with its thermal and coal plants.\n- **İÇDAŞ** : With its high installed capacity and generation capacity, it ranks near the top.\n- **Cengiz Enerji** : It is one of the leading producers with its natural gas and other energy investments.\n- **EMBA Power** : With large investments such as the Hunutlu Thermal Power Plant, it ranks high in generation.\n- **Limak Enerji** : With various power plants, it is among the top 10 companies generating the most electricity.\n- **Çelikler Holding** : It has a significant share in thermal and renewable energy generation.\n- **Aydem Enerji** : It is known particularly for its strength in renewable energy (hydroelectric, wind).[](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[3]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[4]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)\n\nIf you wish, I can tell you about the following:**Which energy sources** these companies use (coal, natural gas, renewables) Which companies **are traded on the stock exchange** (share details)", "6a9efe76-ebb9-4281-9824-6d4a2e675d29": "Some of the large energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments are as follows:\n\n1. **OYAK Çimento**\n   It has commissioned a solar power plant in Beypazarı, Ankara with 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp of installed capacity. This project is the largest renewable energy project implemented at a single location by an industrial manufacturer in Türkiye. ([solargundem.com](https://www.solargundem.com/oyak-cimento-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oz-tuketim-amacli-gunes-enerjisi-santralini-devreye-aldi-3419461?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ACWA Power**\n   This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two giant solar power plants with a total capacity of 5,000 MW in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. These projects stand out as one of the largest foreign direct investments in the Turkish energy sector. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji (AYDEM)**\n   It operates solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants. It generates electricity in Türkiye exclusively from renewable energy sources and has more than 1,000 MW of installed capacity. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji (NATEN)**\n   It operates in the installation and operation of solar power plants. The company carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house and has developed many ground-mounted solar plant projects in Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Margün Enerji (MAGEN)**\n   It works in solar power generation and project development. It carries out turnkey SPP installations and provides operation services. It has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in Türkiye's solar energy sector.", "6b8403c8-729c-4d87-a694-c0c6eb63d593": "The **private sector companies** and groups with the largest installed capacity and generation in hydroelectric energy (HPP) in Türkiye are as follows:[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its hydroelectric portfolio and total renewable/balanced energy capacity, it is at the top of the private sector. With hydroelectric capacity of 1,353 MW, it is one of the largest players in the sector.[[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313)[[2]](https://www.iklimhaber.org/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisini-ele-alan-mw100-raporu-aciklandi/)\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With large projects such as the **Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP** in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, it is one of Türkiye's largest HPP operators in the private sector.[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. With its large HPP portfolio (approximately 850+ MWm of installed capacity), it is among the country's leading hydroelectric producers.[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Limak Enerji (Limak Holding):** With the Çetin, Alkumru, Kirazlık, Uzunçayır, Kargı, Gürsöğüt, Seyrantepe, Pembelik and Tatar HPP projects, it has a total hydroelectric installed capacity exceeding 1,300 MW.[[1]](https://www.limak.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerji-uretimi)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is one of the important producers that stand out with numerous hydroelectric plants located in various regions of Türkiye.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Akenerji:** With HPP investments such as Uluabat, Feke I, Feke II, Gökkaya, Burç and Bulam, it has long been an active player in private sector electricity generation.[[1]](https://www.akenerji.com.tr/yatirimlarimiz)\n\n*(Note: In the overall ranking, the largest hydroelectric producer in Türkiye is the public company **EÜAŞ** ; in the private sector, ENKA, Enerjisa Üretim and Cengiz Enerji lead in terms of installed capacity).* [[1]](https://hizmetix.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-kim/)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)Feel free to let me know if you do not want more detailed information about a specific **company's HPP portfolio**, **location** or **generation figures**.", "6cef18c1-ad2b-48ba-8aae-d7341792467a": "Among the large energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye are pioneering names that have delivered giant projects.\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji** : In Karapınar, Konya, it built the Karapınar YEKA-1 SPP project, one of the largest solar plants in Türkiye and Europe.[](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/) [[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOorwI54JprxSOin6oAkAsIMnxZSu6o0rUOS3cC38xb9R3BvCO5Ot)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/)[[3]](https://ceyrekmuhendis.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-santralleri/)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji** : With its renewable energy investments and unlicensed/licensed SPP projects, it is one of the largest players in the sector.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Zorlu Enerji** : It is one of the large groups that have added solar energy to their portfolio and build renewable energy plants both in Türkiye and abroad.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** : It has solar power plants in operation in different regions of Türkiye and hybrid plant investments.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **CW Enerji** : It is one of the leading firms carrying out both panel manufacturing and large-scale ground-mounted and rooftop SPP installations.[](https://www.facebook.com/cwenerji/videos/t%C3%BCrkiyenin-ve-avrupan%C4%B1n-en-b%C3%BCy%C3%BCk-g%C3%BCne%C5%9F-paneli-%C3%BCreticisi-cw-enerji-sekt%C3%B6rde-en-ye/759288965213232/?locale=ms_MY) [[1]](https://www.facebook.com/cwenerji/videos/t%C3%BCrkiyenin-ve-avrupan%C4%B1n-en-b%C3%BCy%C3%BCk-g%C3%BCne%C5%9F-paneli-%C3%BCreticisi-cw-enerji-sekt%C3%B6rde-en-ye/759288965213232/?locale=ms_MY)\n- **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri** : In addition to solar panel manufacturing, it delivers large turnkey SPP projects.[](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/) [[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n\nIs there any other detail you would like to learn about solar energy investments? For example:\n\n- **Investment costs or incentives**\n- **Hybrid (solar + wind/storage) plant projects**\n- A specific **company's total installed capacity**", "6fac6747-1c29-4b34-a11e-66c8a3099121": "The leading private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye include [Enerjisa Üretim](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/), [Cengiz Enerji](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji), [Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr) and Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)[[3]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[4]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)Leading Private Hydroelectric Producers\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its broad portfolio, it is among Türkiye's largest private electricity producers and has significant HPP capacity.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With large projects such as the Beyhan HPP in Bingöl, it is one of the largest HPP operators in the private sector.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Starting from Türkiye's first private sector HPP investments (Bereket 1-2), it focuses entirely on renewable sources.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It owns numerous hydroelectric plants installed in various provinces of Türkiye.\n- **Energo-Pro:** With the numerous HPPs it operates across the country, it has a significant hydroelectric generation volume.[](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr) [[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)[[2]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[3]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)[[4]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[5]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri)[[6]](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html)\n\nIn the public sector, the largest producer is the state entity [EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.)](https://www.euas.gov.tr/).[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)For which company would you like more detailed information on **installed capacity** or the **list of plants**?", "735c15a4-7f57-45b7-9350-f6e7db4bee83": "Among Türkiye's largest private sector electricity producers, ENKA, Eren Enerji and Enerjisa Üretim are at the top.[[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)Although the public entity EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim AŞ) ranks first overall, the other large companies that generate the most electricity and lead in the private sector are as follows:[[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n\n### Largest Private Electricity Producers\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** It is the leader in the private sector in terms of generation and capacity.\n- **Eren Enerji:** With its high share of generation, it is among the largest in the private sector.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its broad plant portfolio, it is one of the largest players in the sector.\n- **İÇDAŞ:** With its intensive industrial and energy production, it ranks near the top.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** It is one of the large producers with high installed capacity.\n- **Limak Enerji:** It is one of the leading groups by generation volume.\n- **EMBA Power:** It is on the list with its thermal and large-scale generation facilities.\n- **Çelikler Holding:** It is active in domestic coal and electricity generation.[[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi-28-02-24/)[[3]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[4]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[5]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n\nIf you wish, I can also explain in detail **which energy sources** (natural gas, coal, renewables) these companies use or their **installed capacity rankings**.", "74c5cb90-76bf-40de-9f02-bd7ec150e02a": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   It is one of Türkiye's largest renewable energy producers. As of 2024, it has more than 4,500 MW of installed capacity. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Kalyon Enerji**\n   It is making significant investments in solar energy. In 2024, it commissioned the 1,000 MW Karapınar Solar Power Plant. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Zorlu Enerji**\n   It operates in geothermal, wind and solar energy. As of 2024, its total installed capacity is 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW is in Türkiye and 348.4 MW is abroad. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Aydem Enerji**\n   With its hydroelectric, wind and geothermal power plants, it reached 1,180 MW of installed capacity in 2024. The company aims to increase its total installed capacity by approximately 80% by 2026. ([getmidas.com](https://www.getmidas.com/midasin-kulaklari/guclu-yatirimlariyla-on-plana-cikan-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-p-44847?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   With its solar, wind and hydroelectric power plants, it has 699 MW of installed capacity as of 2024. The company is strengthening its position in the sector with hybrid energy projects. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Borusan EnBW Enerji**\n   It operates in wind energy and reached 725 MW of installed capacity as of 2024. The company is increasing its capacity with new wind turbine investments. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Polat Enerji**\n   With its wind and solar power plants, it has more than 500 MW of wind energy capacity as of 2024. The company is strengthening its position in the sector through technology partnerships. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Galata Wind Enerji**\n   It generates wind and solar energy. As of 2024, it reached 354.2 MW of installed capacity. With its low leverage ratio and net profitability, it is seen as a safe haven for investors. ([hisse.net](https://www.hisse.net/haber/turkiye-de-2050-yilinda-yenilenebilir-enerjinin-payi-yuzde-77-120-gw-yatirim-ve-borsadaki-sirketler-18133?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Kalyon Güneş Teknolojileri**\n   With integrated cell and module production, it is of strategic importance. As of 2024, it generated USD 61 million in revenue and reported USD 11.4 million in EBITDA. ([hisse.net](https://www.hisse.net/haber/turkiye-de-2050-yilinda-yenilenebilir-enerjinin-payi-yuzde-77-120-gw-yatirim-ve-borsadaki-sirketler-18133?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **CW Enerji**\n    It is one of Türkiye's largest PV panel manufacturers. As of 2024, it generated TL 3.1 billion in turnover and reported TL 865 million in EBITDA. ([hisse.net](https://www.hisse.net/haber/turkiye-de-2050-yilinda-yenilenebilir-enerjinin-payi-yuzde-77-120-gw-yatirim-ve-borsadaki-sirketler-18133?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to the country's energy transition by making significant investments in Türkiye's renewable energy sector.", "754ddb54-f9b8-4a16-b426-135d6be21f2b": "There are many important players among the private companies generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye. These companies make significant contributions to Türkiye's security of energy supply and renewable energy targets. Here are some of the prominent private companies:\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's strongest private sector producers of hydroelectric energy. It generates clean energy with six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity. The Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, is the largest hydroelectric plant in Türkiye operated by the private sector.\n2.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, with a total installed capacity of 852.1 MWm. 71.1 percent of Aydem Enerji's total installed capacity of 1,198 MWm consists of hydroelectric plants.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is a company focused on the use of domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation. It currently has 12 hydroelectric plants.\n4.  **Energo-Pro** - It started operating in the Turkish market in 2010 and operates 8 hydroelectric power plants. It has an annual generation of 1.7 TWh (100% from renewable hydroelectric sources). With the Alpaslan 2 Dam and HPP project, with 280 MW of installed capacity, the company operates the largest dam in Türkiye operated by an independent power producer.\n5.  **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Part of IC Holding, the company has an HPP portfolio of 9 hydroelectric plants. Located in Trabzon, Erzincan, Tokat, Mersin and Giresun, these plants have a total installed capacity of approximately 388 MW.\n6.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is among the companies with a 100 percent renewable energy portfolio. Its hydroelectric portfolio includes 12 HPPs operating in different regions of Türkiye. The total installed capacity of these plants is 228.7 MW, and their annual generation capacity is stated as approximately 895 GWh.\n7.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It continues its operations with seven hydroelectric plants. The company generates electricity with geothermal, wind and hydroelectric plants.\n8.  **Enda Enerji Holding** - It has 13 power plants based entirely on renewable sources and a total installed capacity of 189.12 MWe. Its portfolio includes 4 hydroelectric plants, with a total installed capacity of 104.08 MWe.\n9.  **ENKA** - It is one of the largest companies in the private sector in overall electricity generation, with a total installed capacity of 3,978 MW. Although its installed capacity specific to hydroelectric energy is not stated, its size in overall energy generation is notable.\n10. **Limak Enerji** - With 3,033 MW of installed capacity, it is among Türkiye's largest electricity producers. The company also has hydroelectric plants.", "766a3f56-d565-448c-bbb7-9b064629d501": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation and investment in Türkiye are as follows:[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It is one of the pioneering companies whose portfolio consists largely of domestic and renewable sources, with large investments in wind, solar and hydroelectric.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It is a company that builds and operates only renewable energy (hydroelectric, wind and solar) plants, with projects all over Türkiye.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** With its geothermal, wind and hydroelectric power plants, it is among the large players in the renewable energy generation market.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Aydem Enerji:** It is an established energy group that built Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant and also focuses on wind and solar energy investments.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Akenerji:** It is one of the companies that have long been generating clean energy with hydroelectric and wind plants.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\nWould you like more detailed information about renewable energy companies' **share performance**, **generation types (solar, wind, geothermal)** or **installed capacities**?", "7844d634-274e-4300-a85c-605f15abbaff": "The leading private sector companies with the largest installed capacity and generation in hydroelectric energy (HPP) in Türkiye:[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n\n- **[Cengiz Enerji](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji):** With 6 hydroelectric plants, it has approximately 2,265 MW of installed capacity. It operates the private sector's largest HPP, Yukarı Kaleköy (626.85 MW) in Bingöl, and its 2nd largest HPP, Beyhan-1 (582.1 MW) in Elazığ. Aşağı Kaleköy and the Oymapınar HPP in Antalya are also in its portfolio.[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n- **[Enerjisa Üretim](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/):** With the numerous HPPs it owns, it is among Türkiye's largest private electricity producers and renewable energy players.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** With the numerous HPPs in its portfolio across Türkiye (more than 228 MW of installed capacity), it is one of the leading private companies in hydroelectric and renewable energy generation.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **[Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/):** It is one of the large hydroelectric investors that delivered Türkiye's first private sector HPP projects and whose portfolio consists entirely of renewable sources.[[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **[Zorlu Enerji](https://www.zorluenerji.com.tr/):** With the multiple HPP projects it owns, it is one of the important private groups operating in hydroelectric and wind energy generation.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n*(Note: The largest share of overall electricity and hydroelectric generation in Türkiye belongs to the state-owned **EÜAŞ - Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** .)* [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)Would you like more details on the **installed capacity ranking** of hydroelectric plants or **a specific company's projects**?", "7a504893-5c05-4de9-aa89-dd8433e69cba": "The leading energy companies building, operating or developing large-scale solar power plant (SPP) projects in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji (Kalyon Holding):** It owns **Kalyon Karapınar SPP** , located in Karapınar, Konya, which with 1,350 MW of installed capacity is the largest solar power plant in Türkiye and Europe. It also has a solar panel manufacturing factory (Kalyon PV) in Ankara.[[1]](https://www.kalyonenerji.com/tr/portfoyumuz)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/sirket-haberleri/karapinar-ges-1-milyar-dolarlik-dogal-gaz-kullaniminin-onune-gecti/52224)\n- **CW Enerji:** Based in Antalya, it builds large-scale ground-mounted and rooftop SPP projects and produces approximately 1.8 GW of solar panels per year.[[1]](https://cw-enerji.com/tr/index.html)\n- **Alfa Solar Enerji:** It is one of the companies manufacturing photovoltaic panels at its factory in the Kırıkkale Organised Industrial Zone while also offering system and consulting solutions for large SPP projects.[[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is one of the large renewable energy producers whose portfolio includes hydroelectric, wind and a significant share of SPP investments (121.4 MW of SPP capacity).[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Margün Enerji:** It is among the companies building and operating numerous licensed and unlicensed ground-mounted and rooftop solar power plants across Türkiye (an SPP portfolio of approximately 118 MWp).[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Galata Wind (100% Renewable):** It is growing the share of solar and wind energy in its portfolio with projects such as Çorum SPP (9.4 MW), Taşpınar Hybrid SPP (79 MW WPP + hybrid SPP) and Erzurum SPP (24.7 MW).[[1]](https://www.doganholding.com.tr/sektorler/elektrik-uretimi/)\n- **Naturel Enerji:** It is one of the large publicly traded firms developing, building and generating electricity from numerous solar power plants in different regions of Türkiye.\n\nWould you like detailed information on **financial incentives**, **licensing processes** or **installation costs in a specific region** for solar energy investments?", "7d89163e-7377-4479-83a2-7beb3dc01a51": "The leading private sector energy companies that generate the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye and hold large HPP (Hydroelectric Power Plant) portfolios are**Cengiz Enerji**, **Enerjisa Üretim**, **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji**, **Limak Enerji** and **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** .[[1]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/hidroelektrik-santrallerimiz/)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)[[3]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)[[4]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/106/yenilenebilir-enerji-santralleri)[[5]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri)[[6]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n### Leading Private Companies and HPP Investments\n\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With the **Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP** in Bingöl, with 626.85 MW of installed capacity, it is home to the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector.[[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It manages a strong HPP portfolio of approximately 1,350 MW with a total of 12 hydroelectric plants located in Adana, Kahramanmaraş, Artvin and Trabzon.[[1]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/hidroelektrik-santrallerimiz/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Having built Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, the company has raised its total renewable energy installed capacity to 1,216 MW with the numerous HPPs in its portfolio.[[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/)[[2]](https://www.dha.com.tr/ekonomi/aydem-yenilenebilir-enerji-kurulu-gucunu-1-216-mwa-yukseltti-2919130)\n- **Limak Enerji:** With dam and run-of-river hydroelectric plants located in different regions of the country, it is among the leading private players in total electricity generation and hydro capacity.[[1]](https://www.forbes.com.tr/ekonomi/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** With the numerous hydroelectric plant (HPP) investments in its portfolio, it is one of the companies that stand out in renewable energy generation.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n*(Note: The largest part of total hydroelectric generation in Türkiye is carried out by the public entity **EÜAŞ - Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** .)* [[1]](https://tr.investing.com/news/forex-news/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-arastrmas-ackland-3257865)If you wish:\n\n- I can detail the companies' **shares of total electricity generation**.\n- I can list the **companies with HPP portfolios** traded on Borsa İstanbul (BİST).\n\nHow would you like to continue?", "825e1f2e-0159-445b-bc07-99dbb94649b1": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   With six hydroelectric plants totalling 2,265 MW of installed capacity, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric producer. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ENKA**\n   With 3,978 MW of installed capacity, ENKA is Türkiye's second largest electricity producer and has significant generation capacity with its hydroelectric plants. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   With 3,901 MW of installed capacity, Enerjisa Üretim is Türkiye's third largest electricity producer and has significant generation capacity with its hydroelectric plants. ([aa.com.tr](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Merge Enerji**\n   Developing projects in hydroelectric, wind and solar energy, Merge Enerji operates the Duru-1 and Duru-2 hydroelectric plants in Amasya, with capacities of 5.29 MW and 5.40 MW. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Kurtsuyu Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**\n   Operating the Daran Hydroelectric Plant with 68.74 MW of installed capacity, the company generates an average of 278 million kWh of energy per year. ([kurtsuyu.com.tr](https://kurtsuyu.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**\n   With 15 active power plants with 526.2 MW of installed capacity, it contributes to Türkiye's renewable energy generation. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://www.turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Energo-Pro**\n   With approximately 100 MW of installed capacity from 5 hydroelectric plants in Sivas, Tokat, Ankara and Artvin, Energo-Pro aims to meet the electricity needs of 610 thousand households by the end of 2020. ([turkiyegazetesi.com.tr](https://www.turkiyegazetesi.com.tr/ekonomi/energo-pro-610-bin-haneyi-aydinlatacak-610351?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and continue their investments aimed at increasing the use of renewable energy sources.", "866af0a3-f390-4b94-8be9-c50600d72c15": "Türkiye's largest private electricity producers hold an important position in the sector with their installed capacity and generation portfolios. Below are the largest private electricity producers by installed capacity as of 31 December 2024:\n\n1. **ENKA**\n   Total installed capacity: 3,978 MWe. ENKA represents 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim**\n   Total installed capacity: 3,901 MWe. Enerjisa Üretim has a balanced generation portfolio of hydroelectric, natural gas and wind power plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji**\n   Total installed capacity: 3,161 MWe. Cengiz Enerji stands out with its generation capacity made up of various energy sources. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji**\n   Total installed capacity: 3,033 MWe. Limak Enerji generates power with hydroelectric and wind power plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji**\n   Total installed capacity: 2,818 MWe. Eren Enerji stands out with its plants based on renewable energy sources. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Çelikler Holding**\n   Total installed capacity: 2,769 MWe. Çelikler Holding generates energy with coal and natural gas plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Aydem Enerji**\n   Total installed capacity: 1,946 MWe. Aydem Enerji generates power with hydroelectric and wind power plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **İÇDAŞ**\n   Total installed capacity: 1,684 MWe. İÇDAŞ generates energy with natural gas and coal plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Bilgin Enerji**\n   Total installed capacity: 1,639 MWe. Bilgin Enerji generates power with hydroelectric and wind power plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Kalyon Enerji**\n    Total installed capacity: 1,500 MWe. Kalyon Enerji generates renewable energy with solar and wind power plants. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's energy generation and play a critical role in meeting the country's electricity needs by drawing on various energy sources.", "8893ca85-72ed-4f3a-a158-f542de15d3a8": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies are identified through reports such as \"MW100, Türkiye's 100 Largest Electricity Generators Survey\", prepared by the international consultancy Kearney together with Enerji Günlüğü. According to these reports, the private companies that stand out based on installed capacity as of 31 December 2024 are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - It is Türkiye's largest private electricity generator. As of 31 December 2024, it has an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe and accounts for approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. ENKA's success in power generation is based on projects such as its natural gas combined cycle plants in Gebze, Adapazarı, İzmir and Kırklareli and the Kameno Photovoltaic Power Plant. The company also invests in renewable energy, aiming for a sustainable future.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe as of 31 December 2024. Enerjisa has a balanced generation portfolio of natural gas, domestic coal, hydroelectric and wind plants.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - It stands out with an installed capacity of 3,161 MWe as of 31 December 2024. The company is notable for its balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It rose to fifth place with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe as of 31 December 2024.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - It had an installed capacity of 2,824 MWe as of 31 December 2019.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - It had an installed capacity of 2,713 MWe as of 31 December 2019.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - It had an installed capacity of 1,965 MWe as of 31 December 2019.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - It is on the list with an installed capacity of 1,665 MWe as of 31 December 2019.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - It had an installed capacity of 1,580 MWe as of 31 December 2019.\n10. **Aksa Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producers. The company, whose main shareholder is Kazancı Holding, has built more than 30 power plants using a variety of sources such as coal, natural gas, wind and hydroelectric power.\n11. **Kalyon Enerji** - In 2024, it achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector, significantly expanding its renewable energy portfolio through its solar power plant (SPP) in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ.", "8b8b91ca-5afc-487f-b654-b0ac81bfa3f3": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**  \n   With six hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 2,265 MW, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric generator. Its prominent facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl with an installed capacity of 626.85 MW and the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP in Elazığ with an installed capacity of 582.1 MW. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Energo-Pro Türkiye**  \n   It operates in Türkiye with eight hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW. Prominent among these plants are the Karakurt Dam and HPP in Kars province and the Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP in Muş province. ([energo-pro.com.tr](https://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Merge Enerji**  \n   It generates a total installed capacity of 10.69 MW with its Duru-1 and Duru-2 hydroelectric plants in Amasya province. It also has wind power plant projects in Çanakkale and Tekirdağ provinces and solar power plant projects in Eskişehir and Ankara provinces. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   It operates across Türkiye with 15 active power plants with a total installed capacity of 526.2 MWe. These plants include hydroelectric, wind and geothermal facilities. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://www.turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**  \n   With eight hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 205 MW, it is one of Türkiye's first private sector electricity generators. It also contributes to power generation with wind and solar energy projects. ([tektug.com](https://www.tektug.com/yesil-projeler/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and contribute to environmentally friendly power generation by increasing the use of renewable energy sources. ", "9080d839-6f68-458e-808b-3c9dce4e25b8": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies are ranked as follows by their installed capacity as of 31 December 2024:\n\n1. **ENKA**: With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it is the largest electricity generator in the private sector. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim**: It ranks second with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji**: It ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,147 MWe. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji**: It ranks fourth with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji**: It ranks fifth with an installed capacity of 2,818 MWe. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies control approximately 50% of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/?utm_source=openai)) ", "92b8aa7d-10e1-4fa6-b151-a2f41eff8caa": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Polat Enerji**  \n   Polat Enerji, which has one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios, reached an installed capacity of 328.9 MWm with the Soma Wind Power Plant established in 2009. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji, which operates 7 wind power plants with an installed capacity of 451.1 MW, holds an important position in the sector with projects such as Sarıtepe WPP. ([akfenren.com.tr](https://www.akfenren.com.tr/varliklarimiz/res/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Eksim Enerji**  \n   With over 1000 MW of licensed capacity, Eksim Enerji is one of the companies with the largest licensed wind energy portfolio in Türkiye, with projects such as Silivri WPP. ([eksimenerji.com.tr](https://eksimenerji.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-enerjisi-santralleri?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Demirer Holding**  \n   The Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in the Şarköy district of Tekirdağ generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year with an installed capacity of 30.5 MW. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Medyol Enerji**  \n   Medyol Enerji, which operates in the wind energy sector with projects such as Çerkeş WPP and Kırklareli Yeni WPP, has a total installed capacity of 50 MW. ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://medyolenerji.com.tr/projelerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Boydak Enerji**  \n   Boydak Enerji, which operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant, generates approximately 151 GWh of electricity per year with this 47.5 MW plant. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **RT Enerji**  \n   RT Enerji, which develops power plant projects based 100% on renewable energy sources, has an installed capacity of 377.4 MWe. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **EOLOS Rüzgar Enerjisi A.Ş.**  \n   Şenköy WPP, located within the borders of Hatay province, targets 110 million kWh of electricity generation per year with an installed capacity of 36 MW. ([santralmadencilik.com](https://www.santralmadencilik.com/eolos-ruzgar.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Çalık Enerji**  \n   Çalık Enerji, which operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant, generates 155 GWh of electricity per year with this plant in Urla, İzmir. ([demirciliruzgar.com](https://www.demirciliruzgar.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Santral Madencilik A.Ş.**  \n    Santral Madencilik A.Ş., the owner of EOLOS Rüzgar Enerjisi A.Ş., was established in 2010 and operates in the wind energy sector with projects such as Şenköy WPP. ([santralmadencilik.com](https://www.santralmadencilik.com/eolos-ruzgar.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in Türkiye's wind energy sector. ", "93b49dea-06df-438f-9bf6-264e6d232f51": "The main energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two large solar power plants in Türkiye with a total capacity of 5,000 MW. The projects will be implemented in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **OYAK Çimento** - It commissioned a solar power plant with an installed capacity of 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp in Beypazarı, Ankara. This project is the largest renewable energy project implemented by an industrial producer in Türkiye at a single location for self-consumption. ([enerjiekonomisi.com](https://www.enerjiekonomisi.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oztuketim-gunes-santralini-devreye-aldi/41773?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants. It generates electricity in Türkiye exclusively from renewable energy sources and has an installed capacity of over 1,000 MW. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates in the field of solar power plant installation and operation. The company carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house and has developed many ground-mounted solar plant projects in Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Margün Enerji** - It works in solar energy generation and project development. It carries out turnkey SPP installations and provides operation services. It has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW, and all of its electricity generation in Türkiye comes from renewable sources. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Enerjisa Enerji** - It is Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions company. Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, the company serves approximately 10.8 million customers in 3 regions and 14 provinces. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **CW Enerji** - It builds on-grid solar power plants in Türkiye that use CW Enerji brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/cw-enerji-solar-panel/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Jinko Solar** - It builds on-grid solar power plants in Türkiye that use Jinko Solar brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/jinko-solar/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in the solar energy sector in Türkiye. ", "94bbdc80-861b-47b0-837a-6a1ad93ce5ac": "The leading private sector companies active in hydroelectric power (HPP) in Türkiye with the highest installed capacity in their portfolios include Enerjisa Üretim, [Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr), Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and Zorlu Enerji. While the public entity EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.) ranks first in overall electricity generation , private companies stand out mainly with their renewable energy portfolios.[](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913) [[1]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[3]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[4]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)\n\n### Leading Private HPP Companies\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** Its large plant portfolio includes a significant share of hydroelectric capacity.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It was the founder of Türkiye's first private HPP and operates numerous hydroelectric plants.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Its portfolio includes notable HPP investments.\n- **Zorlu Enerji and Others:** Players such as Ayen Enerji and Akiş/Akenerji, which generate power through regional projects and run-of-river HPPs, support the sector.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/)[[2]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[3]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[4]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[5]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri)\n\nIf you like, I can prepare the **installed capacity rankings in megawatts (MW)** of private companies or a detailed list of **HPP companies traded on the stock exchange**.", "95813911-165f-4068-9baa-2b2dd3840759": "The leading companies in renewable energy generation in Türkiye stand out for their portfolio size and investment areas.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n### Prominent Companies\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** A large part of its portfolio consists of domestic and renewable sources. It holds a leading position in wind energy investments.[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It has a balanced green energy portfolio of hydroelectric (HPP), solar (SPP) and wind (WPP) plants.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** In addition to renewable energy generation, mainly geothermal and wind, it also invests in electric vehicle charging infrastructure.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/?srsltid=AU7gw4XPpvkW_qut8d3AgXi2qKBls18S53g44rVIYXv74zKphmayk4gw)\n- **Aydem Enerji:** It is one of the long-established generators that built Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **GÜRİŞ, Borusan EnBW Enerji, Polat Enerji and Eksim Enerji:** These are other major investors that stand out with high capacities in wind and renewable installed capacity.[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** It implemented the Karapınar SPP project, one of the country's largest solar plants.[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/iste-turkiyenin-yesil-enerji-devleri/)\n\nIf you like, I can give you more detailed information about these companies' **IPO status** or **installed capacity breakdown (HPP, WPP, SPP)**.", "965857cc-bd46-4c7d-82ef-59941cd15254": "The major companies operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye include [Polat Enerji](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz), [Eksim Enerji](https://eksimenerji.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-enerjisi-santralleri), [Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html), Gürün/Güriş Holding, Sanko Enerji and the publicly listed Galata Wind (GWIND), Aydem Enerji (AYDEM) and Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE).[[1]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)[[2]](https://www.hocaileborsa.com/haber/borsadaki-ruzgar-enerjisi-sirketleri-hangileri)[[3]](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html)[[4]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)[[5]](https://www.facebook.com/sankoenergy/videos/istanbulun-%C3%A7atalca-il%C3%A7esinde-bulunan-sanko-enerji-%C3%A7atalca-r%C3%BCzg%C3%A2r-enerji-santrali/698847111159479/)\n\n### Leading Wind Energy Companies\n\n- **Polat Enerji:** It operates Soma WPP in Manisa, one of Türkiye's largest wind power plants.[[1]](https://www.instagram.com/p/DF5SheotIz0/)[[2]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)\n- **Eksim Enerji:** It has 1000+ MW of licensed wind and renewable power capacity at numerous locations across the country.[[1]](https://eksimenerji.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-enerjisi-santralleri)\n- **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It manages many WPP projects such as Düzova, Ziyaret and Salman in provinces such as İzmir, Hatay and Kırklareli.[[1]](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html)\n- **Güriş Holding:** It is the investor and operator of large-scale wind projects such as Afyon Kocatepe WPP.[[1]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)\n- **Galata Wind (GWIND):** It is a major generator traded on Borsa İstanbul whose portfolio consists entirely of renewable (wind and solar) energy.[[1]](https://www.hocaileborsa.com/haber/borsadaki-ruzgar-enerjisi-sirketleri-hangileri)\n- **Sanko Enerji:** It has built and operated pioneering, high-capacity wind power plants such as İstanbul Çatalca WPP.[[1]](https://www.facebook.com/sankoenergy/videos/istanbulun-%C3%A7atalca-il%C3%A7esinde-bulunan-sanko-enerji-%C3%A7atalca-r%C3%BCzg%C3%A2r-enerji-santrali/698847111159479/)\n- **Aydem Enerji (AYDEM) & Akfen Yenilenebilir (AKFYE):** They have high wind energy capacity within their diversified clean energy portfolios.[[1]](https://www.hocaileborsa.com/haber/borsadaki-ruzgar-enerjisi-sirketleri-hangileri)\n\nWould you like more details about these companies' **installed capacities** or their **plants in a specific region**?", "9d6ef171-3b3b-4301-905b-2afc96c16802": "The main large companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye:[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It generates energy entirely from renewable sources (hydroelectric, wind, solar).\n- **Enerjisa Üretim / Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA):** Its large portfolio includes a significant share of renewable and green energy investments.\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** It is known for its large projects in geothermal, wind and solar energy.\n- **Aydem Enerji:** Renewable hydroelectric, wind and solar plants make up a large part of its portfolio.\n- **Galata Wind Enerji:** It is a publicly listed company focused on 100% renewable (wind and solar) energy generation.\n- **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN):** It is one of the major players providing diversity in power generation globally and in Türkiye.[](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri) [[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[3]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[4]](https://www.mw100.net/?p=23)[[5]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[6]](https://www.gcmyatirim.com.tr/egitim/makaleler/gelecegin-enerji-sektoru-ve-hisseleri-genel-gorunum-ve-yatirim-araclari)\n\nWould you like me to focus on a specific branch of renewable energy (such as solar, wind or geothermal) or on **investment opportunities on the stock exchange**?", "9db48528-72e6-4a3a-beb9-8632bbd39e5d": "The main private sector companies that generate the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye and stand out in this field are `Enerjisa Üretim, Aydem Enerji (Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji), Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and Zorlu Enerji` .[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)Leading Private Companies\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its large portfolio and high installed capacity, it is among Türkiye's largest private electricity generators and operates a significant number of hydroelectric plants (HPP).[](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913) [[1]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[2]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Having implemented Türkiye's first private sector HPP projects, it is one of the leading players in hydroelectric generation with its fully renewable energy-focused portfolio.[](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr) [[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It stands out in renewable energy generation with its numerous HPP projects in different regions of Türkiye.[](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri) [[1]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** With its hydroelectric plants, it is among the major players contributing to the country's renewable and hydro energy supply.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n*Note: The largest share of overall electricity generation and total HPP installed capacity in Türkiye belongs to the public entity **EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim AŞ)** . The private sector, however, has gained a large share in this field through investments made in recent years.* [](https://temsan.gov.tr/p/186/hidroelektrik) [[1]](https://temsan.gov.tr/p/186/hidroelektrik)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)If you like:\n\n- These companies' **installed capacities** \n- Which regions they have **HPP projects** in\n\nwe can examine in more detail. How would you like to proceed?", "a39a176c-4467-408c-927b-ed571a67412a": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies by installed capacity are as follows:\n\n1. **ENKA** - With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it accounts for 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim** - It ranks second with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji** - It ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,147 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji** - It ranks fourth with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji** - It ranks fifth with an installed capacity of 2,818 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant part of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity and are among the largest private players in the sector. ", "a78f1f89-2665-4172-9948-3885f3ac1ded": "The main energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments are as follows:\n\n1. **OYAK Çimento** - It commissioned a solar power plant with an installed capacity of 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp in Beypazarı, Ankara. This project is the largest renewable energy project implemented by an industrial producer in Türkiye at a single location. ([solargundem.com](https://www.solargundem.com/oyak-cimento-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oz-tuketim-amacli-gunes-enerjisi-santralini-devreye-aldi-3419461?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two large solar power plants in Türkiye with a total installed capacity of 5,000 MW. The projects will be carried out in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Zorlu Enerji** - Zorlu Enerji, one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, has a total installed capacity of 991 MW. The company has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in Türkiye. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Enerjisa Enerji** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions company. The company also invests in renewable energy projects. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji, which operates solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants, has an installed capacity of over 1,000 MW and generates electricity exclusively from renewable energy sources. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji, which operates in the field of solar power plant installation and operation, carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Margün Enerji** - Margün Enerji, which works in solar energy generation and project development, has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye and carries out maintenance and management processes with its own staff. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **CW Enerji** - There are various solar power plants in Türkiye that use CW Enerji brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/cw-enerji-solar-panel/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Jinko Solar** - There are many solar power plants in Türkiye that use Jinko Solar brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/jinko-solar/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in the solar energy sector in Türkiye. ", "aa1e5331-e3b6-4f71-8787-071c46a6dc84": "The largest companies operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye are **Enerjisa Üretim, Borusan EnBW Enerji, Polat Enerji, Eksim Enerji and GÜRİŞ** .[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)According to data from the [Turkish Wind Energy Association (TÜREB)](https://tureb.tr/), Türkiye's installed wind capacity has reached **15,934 MW**. The main wind plant operators leading this large market and their key features are as follows:[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)🏆 Türkiye's Leading Wind Energy Investors\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It is the largest leader in Türkiye's wind energy with a capacity exceeding **1,035 MW** of installed capacity. It operates numerous large-scale WPPs, mainly in Çanakkale and Balıkesir.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Borusan EnBW Enerji:** With approximately **773 MW** of installed wind capacity, it is the second largest player in the sector. Its portfolio includes high-efficiency projects such as Balıkesir WPP and Bandırma WPP.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Polat Enerji:** It has a total of **772 MW** of installed wind capacity. It operates the [Soma WPP](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz) project in Manisa, one of Europe's largest onshore wind farms with a capacity of **328.9 MWm**.[](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz) [[1]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Eksim Enerji:** With its investments in Geyve, Yozgat and Karaman, it has brought its total domestic and international portfolio to **1,186 MW** and its Türkiye wind capacity to **733 MW** , making it one of the giants pushing the 1 GW threshold.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **GÜRİŞ Holding:** [GÜRİŞ](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html) manages **702 MW** of capacity with wind projects concentrated in regions such as Afyonkarahisar (Kocatepe WPP) and Muğla.[](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html) [[1]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n\n\n---\n\n📈 Other Prominent WPP Operators on Borsa İstanbul (BIST) Other popular companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that dedicate serious investment to wind energy in their portfolios are as follows:[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\n- **Galata Wind Enerji (GWIND):** A Doğan Holding affiliate, [Galata Wind](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) is Türkiye's first 100% clean energy and green IPO company. It operates important wind power plants such as Mersin and Şah WPP.[](https://www.doganholding.com.tr/sektorler/elektrik-uretimi/) [[1]](https://www.doganholding.com.tr/sektorler/elektrik-uretimi/)[[2]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It has a large wind portfolio with projects such as Uşak WPP and Yalova WPP. The company is pioneering hybrid plant investments by adding solar panels alongside its wind power plants.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** In addition to hydroelectric and solar, its portfolio includes high-capacity wind power plants in Çanakkale and Denizli.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** It is one of the oldest players in the sector and operates active wind power plants, including pioneering projects such as Gökçedağ WPP in Osmaniye.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://www.bulurum.com/dir/ruzgar-enerji-sirketleri?page=1)\n\n\n---\n\n⚙️ Information Note: Most Preferred Turbine Brands In the turbine technologies that convert wind into electricity at the plants operated by these companies, global brands stand out. The most preferred turbine manufacturers in Türkiye by installed capacity are, in order, **Nordex, Vestas, Enercon, GE (General Electric) and Siemens Gamesa** .[](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyede-en-cok-tercih-edilen-turbin-markalari/) [[1]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyede-en-cok-tercih-edilen-turbin-markalari/)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyede-en-cok-tercih-edilen-turbin-markalari/)Would you like to see the **largest plants by region** for wind investments in Türkiye, or do you need more detailed information about these companies' **wind projects with storage (WPP+Battery)** investments?", "abab9732-2247-4d3a-9313-e969d0374e6f": "Many important companies stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies play a critical role in helping the country reach its sustainable energy targets and invest in different renewable energy sources.\n\nThe companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW. It generates electricity with geothermal, wind and hydroelectric plants. In particular, it is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy generator and aims to meet 20% of geothermal energy.\n2.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji has been traded on Borsa İstanbul since 2010. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion. It has completed licensing processes for wind power plants with storage in locations such as Mersin and Balıkesir.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim (ENJSA)** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa is among Türkiye's largest electricity generators. According to the MW100 survey, it has an installed capacity of 3,607 MWe and focuses on a balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - Founded by Akfen Holding in 2007, it is a company with a 100% renewable energy portfolio. Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW. Its total operating capacity is 887 MW.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - It has the distinction of being the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, wind plants, a geothermal plant and hybrid plants. The total installed capacity of its HPPs is 852.1 MWm.\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - The company, which has two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, has an annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells in total. It aims to reach 2,000 MW of cell production by the end of 2025.\n7.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Founded in 2011, Alfa Solar Enerji operates photovoltaic panel production facilities with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW and plays an important role in developing Türkiye's renewable energy generation capabilities.\n8.  **Galata Wind Enerji A.Ş. (GWIND)** - It builds and operates power generation facilities primarily using wind and solar energy sources. It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out with their wind energy investments.\n9.  **Oltan & Köleoğlu Enerji** - It is Türkiye's highest-capacity biomass energy company and one of Europe's largest biomass energy generators. With a total biomass installed capacity of 100 MWe and annual electricity generation of 690 GWh, it meets the needs of 290,000 households. It also contributes to the circular economy by disposing of more than 1 million tonnes of waste per year. It has commissioned large biomass facilities such as the Afyon Eber Power Plant.\n10. **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - A GÜRİŞ Holding affiliate, the company operates Türkiye's most efficient geothermal power plant with 260 MW in Germencik, Aydın.\n\nThese companies play a pioneering role in efforts to increase Türkiye's renewable energy installed capacity and strengthen its energy independence.", "ac2b9efe-c939-400a-8480-5a533b8bb8a0": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies have been determined according to the data, as of 31 December 2024, of the \"MW100, Türkiye's 100 Largest Electricity Generators Survey\", prepared in cooperation between the international consultancy Kearney and Enerji Günlüğü. While the public entity EÜAŞ tops the list, the companies that stand out in the private sector are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - It is the largest electricity generator in the private sector with an installed capacity of 3,978 megawatts (MWe). It accounts for 3.4 percent of Türkiye's total generation capacity. Although the installed capacity of ENKA's plants is high, generation activity at its natural gas plants is declining due to market conditions.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe and is closing in on ENKA by commissioning new plants. The company is notable for its balanced resource mix.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with an installed capacity of 3,161 MWe, Cengiz Enerji stands out for its balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It rose to fifth place with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. According to Enerji Atlası data, it has 16 plants and an installed capacity of 3,638 MW.\n5.  **Kalyon Enerji** - Kalyon Enerji, which achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024, has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio with its solar power plant (SPP) in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 6 plants and an installed capacity of 1,399 MW.\n6.  **Aydem Enerji** - Its total installed capacity increased by 179 MWe compared with 2023. As Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji AŞ, it has 19 plants and an installed capacity of 1,121 MW.\n7.  **Çalık Enerji** - It generates electricity using various energy sources such as hydroelectric, wind and solar power plants and offers sustainable energy solutions by investing in renewable energy sources.\n8.  **Aksa Enerji** - Founded in 1997, Aksa Enerji is one of Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producers. Its main shareholder is Kazancı Holding. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 2 plants and an installed capacity of 1,170 MW.\n9.  **Eren Enerji** - According to the MW100 2019 report, it was in the top 10 with an installed capacity of 2,824 MWe. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 3 plants and an installed capacity of 2,810 MW.\n10. **Çelikler Holding** - According to the MW100 2019 report, it was in the top 10 with an installed capacity of 2,713 MWe. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 12 plants and an installed capacity of 2,769 MW.\n11. **Bilgin Enerji** - According to the MW100 2019 report, it was in the top 10 with an installed capacity of 1,580 MWe. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 12 plants and an installed capacity of 1,733 MW.\n12. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n13. **Zorlu Enerji** - It has significant investments in renewable energy. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 14 plants and an installed capacity of 612 MW.\n14. **İÇDAŞ** - According to the MW100 2019 report, it was in the top 10 with an installed capacity of 1,665 MWe. According to Enerji Atlası, it has 3 plants and an installed capacity of 1,665 MW.\n\nThese companies make significant contributions to Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity and stand out particularly for their investments in renewable energy sources.", "ae3652f4-e761-4f40-b21f-7194ab60011a": "The major energy companies that build solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye or have significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - It is a notable player in the sector with solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp. The company has also completed turnkey SPP installations abroad with a capacity of 61 MWp and has taken over the operation and maintenance of these facilities.\n2.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji Grubu** - Its portfolio includes solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed). Over the last five years, the company has commissioned modern power plants in many regions of Türkiye.\n3.  **Zorlu Enerji Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - It operates in various energy fields such as electricity generation, trading, distribution, solar panel sales and electric vehicle charging station infrastructure. The company is one of the renewable energy pioneers and obtains all of its electricity generation in Türkiye from renewable sources.\n4.  **Enerjisa Enerji** - It is a large company leading Türkiye's energy transition, operating in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. There are two solar power plants under the Enerjisa Üretim umbrella.\n5.  **Aksa Enerji** - It is Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producer. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion.\n6.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It is a company that directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources and is among Türkiye's leading energy organisations.\n7.  **Galata Wind** - It serves Türkiye by converting the power of solar and wind energy into clean energy. The company has solar power plant investments such as Çorum SPP and Erzurum SPP.\n8.  **CW Enerji** - Founded in 2010, it is a manufacturing and services company operating in the photovoltaic energy generation sector. With an annual solar panel production capacity of 1.8 GW, it is one of the country's leading solar panel manufacturers and carries out turnkey SPP projects.\n9.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri** - Founded in 2014, the company is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. With two production facilities in Türkiye, it has a total annual solar panel production capacity of 2,400 MW.\n10. **YEO Teknoloji** - It provides EPC (Engineering, Procurement, Construction) and project development services for Solar Power Plant projects. The company operates both domestically (unlicensed and licensed SPP facilities with storage) and abroad.\n\nThese companies are making significant investments to meet Türkiye's growing energy needs and reach its renewable energy targets.", "af7ee2e1-aeb8-42e7-b97d-9e98f2f48a96": "The major energy companies that build solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye or have significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim operates solar power plants in Bandırma and Karabük. It is also carrying out hybrid conversions with solar technology at its existing plants. Enerjisa Enerji also develops SPP projects for public and private sector businesses under the \"İşimin Enerjisi\" umbrella, and with projects that reached an installed capacity of 102.4 MWp in 2024, it has the capacity to supply energy to 86 thousand households.\n\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji** - Zorlu Enerji, one of Türkiye's pioneers in renewable energy, implements its solar energy investments through hybrid generation models. It increases generation efficiency by building SPPs integrated with geothermal, hydroelectric and wind plants. It converted the Manisa Alaşehir Geothermal Power Plant into a hybrid plant by building an integrated 3.58 MWp SPP. It also offers solar panels and inverter solutions under the Zes Solar brand.\n\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - The company, part of Akfen Holding, owns many licensed and unlicensed solar power plants across Türkiye. As of 2020, it had an SPP portfolio with an installed capacity of 121.4 MW and has signed agreements for 3 new Hybrid SPP projects of 20 MW in Denizli and Çanakkale.\n\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - Limak Enerji is one of Türkiye's leading energy companies. It has commissioned at full capacity Türkiye's second largest solar power plant (Erzin-1 YEKA SPP) with a total installed capacity of 140 MW in Erzin, Hatay. It also has other solar power plants such as Apa SPP with an installed capacity of 16.3 MWp in Çumra, Konya.\n\n5.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji, Aydem Enerji's company active in renewable energy generation, focuses on renewable energy sources including hybrid solar plants. By commissioning Türkiye's largest hybrid SPP in Uşak, it aims to generate 164 GWh of energy per year.\n\n6.  **Kontrolmatik** - Kontrolmatik, which offers sustainability- and efficiency-focused solutions in the energy sector, provides integrated solutions covering all engineering, procurement, construction (EPC), electrification, automation and commissioning processes of solar power plants. It has also signed cooperation agreements with Smart Güneş Teknolojileri on energy storage systems.\n\n7.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri** - Founded in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. It has production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye and a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n\n8.  **Aksa Enerji** - Aksa Enerji, Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producer, aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion under its 2030 strategy. These targets also include solar energy investments.\n\n9.  **Galata Wind** - Operating within Doğan Holding, Galata Wind contributes to clean energy generation with wind and solar energy projects. It has solar power plant investments such as Çorum SPP and Erzurum SPP.\n\n10. **GAMA Enerji** - Operating in energy and water infrastructure, GAMA Enerji has a broad energy portfolio. Through affiliates or business partners such as \"Gama Solar Elektrik\", it provides solar power plant installation and charging station services.", "b05f23f5-f659-4a6a-b34b-3248ea1f4fd1": "Among Türkiye's largest private electricity generators excluding the public sector,**ENKA**, **Enerjisa Üretim**, **Eren Enerji**, **Cengiz Enerji** and **İÇDAŞ** stand out.[[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[3]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi-28-02-24/)[[4]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[5]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[6]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n\n### Leading Private Electricity Generators\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** It is one of the major generators at the top of the private sector with its natural gas plants.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** Through the partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, it has a large installed capacity and portfolio.\n- **Eren Enerji:** With its thermal power plants in Zonguldak, it has a high share of electricity generation in the private sector.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With its plants using natural gas and other sources, it is among the top 10 largest generators.\n- **İÇDAŞ:** It is one of the major private generators operating in the energy and steel sectors.\n- **EMBA Power and Limak Enerji:** They are other major private energy companies with high installed capacity in the sector.[[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi-28-02-24/)[[3]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[4]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[5]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[6]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)\n\nIf you like, I can provide more details about these companies' **installed capacities (MW)** or **which energy sources (natural gas, coal, renewables)** they use.", "b1cc962b-da12-4bca-858f-dadba1538608": "Among the leading energy companies building and operating large-scale solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, `Kalyon Enerji`, which implemented the country's largest plant, Karapınar SPP, holds the leading position. In addition, major players such as Zorlu Enerji, Enerjisa Enerji, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and CW Enerji include solar investments in their portfolios.[](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/) [[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOoo0Sbd55HAHPKZIsSg3jrecHUpHQDrIvcLqwJzTVoJowjLtCJV9)[[2]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27de_g%C3%BCne%C5%9F_enerjisi)\n\n### Leading Companies and Their Projects\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** It built the country's largest solar plant in Karapınar, Konya, with an installed capacity of 756 MW.\n- **Enerjisa Enerji:** It builds unlicensed and licensed industrial rooftop and ground-mounted SPP projects in various regions.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Its portfolio includes solar plant investments of hundreds of megawatts.\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** It is growing its renewable energy portfolio with solar and wind projects.\n- **CW Enerji:** In addition to large-scale ground-mounted and rooftop SPP installations, it manufactures panels.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27de_g%C3%BCne%C5%9F_enerjisi)[[3]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOoo0Sbd55HAHPKZIsSg3jrecHUpHQDrIvcLqwJzTVoJowjLtCJV9)[[4]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[5]](https://www.facebook.com/cwenerji/videos/t%C3%BCrkiyenin-ve-avrupan%C4%B1n-en-b%C3%BCy%C3%BCk-g%C3%BCne%C5%9F-paneli-%C3%BCreticisi-cw-enerji-sekt%C3%B6rde-en-ye/759288965213232/?locale=ms_MY)\n\nIf you are interested, I can provide more details about these companies' **installed capacities** or **future investment plans**.", "b6dc9d46-cbe1-4837-87ce-fdfd4cb81971": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies invest in different renewable energy sources such as wind, solar, hydroelectric and geothermal in order to meet the country's growing energy needs and contribute to a sustainable future.\n\nHere are some of the leading companies in renewable energy generation in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is one of Türkiye's leading domestic energy companies and generates electricity from solar, wind and geothermal sources. In particular, it is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy generator. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW comes from domestic plants.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is one of Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions companies. In addition to electricity infrastructure investments, the company offers customer solutions such as solar systems and e-mobility. Enerjisa Üretim currently has 12 hydroelectric plants, five wind power plants and two solar power plants.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion under its 2030 strategy. In addition to Türkiye, the company has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji's portfolio includes power plants with total installed capacity. This portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants (WPP) with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji / Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - As the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji holds an important place in renewable energy. Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, and the total installed capacity of these HPPs is 852.1 MWm. It also has wind, geothermal and hybrid plants.\n6.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding (MOGAN)** - Among the new renewable energy companies traded on Borsa İstanbul, Mogan Enerji combines wind, geothermal, hydroelectric and solar sources in its portfolio. The company's total installed capacity is 1,058.01 MW.\n7.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is one of Türkiye's important wind energy companies and stands out with its investments in the renewable energy sector.\n8.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji owns important wind power plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP, Göktepe WPP, Poyraz WPP, Ege WPP and Seyitali WPP. With an installed capacity of 328.9 MWm, Soma WPP is in the top ten among onshore wind plants in Europe. Geycek WPP is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant, combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n9.  **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - Founded in 1999 by GÜRİŞ İNŞAAT VE MÜHENDİSLİK A.Ş., GÜRMAT ENERJİ ÜRETİM A.Ş. operates to build and run the Aydın Germencik geothermal power plant. It is one of the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy.\n10. **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Operating in the solar energy sector, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri stands out in areas such as solar panel production and solar power plant installation.\n11. **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Among the domestic solar panel manufacturers in Türkiye, Alfa Solar Enerji makes significant contributions to the solar energy sector.\n\nThese companies play a critical role in helping Türkiye reach its renewable energy targets and contribute to environmental sustainability.", "b72ccd1c-e905-4ed6-bdf9-6acde43a9861": "There are many private companies generating hydroelectric power in Türkiye. These companies play an important role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are some of the private companies that generate the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye or stand out in this field:\n\n1.  **Cengiz Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's strongest private sector generators in hydroelectric power. It operates six hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 2,265 MW. In particular, the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl, with an installed capacity of 626.85 MW, is the largest hydroelectric plant operated by the private sector. The company also owns the Aşağı Kaleköy Dam and Hybrid Power Plant, Türkiye's first and Europe's largest hybrid power plant.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Focusing on domestic and renewable sources in electricity generation, the company currently owns 12 hydroelectric plants. It states that it will continue its renewable energy investments.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants (HPP) with a total capacity of 228.7 MW. The company stands out for its investments in renewable energy sources.\n4.  **Aydem Enerji** - It has the distinction of being the founder of the country's first private hydroelectric plant. The company operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants.\n5.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It continues its operations with seven hydroelectric plants. The company supports Türkiye in reaching its renewable energy targets.\n6.  **Akenerji** - It began its renewable energy investments in 2005 and has a total installed capacity of 388 MWe with hydroelectric and wind plants. It is stated to have the capacity to meet 3% of Türkiye's energy needs on its own.\n7.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company, which directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources, also has hydroelectric plants.\n8.  **ENKA** - According to the MW100 Survey, it is one of the largest private sector companies in terms of installed capacity. With a total installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it accounts for 3.4 percent of Türkiye's total generation capacity. However, although a large part of this installed capacity comes from natural gas plants, its size in overall energy generation is significant.\n9.  **Limak Enerji** - According to the MW100 survey, it rose to fifth place with 3,033 MWe.\n10. **Bilgin Enerji** - Its installed capacity is stated as 1,580 MWe, and its portfolio also includes hydroelectric plants.\n11. **Özdoğan Enerji** - It is active in the hydroelectric energy sector with projects such as the Ayvalı Dam and HPP in Erzurum (122 MW).\n\nThese companies stand out for their investments in renewable energy sources for Türkiye's security of energy supply and a sustainable future.", "ba1c85dd-3b96-472f-a326-784eb9eb217e": "The main major investors operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye [ [Piagrid](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) ] and their capacity sizes:[[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n\n### 📊 Main WPP Operators\n\n- ###⚡ Enerjisa Üretim\n\t- Installed capacity: ~1,035 MW\n\t- Key projects: A distributed, high-capacity onshore WPP portfolio.[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- ### 🌀 Borusan EnBW Enerji\n\t- Installed capacity: ~773 MW\n\t- Key projects: Wind power plants in the Balıkesir and Bandırma regions.[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- ### 🌬️ Polat Enerji\n\t- Installed capacity: ~772 MW\n\t- Key projects: One of Türkiye's largest, [the 328.9 MW capacity Soma WPP.[[1]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- ### 🏭 Eksim Enerji\n\t- Installed capacity: ~733 MW\n\t- Key projects: Renewable energy investments across Anatolia.[[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- ### ⚙️ GÜRİŞ Holding\n\t- Installed capacity: ~702 MW\n\t- Key projects: Kocatepe WPP, Ulu WPP and Belen WPP.[[1]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- ###💡 [Galata Wind](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) \n\t- Key projects: Şah WPP (Balıkesir) and Mersin WPP (Mut).[[1]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)\n\nIf you like, I can provide more details about these companies' **Borsa İstanbul (BIST) status**, **distribution by geographic region** or **future investment plans**.[[1]](https://sehatek.com.tr/ruzgar-enerjisi-nedir-kullanim-alanlari-nelerdir/)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)", "bb19668d-e1e5-4377-9543-874193a983be": "The main large companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye:[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim / Enerjisa Enerji** : It is among the leaders of the sector with the high renewable energy investments in its portfolio and its strength in electricity generation.[](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.mw100.net/?p=23)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** : With a portfolio focused entirely on renewable sources, it stands out in wind, solar and hydroelectric power.[](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/) [[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** : With its geothermal, wind and solar energy investments, it is one of Türkiye's leading renewable energy players.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n- **Aydem Enerji** : With electricity generation weighted towards renewable sources, it is among the major generators in the sector.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)\n- **Galata Wind Enerji** : It operates wind and solar plants with a 100% renewable energy portfolio.[](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri) [[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://www.gcmyatirim.com.tr/egitim/makaleler/gelecegin-enerji-sektoru-ve-hisseleri-genel-gorunum-ve-yatirim-araclari)\n- **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** : It is active with diversified energy investments and renewable projects.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n\nWhich **renewable energy source** (solar, wind, geothermal, hydroelectric) or **region** would you like to learn more about?", "bc759e94-06c9-4b17-88de-3fa4f7e6ca31": "According to data from the Turkish Wind Energy Association ([TÜREB](https://tureb.tr/) ), the leading investors operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye hold a large part of the wind energy market. **With an installed capacity approaching the 16,000 MW mark**, Türkiye is one of Europe's largest onshore wind markets.[](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/) [[1]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/ruzgar-enerjisi-sektoru-2026ya-26-gwlik-proje-stogu-ile-girdi/)[[3]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)The **main companies with the largest installed capacity** in wind energy generation and plant operation in Türkiye, and their key features, are as follows:\n\n### 1. Enerjisa Üretim\nIt is one of the largest investors in wind energy in Türkiye. With 18 active wind plants located in regions such as Akhisar, Balıkesir, Çanakkale and Erciyes, it operates **over 1,035 MW** of wind capacity. The company is rapidly increasing this capacity through YEKA projects and new phase investments (Uygar WPP, etc.).[](https://www.businesslife.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-ikinci-ruzgar-enerjisi-santrali-olacak) [[1]](https://www.businesslife.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-ikinci-ruzgar-enerjisi-santrali-olacak)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)[[3]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-santrallerimiz/)[[4]](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/enerji-uretimi/ruzgar-santrallerimiz/)\n\n### 2. Borusan EnBW Enerji\nOperating in partnership with Germany's EnBW, Borusan EnBW is one of the top partners in wind plant capacity. With **around 773 MW** of installed wind capacity, it operates huge plants in provinces with high wind potential such as Balıkesir, Çanakkale and İzmir.[](https://icci.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-10-bin-megavati-asti/) [[1]](https://icci.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-10-bin-megavati-asti/)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)\n\n### 3. Polat Enerji\nIt is one of Türkiye's most established companies in renewable energy. With **771 MW of installed capacity**, the company manages **Soma WPP** (328.9 MWm) in Manisa, which has long been one of Türkiye's largest wind power plants, as well as large projects such as Geycek and Göktepe.[](https://polatenerji.com/santrallerimiz) [[1]](https://polatenerji.com/santrallerimiz)[[2]](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz)[[3]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)\n\n### 4. Eksim Enerji\nWith one of the largest wind portfolios outside the stock exchange, Eksim Enerji is among Türkiye's top 5 wind energy investors with approximately **732 MW of installed capacity**. In addition to wind, the company also focuses on WPP investments with storage.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)\n\n### 5. GÜRİŞ Holding (Mogan Enerji)\nOne of the pioneering players in renewable energy, GÜRİŞ is near the top of the list with **702 MW of wind capacity**. It makes a major contribution to clean energy generation with the Albay Çiğiltepe WPP in Afyonkarahisar and wind plants in regions such as Kocaeli/Hatay.[](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/) [[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[2]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyenin-ruzgar-enerjisi-kurulu-gucu-16-gwa-dayandi/)[[3]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)\n---\n\n### Other Important WPP Companies Traded on Borsa İstanbul (BIST)\nOther important players among publicly listed companies that generate electricity from wind and are growing their portfolios with wind-hybrid projects are as follows:\n\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It has brought its wind-focused clean energy portfolio, including wind and hybrid SPPs, to over 530 MW.\n- **Galata Wind (GWID):** A Doğan Holding affiliate, the company obtains all of its approximately 354 MW of installed capacity from wind and solar and stands out with its wind power plants.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji (AYDEM):** It has increased the share of wind energy in its total installed capacity to over 268 MW.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\n*(Note: The supply of turbines used during plant construction is handled by global giants such as **Nordex**, **Enercon**, **Vestas** and **Siemens Gamesa** as market leaders.)* [](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[2]](https://yesilekonomi.com/ruzgar-enerjisi-sektoru-2026ya-26-gwlik-proje-stogu-ile-girdi/)Would you like to learn the **active plant locations** of a specific one of these companies, or would you like to examine the details of Türkiye's **largest wind power plants**?", "bc960172-d521-4a67-be12-5b7736571ecd": "The main public and private sector companies that stand out in renewable energy generation and investment in Türkiye are as follows:[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\n- **EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.):** As a large public entity, it leads in total installed capacity and generation with its giant hydroelectric plants (HPP).[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its broad renewable energy portfolio (wind, solar, hydroelectric), it is among the largest electricity generators in the private sector.[[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It is one of the pioneering companies whose entire portfolio consists of one hundred percent renewable sources such as hydro, solar and wind.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** It stands out with its investments, especially in geothermal energy, as well as in wind and solar.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Galata Wind Enerji:** It is one of the important publicly listed green energy generators, focusing entirely on wind and solar energy projects.[[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n- **Aydem Enerji:** With its generation portfolio based on renewable sources, it is among the long-established players in the sector.[[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)\n- **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG) and Alfa Solar Enerji:** They are technology and energy companies that stand out in solar panel production and solar power plant (SPP) investments.[[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n\nWould you like more detailed information about renewable energy companies' **share performance**, **installed capacity breakdown** or **a specific energy type (solar, wind, etc.)**?", "c0ce3ccf-0be8-4f31-807f-7b08b96deea6": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**  \n   With six hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 2,265 MW, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric generator. Its prominent facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP with an installed capacity of 626.85 MW and the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP with a capacity of 582.1 MW. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Energo-Pro Türkiye**  \n   Founded in Ankara in 2010, Energo-Pro operates in Türkiye with eight hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW. These plants are located in the provinces of Sivas, Tokat, Ankara and Artvin. ([energo-pro.com.tr](https://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Merge Enerji**  \n   Developing hydroelectric, wind and solar energy projects since 2005, Merge Enerji operates the Duru-1 (5.29 MWe) and Duru-2 (5.40 MWe) hydroelectric plants in Amasya. ([mergeenerji.com.tr](https://www.mergeenerji.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   Contributing to Türkiye's transition to a low-carbon economy with its hydroelectric, wind and geothermal energy investments, Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji has a total installed capacity of 526.2 MWe with 15 active power plants. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Tektuğ Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**  \n   Active in renewable energy generation since 2000, Tektuğ holds an important position in the sector with its projects with a total installed capacity of 150 MW. ([tektug.com](https://www.tektug.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and continue their investments aimed at increasing the use of renewable energy sources. ", "c12f8f29-fbe1-438d-a9b1-042ddaeb309d": "Among Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies excluding the public sector, **ENKA**, **Eren Enerji** and **Enerjisa Üretim** stand out.[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[3]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)Leading Private Electricity Generators\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** It is one of the companies at the top of the private sector in installed capacity and total electricity generation.\n- **Eren Enerji:** It is one of the major generators with the highest share in the private sector by generation volume.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** Through the partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, it is among the country's largest private players.\n- **Other Major Generators:** İÇDAŞ, Cengiz Enerji, EMBA Power, Limak Enerji, Çelikler Holding, Zorlu Enerji and Aydem Enerji are also among the private groups that generate the most electricity.[](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[3]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi/)[[4]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[5]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n\nIf you like, I can also tell you about:\n\n- These companies' **generation types** (natural gas, coal, renewables)\n- Which plants they own\n\nHow would you like to proceed?", "c149397a-6f39-41b6-a6a8-4535dc4db074": "The leading private companies that generate the most hydroelectric power (HPP) in Türkiye and have large dams/plants in their portfolios are **Enerjisa Üretim**, **Cengiz Enerji**, **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** and **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** .[](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913) [[1]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[2]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)Leading Private HPP Generators\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its broad renewable and hydro portfolio across Türkiye, it is among the largest electricity and hydroelectric generators in the private sector.[](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** It stands out with huge dam and HPP projects such as **Lalahisar** in Bingöl or **Lower Kaleköy (Altınkale)** in Bingöl, one of the largest in the private sector; some of the largest HPPs operated by the private sector belong to this group.[](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji) [[1]](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Focusing entirely on renewable sources, the company is one of the pioneers of Türkiye's first private sector HPP investments and has a high HPP installed capacity.[](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr) [[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is one of the important renewable energy players operating many hydroelectric plants in different regions of the country.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27deki_hidroelektrik_santralleri)\n- **Energo-Pro Türkiye:** By housing numerous HPPs with high installed capacity, it provides a significant volume of hydroelectric generation.[](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html) [[1]](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html)\n\nWould you like more details about the **installed capacities** or **locations** of the hydroelectric plants?", "c1981d21-21b8-4c71-881c-800e1a3155a2": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Eksim Enerji** - It is one of the few private sector WPP generators in Türkiye to exceed the 1 GW threshold. With investments such as Yozgat WPP, Geyve WPP, Skole WPP and Karaman WPP, it has brought its total installed capacity to approximately 1,186.5 MW. It is also stated to generate 1.2 million MWh of electricity per year with 428 MW of active installed capacity.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - With 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity, it is one of Türkiye's leading wind generation companies.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It generates electricity with 1,252.9 MW of installed capacity at a total of 18 wind plants in many locations such as Akhisar, Akköy, Armutçuk, Balıkesir, Çanakkale, Çeşme and Dağpazarı. The company is the market leader in private sector electricity generation.\n4.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios. It owns important plants such as Soma WPP (in the top ten among onshore wind plants in Europe with 328.9 MWm of installed capacity), Geycek WPP (Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant), Göktepe WPP, Poyraz WPP, Ege WPP and Seyitali WPP.\n5.  **Galata Wind** - It is among the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out with their wind energy investments.\n6.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the companies on Borsa İstanbul notable for its wind energy investments.\n7.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates three wind plants in different regions of Türkiye and continues to invest in renewable energy sources.\n8.  **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - It is one of the companies operating in the wind energy sector on Borsa İstanbul.\n9.  **Ayen Enerji** - With its wind power plant portfolio, it is among Borsa İstanbul energy shares.\n10. **Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It has delivered important projects such as the Bandırma Wind Power Plant (BARES). BARES has been an investment that significantly increased Türkiye's wind capacity.\n11. **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates many wind power plants such as Düzova WPP, Ziyaret WPP, Salman WPP, Karadere WPP, Şadıllı WPP, Ortamandıra WPP, Karova WPP, Kızılcaterzi WPP and Tayakadın WPP.\n12. **GÜRİŞ** - It has been involved in projects such as the Kocatepe Wind Power Plant (100 MW), Zeliha WPP (25 MW) and Kanije WPP (64 MW).", "c1deef24-9d09-4359-89ed-13b89a58d648": "Some of the major energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments are as follows:\n\n1. **OYAK Çimento** - By commissioning a solar power plant with an installed capacity of 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp in Beypazarı, Ankara, it delivered the largest renewable energy project implemented by an industrial producer in Türkiye at a single location. ([solargundem.com](https://www.solargundem.com/oyak-cimento-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oz-tuketim-amacli-gunes-enerjisi-santralini-devreye-aldi-3419461?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company stands out with its plans to build two giant solar power plants with a total capacity of 5,000 MW in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Enerjisa Enerji** - By installing a solar power plant with an installed capacity of 4.1 MW on the roof of the Ali Sami Yen Sports Complex Türk Telekom Arena Stadium, it enabled the stadium to generate its own energy. ([stendustri.com.tr](https://www.stendustri.com.tr/ali-sami-yen-spor-kompleksine-gunes-santrali-kurulacak?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Polat Enerji A.Ş.** - By building a wind power plant with an installed capacity of 140.4 MW in Soma, Manisa, it operates one of Türkiye's largest wind power plants. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soma_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Jinko Solar** - It has gained an important place in the sector with Jinko Solar panels used in various solar power plants in Türkiye. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/jinko-solar/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **CW Enerji** - It operates in the sector with on-grid solar power plants built in Türkiye with CW Enerji brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/cw-enerji-solar-panel/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Hanwha Solar** - It is known for various solar power plants built in Türkiye with Hanwha Solar brand solar panels. ([enerjiatlasi.com](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/gunes-paneli/hanwha-solar/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in the solar energy sector in Türkiye. ", "c517dcb9-6d1e-4817-b3b6-d35f0ce708bc": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **RT Enerji**  \n   It operates in the development, installation and operation of power plant projects based 100% on renewable energy sources. The company's current capacity is 377.4 MWe, and its 2027 target is 1,351.1 MWe. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Eolos Rüzgar Enerjisi Üretim A.Ş.**  \n   Founded in 2010, the company operates the Şenköy Wind Power Plant located within the borders of Hatay province. The plant has a total installed capacity of 36 MW, and annual electricity generation of 110 million kWh is targeted. ([santralmadencilik.com](https://www.santralmadencilik.com/eolos-ruzgar.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Çalık Enerji**  \n   Active in the energy sector since 1998, the company operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant in the Urla district of İzmir province. The plant has an installed capacity of 40 MW and generates 155 GWh of electricity per year. ([demirciliruzgar.com](https://www.demirciliruzgar.com/index.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   The company has 7 wind power plants with an installed capacity of 451.1 MW. One of its prominent plants is the Sarıtepe Wind Power Plant in Osmaniye province, with an installed capacity of 57 MWm/50 MWe. ([akfenren.com.tr](https://www.akfenren.com.tr/varliklarimiz/res/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Polat Enerji**  \n   With one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios, the company operates the Soma Wind Power Plant with an installed capacity of 328.9 MWm. This plant is in the top ten among onshore wind plants in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Demirer Holding**  \n   The Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant, built in the Şarköy district of Tekirdağ province, has an installed capacity of 30.5 MW and generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. This generation meets the electricity consumption of 40,000 homes. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Medyol Enerji**  \n   Specialising in the renewable energy sector, the company operates the Çerkeş Wind Power Plant. This plant has a total installed capacity of 50 MW with 12 ENERCON E-138 EP3 E2 4.2 MW turbines. ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://medyolenerji.com.tr/projelerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Boydak Enerji**  \n   The company, which operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant, uses 19 Nordex N100/2500 model turbines at this plant located within the borders of İstanbul province. The total installed capacity is 47.5 MW, and annual electricity generation of 151 GWh is targeted. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold an important place in Türkiye's wind energy sector and contribute to renewable energy generation. ", "c5aa0e4c-0398-49b3-ad0b-fb0d58acf7cb": "Among the largest energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, `Kalyon Enerji, Enerjisa Enerji, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and Zorlu Enerji` stand out.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4WK0MjnaoBVrqoiNvRKAnelEyX5yRTC82_aEvnXwKHq3v_2raVi)\n\n### Leading Major Energy Companies\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** In Karapınar, Konya, it built **Karapınar SPP** (756 MW installed capacity), Türkiye's largest and one of the world's few largest solar plants.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4WK0MjnaoBVrqoiNvRKAnelEyX5yRTC82_aEvnXwKHq3v_2raVi)[[2]](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrkiye%27de_g%C3%BCne%C5%9F_enerjisi)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA):** It is one of the country's largest electricity generators and distribution companies, building licensed and unlicensed solar power plants in different regions as part of its renewable energy investments.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://dnzyapienerji.com.tr/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-ureticileri/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It is a major generator whose portfolio includes significant solar energy (SPP) investments in addition to wind and hydroelectric plants.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** It is one of the long-established energy groups growing its portfolio with solar energy projects alongside various renewable energy sources.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Engineering/Energy Giants such as Girişim Elektrik (GESAN) & Kontrolmatik:** In addition to plant investment, they are among the main technology and engineering firms undertaking turnkey installation (EPC) of large-scale SPP projects across Türkiye.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/yatirim/enerji-sektorunde-karliligi-en-yuksek-hisseler)\n\nIf you like:\n\n- A specific **company's total SPP capacity** \n- Or **large plant projects by city** \n\nwe can examine in more detail.", "c7411e6d-fc91-4827-a333-d3f21eb65465": "The leading private sector companies in hydroelectric power generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Cengiz Enerji**  \n   With six hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 2,265 MW, it is Türkiye's largest private sector hydroelectric generator. Its prominent facilities include the Yukarı Kaleköy Dam and HPP in Bingöl with an installed capacity of 626.85 MW and the Beyhan-1 Dam and HPP in Elazığ with an installed capacity of 582.1 MW. ([cengizenerji.com.tr](https://www.cengizenerji.com.tr/hidroelektrik-enerji?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ENKA**  \n   As Türkiye's second largest electricity generator with an installed capacity of 3,978 MW, ENKA has significant generation capacity with its hydroelectric plants. ([haber.doviz.com](https://haber.doviz.com/gundem-haberleri/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belli-oldu/762969?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Enerjisa Üretim**  \n   Operating as a partnership of the German energy giant E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim is Türkiye's third largest electricity generator with a capacity of 3,901 MW. ([haber.doviz.com](https://haber.doviz.com/gundem-haberleri/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belli-oldu/762969?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Türker Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   It operates in hydroelectric, wind and geothermal energy with 15 active power plants with an installed capacity of 526.2 MWe. The company focuses on environmentally friendly and sustainable energy generation. ([turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com](https://turkeryenilenebilirenerji.com/en/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Kurtsuyu Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.**  \n   The company, which operates the Daran Hydroelectric Power Plant with an installed capacity of 68.74 MW, generates an average of 278 million kWh of energy per year. The plant is located on the Ermenek Stream in the Sarıveliler district of Karaman province. ([kurtsuyu.com.tr](https://www.kurtsuyu.com.tr/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Asmaz Enerji İletişim İnşaat**  \n   Operating in hydroelectric power generation, Asmaz Enerji provides engineering, construction and operation services for run-of-river and dam-type HPP projects. ([asmaz.com.tr](https://www.asmaz.com.tr/enerji/hidro-enerji/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Energo-Pro**  \n   Serving with hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of approximately 100 MW in Sivas, Tokat, Ankara and Artvin, Energo-Pro aims to meet the electricity needs of 610 thousand households by the end of 2020. ([turkiyegazetesi.com.tr](https://www.turkiyegazetesi.com.tr/ekonomi/energo-pro-610-bin-haneyi-aydinlatacak-610351?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Berkman Dam and HPP**  \n   Located on the Ceyhan River in Osmaniye province, the Berkman Dam and HPP generates an average of 160 million kWh of energy per year with an installed capacity of 39 MW. The plant is operated by the Enova Enerji Company. ([ozaltin.com](https://www.ozaltin.com/tr/tum-projeler/baraj-ve-hes-projeleri/berkman-dam-and-hepp/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's hydroelectric power generation and contribute to increasing the use of renewable energy sources. ", "c84a0e2d-c5a5-4d2c-98be-34fc3136ffcd": "The major energy companies that build solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye or carry out significant activities in this field are as follows:\n\n1.  **Kalyon Enerji** - It is the investor and operator of the Karapınar Solar Power Plant with an installed capacity of 1,350 MWp, the largest in Türkiye and Europe and one of the few largest solar plants in the world. The company offers turnkey solutions in solar energy projects and also manufactures solar panels in-house.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, and its total installed capacity also includes solar power plants. The company provides engineering, procurement, construction, operation and maintenance services.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes various renewable energy plants, including solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed). The company operates in energy generation.\n4.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - Since 2014, it has provided project development, turnkey installation (EPC) and Operation and Maintenance services in renewable energy and climate technologies. With solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp, it is one of the sector's important players. It also carries out SPP installations abroad.\n5.  **Enerjisa Enerji** - Operating in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions, the company has adopted a sustainability approach and is also active in customer solutions business lines such as solar systems.\n6.  **Aksa Enerji** - It is one of Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producers. Under its 2030 strategy, it aims to increase its installed capacity by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion, has completed licensing processes for wind power plants with storage and is making hybrid energy investments.\n7.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - It is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. It has production facilities in Türkiye and offers solar panel production and solar power plant solutions.\n8.  **YEO Teknoloji** - It provides EPC (Engineering, Procurement and Construction) services and project development activities for Solar Power Plant (SPP) projects. It plays an active role in licensed and unlicensed SPP projects both domestically and abroad.\n9.  **Entegro Enerji Sistemleri** - It was founded in 2013 through the merger of experienced engineering firms from Germany and Türkiye. Specialising in ground-mounted SPP, industrial-commercial rooftop SPP and solar car park projects, it offers turnkey solutions.\n10. **Alfa Solar Enerji** - Founded in 2011, it produces high-efficiency solar panels with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW in Kırıkkale. It holds an important place in the sector by serving Türkiye's leading solar energy generators.\n11. **Masfen Enerji** - It is a company providing turnkey services in rooftop SPP and ground-mounted SPP projects. It has reached a total installed capacity of 460 MW in licensed and unlicensed solar energy projects in Türkiye and Europe.\n12. **Liva Enerji** - In the solar electricity generation sector, it has delivered important projects in turnkey Solar Power Plant (SPP) installation for rooftop and ground-mounted applications.", "ca384b7d-783d-4e82-aa28-dd87d7a5a593": "Among the largest energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye are the main players that stand out with giant projects.Major Large Energy Companies\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji (Kalyon Holding):** It is the founder and operator of **Karapınar YEKA-1 SPP** in Karapınar, Konya, the largest single-site solar plant in Türkiye and Europe. The plant has an installed capacity of approximately 1,350 MWp.[](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/) [[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOoqqs7ChYe3toaD-j0qrjWYCA-vZGPmCzQo23YwH3s9KwOa7QBMo)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/)[[3]](https://ceyrekmuhendis.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-santralleri/)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA):** As one of Türkiye's largest electricity generation and distribution companies, it focuses on SPP investments and turnkey projects in its renewable energy portfolio.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://dnzyapienerji.com.tr/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-ureticileri/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** In addition to hydroelectric and wind, its portfolio includes a considerable capacity of solar power plants commissioned in different regions of Türkiye.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** In addition to geothermal and wind, it is among the major energy players that also invest in solar energy projects as part of their renewable energy investments.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG) & CW Enerji:** They are among Türkiye's leading industrial and energy firms both in large-scale SPP installations and in solar panel production.[](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/) [[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)[[2]](https://www.facebook.com/cwenerji/videos/t%C3%BCrkiyenin-ve-avrupan%C4%B1n-en-b%C3%BCy%C3%BCk-g%C3%BCne%C5%9F-paneli-%C3%BCreticisi-cw-enerji-sekt%C3%B6rde-en-ye/759288965213232/?locale=ms_MY)\n- **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS):** With its solar panel production and the equipment/installation support it provides to solar plant projects, it is one of the largest publicly listed players in the sector.[](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/) [[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n\nWould you like to learn more about a specific **region** or **investment scale** (for example, large licensed plants or rooftop SPP projects)?", "d19003e3-8ff5-4b5f-a8cd-f51ff034623d": "Among the major energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, `Kalyon Enerji, Enerjisa Enerji, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and Zorlu Enerji` stand out.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4UK181B66a7nXgqpSOzhUSNsexdpMp-AkuvkzdO3nJJ-oWpF8wC)\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** With **Karapınar SPP**, which it built in Karapınar, Konya, with an installed capacity of 1,350 MWp, it has implemented one of the largest solar plants in Türkiye and Europe.[[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AU7gw4UK181B66a7nXgqpSOzhUSNsexdpMp-AkuvkzdO3nJJ-oWpF8wC)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/?hl=tr)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji:** As part of its renewable energy investments, it runs licensed and unlicensed solar power plant projects in different regions and offers its customers self-consumption-focused SPP solutions.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** In addition to hydroelectric and wind, its portfolio includes solar power plants (SPP) that it has commissioned at different locations across Türkiye.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** It is one of the major players diversifying its renewable energy portfolio by investing in solar energy projects and carrying out turnkey SPP installations.[[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri and Alfa Solar Enerji:** They are other important companies that stand out in the sector both in panel production and in the investment and installation process of large-scale SPP projects.[[1]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)[[2]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n\nIs there any other detail you would like to learn about solar energy investments? For example:\n\n- **Large licensed projects** or **rooftop (self-consumption) SPP** systems\n- A specific company's **installed capacities**", "d312d323-9aa1-442a-98ec-37bd96218f47": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies invest in various renewable energy sources such as wind, solar, hydroelectric and geothermal in order to meet the country's growing energy needs and contribute to a sustainable future. Here are the main companies operating in this field in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's leading domestic energy companies, Zorlu Enerji generates power from solar, wind and geothermal sources. It is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy generator and owns 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in the country.\n\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions company. Hydroelectric and wind plants hold an important place in its generation portfolio. Enerjisa Üretim currently has 12 hydroelectric plants, five wind power plants and two solar power plants.\n\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji is one of Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producers. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by increasing its renewable energy investments. In addition to Türkiye, it has renewable and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - The portfolio of Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji Group includes a total of 12 hydroelectric plants with a capacity of 228.7 MW, solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW and wind power plants with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - As the founder of the country's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji is an important player in renewable energy. The company's hydroelectric plants include facilities such as Bereket I and II HPP, Aksu HPP, Koyulhisar HPP and Akıncı HPP.\n\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Standing out in the solar energy sector, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri has an annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells in total with two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa. The company aims to reach 2,000 MW of cell production by the end of 2025.\n\n7.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - It is one of Türkiye's important domestic solar panel manufacturers.\n\n8.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - Operating in wind energy generation, Galata Wind operates wind plants in various regions of Türkiye.\n\n9.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy. It owns large wind power plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP, Göktepe WPP and Poyraz WPP. In particular, Soma WPP, with an installed capacity of 328.9 MWm, is in the top ten among onshore wind plants in Europe.\n\n10. **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - Founded by GÜRİŞ İNŞAAT VE MÜHENDİSLİK A.Ş., GÜRMAT ENERJİ ÜRETİM A.Ş. builds and operates the Aydın Germencik geothermal power plant. It is one of the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy.\n\n11. **Enda Enerji Holding A.Ş.** - It undertakes initiatives in sustainable and clean energy generation with solar (SPP), wind (WPP), geothermal (GPP) and hydroelectric power plants (HPP). It has affiliates such as Tuzla Jeotermal Enerji A.Ş.\n\nThese companies play a critical role in helping Türkiye reach its renewable energy targets and make significant contributions to the growth of the sector.", "d37a4ef7-e91c-4d43-83a7-8e8f0b808c81": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye include both energy investors and wind turbine manufacturers. According to TÜREB data, Türkiye's largest wind investors as of January 2026 are as follows:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - With a capacity of 1,035 MW, it is one of Türkiye's largest wind energy investors. The company currently has five wind power plants.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of 773 MW and is among the important wind energy investors in Türkiye.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios. It houses large plants such as Soma WPP (328.9 MWm), Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe) and Göktepe WPP (121.1 MWe). Geycek WPP is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant, combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - With investments such as Yozgat WPP, Geyve WPP, Skole WPP and Karaman WPP, it has brought its total installed capacity to approximately 1,186.5 MW. Eksim Enerji is one of the few private sector WPP generators in Türkiye to exceed the 1 GW threshold.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It has an installed capacity of 702 MW and has projects such as Kocatepe WPP (100 MW), Fatma WPP (80 MW), Zeliha WPP (25 MW) and Kanije WPP (64 MW).\n6.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes wind power plants with a capacity of 348.9 MW.\n7.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It operates in various fields such as electricity generation, trading and distribution. The company's wind power plants also hold an important place in its portfolio. It has investments such as Gökçedağ WPP.\n8.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is one of the companies that stand out with direct wind power plant (WPP) investments.\n9.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is among the companies known for their wind power plant investments and traded on Borsa İstanbul. It has plants in the Bandırma area of Balıkesir.\n10. **Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It has carried out large wind energy investments such as the Bandırma Wind Power Plant (BARES). BARES stands out with an installed capacity of 50 MW.\n\nThere are also international companies that supply wind turbines in Türkiye and hold an important place in the sector:\n\n*   **Nordex** - It is the brand with the highest installations in Türkiye in 2025 (1,120 MW) and stands out in the total installed base.\n*   **Vestas** - It is one of the global leaders of the wind sector worldwide, and its turbines are used at many licensed WPPs in Türkiye.\n*   **Enercon** - It is the brand with the second most installations in Türkiye in 2025 (835 MW) and is known for its gearless turbine technology.\n*   **GE Vernova (General Electric)** - It takes part in large WPP projects and cooperates with local tower and blade production in Türkiye.\n*   **Siemens Gamesa** - It is one of the global leaders of wind energy worldwide and is actively involved in both onshore and large-scale projects in Türkiye.\n*   **Goldwind** - The China-based company supplies turbines to large-scale onshore WPP projects in the Turkish market.", "d4255e4e-43ee-45b0-a71d-0db3db17532f": "Türkiye's largest public electricity generator is `Elektrik Üretim AŞ (EÜAŞ)`, and excluding the public sector, the **largest electricity generation companies in the private sector** lead the way:[[1]](https://www.aksiyon.com.tr/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-liderligini-surdurdu-112131/amp)[[2]](https://safranbolubirlik.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/)\n\n- **ENKA** (One of the largest electricity generators in the private sector)\n- **Enerjisa Üretim** (A partnership of Sabancı Holding and Germany's E.ON)\n- **Eren Enerji** \n- **Çelikler Holding** \n- **Cengiz Enerji** \n- **Limak Enerji** \n- **Aydem Enerji** \n- **İÇDAŞ** \n- **Bilgin Enerji** \n- **Zorlu Enerji** \n- **Aksa Enerji** [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.aksiyon.com.tr/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-liderligini-surdurdu-112131/amp)[[3]](https://safranbolubirlik.com/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/)[[4]](https://www.hakimiyet.com/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/73596/)[[5]](https://ekonomiknokta.com/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-h342.htm)\n\n*Note: According to the results of the **MW100** survey prepared in cooperation between Kearney and [Enerji Günlüğü](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/iste-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-36547h.htm), the rankings are updated based on the companies' installed capacities and annual generation performance.* [[1]](https://haberekonomi.com.tr/index.asp?sayfa=haber&icerik=24054)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/iste-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-36547h.htm)Would you like to examine the largest private companies by a specific **energy type** (for example, natural gas, coal, solar or wind)?", "d4f89f78-c854-4184-9fba-e23a09a036a9": "There are many important companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye. These companies play a critical role in helping the country reach its renewable energy targets. Here are the main companies and some of their features:\n\n1.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - A joint venture of Borusan and the German energy company Energie Baden-Württemberg, Borusan EnBW Enerji is one of the companies with the most wind energy capacity in Türkiye.\n2.  **Polat Enerji** - Founded with a focus on sustainability, it is one of Türkiye's leading energy companies. It owns plants such as Seyitali WPP (41.5 MWm installed capacity), operating in İzmir since 2007, and Poyraz WPP (85.5 MWe installed capacity), established in 2012.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of the important players in Türkiye's renewable energy sector. They compete by expanding their project portfolios and forming technology alliances.\n4.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It drew attention with the expansion of its wind plant in Mersin and reached a capacity of approximately 95.85 MWe. The company ranks near the top among renewable energy companies in Türkiye in terms of asset size.\n5.  **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji (Fiba Renewables)** - As a Fiba Group affiliate, it was founded in 2007 to develop renewable energy projects and build generation facilities. It operates many wind power plants such as Düzova WPP (İzmir), Ziyaret WPP (Hatay) and Salman WPP (İzmir).\n6.  **GÜRİŞ** - It is an important player in the wind energy sector, taking part in large projects such as the Kocatepe Wind Power Plant (100 MW). It has also undertaken the construction and assembly work of plants such as Zeliha WPP (25 MW), Fatma WPP (80 MW) and Kanije WPP (64 MW).\n7.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is among the companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye.\n8.  **İÇ İçtaş Energy Investment Holding** - It is cited among Türkiye's leading renewable energy companies.\n9.  **Kalyon Enerji** - It is an important company expanding its project portfolio and forming technology alliances in the renewable energy sector.\n10. **Sanko Enerji Grubu** - It ranks near the top among renewable energy companies in Türkiye.\n11. **Bilgin Enerji Yatırım Holding** - It has carried out large wind energy investments such as the Bandırma Wind Power Plant (BARES). BARES has a capacity of 50 Megawatts and generates an average of 120,000 MWh of electricity per year.\n12. **Zorlu Enerji** - It is part of Zorlu Holding, to which Rotor A.Ş., the operator of the Gökçedağ Wind Plant, is affiliated. With an installed capacity of 135 MW, the Gökçedağ Wind Plant is one of the country's large wind plants.\n13. **Cengiz Enerji** - By increasing capacity at the Çerkeş Wind Power Plant, it reached 82.6 MW and began using Türkiye's largest turbine blades.\n14. **Mogan Enerji** - In terms of total assets, it is one of Türkiye's largest renewable energy companies.", "d76368cc-d5f7-4c53-b230-635ee0fb816a": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)**  \n   It is one of the companies with the largest renewable energy investments in Türkiye. It has a broad portfolio in solar, wind and geothermal. In particular, it is one of Türkiye's largest players in geothermal energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)**  \n   Operating in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions, Enerjisa Enerji contributes to renewable energy generation with its wind and hydroelectric plants. By investing in sustainable energy projects, it aims to reduce its carbon footprint. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aydem Enerji (AYDEM)**  \n   With more than 40 years of experience, Aydem Enerji holds an important position in renewable energy generation with its hydroelectric, wind and geothermal power plants. As of 2025, the company reported its total installed capacity as 1,198 MWm. ([yesilhaber.net](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbul-hidroelektrik-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)**  \n   It contributes to Türkiye's energy generation with solar, wind and hydroelectric power plants. The company is known for its environmentally friendly energy projects and continues to meet Türkiye's energy needs by increasing energy efficiency. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Borusan EnBW Enerji (BESEN)**  \n   It is an important player in Türkiye's renewable energy sector and stands out particularly with its wind energy projects. The company owns Türkiye's largest wind power plants and is continuously increasing its renewable energy investments. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)**  \n   With a broad portfolio in energy generation and trading, Aksa Enerji focuses on renewable energy generation with wind and hydroelectric plants. The company strengthens its position in the sector by offering innovative solutions in energy generation. ([valu.com.tr](https://valu.com.tr/blog/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-2025?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Say Yenilenebilir Enerji Ekipmanları A.Ş. (SAYAS)**  \n   Designing and manufacturing equipment such as wind turbine tower internal/external components, blade, generator and rotor transport fixtures, SAYAS is one of the first companies in Türkiye to offer integrated solutions in equipment supply for renewable energy plants. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)**  \n   Founded in İstanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. The company, which has two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells. ([piapiri.com](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Kalyon Enerji**  \n   Operating in solar energy, Kalyon Enerji owns one of Türkiye's largest solar energy projects with the 1,000 MW Karapınar Solar Power Plant. It is also increasing its effectiveness in the sector with local panel production and storage projects. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **Polat Enerji**  \n    Operating with wind and solar energy projects, Polat Enerji has over 500 MW of wind energy capacity. The company is increasing its renewable energy investments through technology partnerships. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies are making significant investments in Türkiye's renewable energy sector and increasing the share of sustainable and environmentally friendly sources in the country's energy generation. ", "dbbf8240-6281-4408-b908-70763ed35831": "Türkiye's largest private sector electricity generators by installed capacity and generation capacity are [ENKA](https://www.enka.com/), [Enerjisa Üretim](https://www.enerjisauretim.com.tr/) , Eren Enerji and Cengiz Enerji .[[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/)\n\n### Largest Private Electricity Generators (Installed Capacity Ranking)\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** With approximately 3,978 MWe of installed capacity, it ranks near the top of the private sector.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It has approximately 3,901 MWe of installed capacity and is also at the top in total generation volume.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With approximately 3,161 MWe of installed capacity, it is one of the country's major generators.\n- **Limak Enerji:** It has an installed capacity of approximately 3,033 MWe.\n- **Eren Enerji:** It is among the largest players in the private sector in installed capacity and actual annual electricity generation.\n- **Other major generators:** İÇDAŞ, EMBA Power, Çelikler Holding and Aksa Enerji.[[1]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi-28-02-24/)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/)[[3]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[4]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313)[[5]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[6]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[7]](https://www.piapiri.com/blog/yatirim-rehberi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-hangileri/)\n\nIf you like, I can detail **which energy sources** (natural gas, coal, renewables) these companies use or their **generation shares**.", "dc06e065-c481-4e2e-89ee-e192f0281cdb": "The main large companies that stand out in renewable energy generation and investment in Türkiye are as follows:Prominent Companies\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With a large part of its portfolio made up of domestic and renewable sources, it is among the country's largest generators in wind, solar and hydroelectric power.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[3]](https://www.mw100.net/?p=23)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** In addition to geothermal, wind and hydroelectric plants, it also stands out with solar panels and electric vehicle charging station infrastructure.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/enerji-hisseleri-2025/?srsltid=AfmBOopxljGbGZsJBuJKqAmd8Jg0rptF0IEK_HGOIaOB2Xosj6B0xU-4)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** It is one of the focused companies that build and operate only renewable energy (hydroelectric, wind and solar) plants.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji (AYDEM):** With roots as the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, it has a 100% renewable energy portfolio.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Galata Wind Enerji (GWIND):** It is an organisation focused on wind and solar energy sources that carries out fully environmentally conscious electricity generation.[](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri) [[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://www.gcmyatirim.com.tr/egitim/makaleler/gelecegin-enerji-sektoru-ve-hisseleri-genel-gorunum-ve-yatirim-araclari)\n- **Esenboğa Elektrik (ESEN):** It is growing in the renewable energy sector, particularly with solar power plant (SPP) investments.[](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri) [[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n\nWould you like more information about renewable energy companies' **share performance**, **generation areas (wind/solar/geothermal)** or **installed capacity details**?", "e14c8770-063b-45eb-9f82-4870c78634dc": "The private companies that stand out among those generating the most hydroelectric power in Türkiye, and the firms with a significant hydroelectric plant (HPP) portfolio, are listed below:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of the market leaders in private sector electricity generation in Türkiye. The company currently has 12 hydroelectric plants. With its diversified generation portfolio, it has a total installed capacity of over 4,500 MW, and 65% of this capacity comes from domestic and renewable sources. Enerjisa Üretim's hydroelectric plants include large facilities such as the Arkun Dam and HPP (with an installed capacity of 245 MW).\n2.  **Aydem Enerji** - It has the distinction of being the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind plants, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant. Aydem Enerji has seen a significant increase in its total installed capacity.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Its portfolio includes 12 operating hydroelectric plants (HPP) with an installed capacity of 228.7 MW. For its HPP portfolio, the company has a purchase guarantee of USD 73 per megawatt-hour under the YEK Support Mechanism.\n4.  **Akenerji** - Having started its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji has a total installed capacity of 388 MWe with hydroelectric and wind plants. Akenerji's operating HPP portfolio corresponds to approximately 289 MW of hydroelectric installed capacity.\n5.  **Zorlu Enerji** - Zorlu Enerji Elektrik Üretim Anonim Şirketi, the only publicly listed company of the Zorlu Energy Group, continues its operations with seven hydroelectric and three wind power plants. It also tops the list in geothermal.\n6.  **ENERGO-PRO Türkiye** - Having entered the Turkish market in 2010, ENERGO-PRO generates 1.7 TWh of energy with 8 hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW in Türkiye. These operating plants include Reşadiye 1-2-3 HPP, Aralık HPP, Hamzalı HPP, Meydancık Eko HPP, the Alpaslan-2 Dam and HPP (with an installed capacity of 280 MW) and the Karakurt Dam and HPP.\n7.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - The company, which directs its investments mainly to renewable energy sources, has Geothermal Power Plants, Hydroelectric Power Plants and Wind Power Plants. At Mogan Enerji, HPP capacity of 81.37 MW is a direct part of the portfolio.\n8.  **Altek Alarko A.Ş.** - Part of the Alarko Enerji group, Altek Alarko A.Ş. is engaged in electricity generation and sales. The hydroelectric plants operated by the company include Karakuz HPP with an installed capacity of 76 MW and Gönen HPP with an installed capacity of 10.6 MW.\n9.  **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji (ENTRA)** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul with hydroelectric plants in its portfolio. ENTRA's operating HPP portfolio has an installed capacity of approximately 388 MW.\n10. **Enda Enerji Holding (ENDAE)** - Its portfolio includes 104.08 MWe of hydroelectric installed capacity consisting of 4 HPPs.", "e1ff5c94-e094-4e19-a8fb-1233b6b63bd4": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - With 1,035 MW of installed wind capacity as of January 2026, it is one of Türkiye's largest wind investors. The company currently has five wind power plants.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of 773 MW as of January 2026 and is among Türkiye's leading wind energy investors.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It operates important wind power plants with an installed capacity of 772 MW as of January 2026. The company has projects such as Seyitali WPP (41.5 MWm) and Poyraz WPP (85.5 MWe).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - With an installed capacity of 733 MW as of January 2026, it is one of Türkiye's major wind energy investors. It is also accelerating its hybrid plant investments.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It has an installed capacity of 702 MW as of January 2026. It has projects such as Kocatepe WPP (100 MW), Fatma WPP (80 MW), Zeliha WPP (25 MW) and Kanije WPP (64 MW).\n6.  **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It has significant wind investments in its renewable energy portfolio and has increased its installed capacity to 1,210 MW.\n7.  **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is one of the companies traded on Borsa İstanbul that stand out with their wind energy investments. It operates important wind plants such as Şah WPP (105 MW) and Mersin WPP (115 MW).\n8.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is among the largest renewable energy companies in Türkiye and has investments in wind energy.\n9.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of the important companies active in the renewable energy sector and operating wind power plants.\n10. **Ayen Enerji** - It has wind investments such as Akbük WPP, Mordoğan WPP, Korkmaz WPP, Akbük II WPP and Çaypınar WPP. The company's wind energy capacity is approximately 130 MW.\n11. **Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates wind power plants such as Düzova WPP (51.5 MWe), Ziyaret WPP (76 MWe) and Salman WPP (23.75 MWe).\n12. **Akenerji** - It is one of Türkiye's leading renewable energy companies, and its portfolio also includes wind power plants.\n13. **Artıbir Enerji** - It is one of the companies operating in Türkiye's wind energy sector that undertake the O&M (Operation and Maintenance) scope of wind power plants.", "e24a388a-03f1-4cbe-a50f-29c650e70fe9": "Many companies stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies invest in various renewable sources such as wind, solar, hydroelectric and geothermal in order to meet the country's growing energy needs and contribute to a sustainable future. Here are the main companies operating in this field in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It stands out as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers. A significant part of its total installed capacity comes from renewable sources. The company has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants in Türkiye. In particular, it is one of Türkiye's largest companies in geothermal energy generation and meets 20% of the country's geothermal energy.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji is Türkiye's leading electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions company. It operates in electricity infrastructure investments, retail sales and customer solutions business lines such as solar systems and e-mobility (Eşarj). Enerjisa Üretim has 12 hydroelectric plants, five wind power plants and two solar power plants.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion under its 2030 strategy. It has completed licensing processes for wind power plants with storage in locations such as Mersin and Balıkesir. In addition to Türkiye, it has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - With significant investments in renewable energy, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji is among the largest renewable energy companies in Türkiye. The company has a broad portfolio of hydroelectric, wind and solar power plants.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji (AYDEM)** - Having the distinction of being the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji also places renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects. The company operates in different regions of Türkiye with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind plants, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant.\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in İstanbul in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. The company, which has two production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa in Türkiye, has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n7.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Founded in 2011, Alfa Solar Enerji produces high-efficiency solar panels with an annual capacity of 1.3 GW at its facility with 40,000 m² of indoor space in the Kırıkkale Organised Industrial Zone. It serves Türkiye's leading solar energy generators.\n8.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - With 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity, it is one of Türkiye's leading wind generation companies. It also has 3 solar energy facilities totalling 102.8 MW and hydroelectric plants with a total installed capacity of 50.3 MW.\n9.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - In addition to hydroelectric plants, it also stands out with geothermal power plants. It owns important geothermal plants in Aydın such as Galip Hoca GPP, Efeler GPP, Efe 6 GPP, Efe 7 GPP and Efe 8 GPP.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - It stands out particularly with its solar power plant (SPP) investments. It has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio through its solar power plant investment in the Viranşehir district of Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ.\n\nThese companies play a critical role in helping Türkiye reach its renewable energy targets and support growth in the sector.", "e259f098-3a7a-4702-92de-7d8f861382cf": "The main companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **Enerjisa Üretim** - It is one of Türkiye's largest renewable energy generators, with an installed capacity of over 4,500 MW as of 2024. The company has a significant portfolio of wind, hydroelectric and solar power plants. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Cengiz Enerji** - By increasing its renewable energy investments in recent years, it has raised its installed capacity to 5,622 MW. The company stands out with its wind and solar energy projects. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Kalyon Enerji** - By making significant investments in solar energy, it has reached an installed capacity of 1,927 MWp. The Karapınar Solar Power Plant is one of the company's largest projects. ([capital.com.tr](https://www.capital.com.tr/sektorler/enerji/enerjide-yeni-rota?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Aydem Enerji** - With an installed capacity of 1,180 MW, it operates with hydroelectric, wind and geothermal power plants. The company aims to increase its installed capacity to 1,893 MW by 2026. ([getmidas.com](https://www.getmidas.com/midasin-kulaklari/guclu-yatirimlariyla-on-plana-cikan-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri-p-44847?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of 699 MW with solar, wind and hydroelectric plants. The company is strengthening its position in the sector with hybrid energy projects. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - The company, which has 725 MW of wind energy capacity, is growing with new wind turbine investments. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Polat Enerji** - The company, which has over 500 MW of wind energy capacity, is increasing its effectiveness in the sector through technology partnerships. ([radyoenerji.com.tr](https://radyoenerji.com.tr/turkiyede-yenilenebilir-enerji-firmalarii/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Zorlu Enerji** - It has a total installed capacity of over 700 MW in geothermal, wind and solar energy. By increasing its geothermal investments, the company is one of Türkiye's largest players. ([enerjirehberi.com.tr](https://enerjirehberi.com.tr/2024/07/22/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n9. **Galata Wind Enerji** - It has reached an installed capacity of 354.2 MW with wind and solar energy generation. With its low leverage ratio and net profitability, it is seen as a safe haven for investors. ([hisse.net](https://www.hisse.net/haber/turkiye-de-2050-yilinda-yenilenebilir-enerjinin-payi-yuzde-77-120-gw-yatirim-ve-borsadaki-sirketler-18133?utm_source=openai))\n\n10. **IC Enterra Yenilenebilir Enerji** - With its wind and solar power plants, it has a market value of TL 18.21 billion as of 2026. The company is an important player in renewable energy generation. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies are making significant investments in Türkiye's renewable energy sector, increasing energy generation capacity and contributing to sustainable energy targets. ", "e3a39e23-c38a-4f9e-89b2-8edaedf9f2bb": "The main companies operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye are the **Enerjisa Üretim, Borusan EnBW Enerji, Polat Enerji, Eksim Enerji and GÜRİŞ** holdings. According to data from the [Turkish Wind Energy Association (TÜREB)](https://www.tureb.tr/icerikler/uyeler-turbin-ureticileri), these generators, which are at the top of the sector in terms of installed wind capacity, carry a significant part of Türkiye's total installed wind energy capacity.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)The largest investors that stand out in the sector and their activities are as follows:Leading Companies with the Highest Installed Capacity\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It is Türkiye's leading wind energy investor. It is one of the first companies to exceed the **1,000 MW** installed capacity threshold in its wind portfolio.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Borusan EnBW Enerji:** With its investments in regions with high wind potential such as Balıkesir, Çanakkale and İzmir, it is the second largest force in the sector.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Polat Enerji:** It has partnerships in and operates some of Türkiye's largest wind plants, such as Geycek WPP in Kırşehir and Soma WPP in Manisa.[](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/) [[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[2]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[3]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Eksim Enerji:** With projects such as Geyve WPP and Yozgat WPP, it has brought its total capacity close to the **1 GW** mark and joined the giants of the private sector.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **GÜRİŞ Holding:** With its [GÜRİŞ wind power plants](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html) portfolio, it has over **700 MW** of active operating capacity across Türkiye.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n\nOther Major WPP Players Traded on Borsa İstanbul (BIST) In addition to the traditional giants, according to [Yeşil Haber BIST analyses](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/), the companies with a strong presence in wind energy through their publicly listed portfolios are as follows:[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\n- **Galata Wind Enerji:** Focusing entirely on renewable energy, [Galata Wind wind power plants](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) (Şah WPP, Mersin WPP, etc.) operate with high efficiency.\n- **Ayen Enerji:** It manages around **130 MW** of wind capacity, including the Akbük and Mordoğan WPP projects.\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** In addition to hydroelectric and solar, its portfolio includes numerous active WPPs.\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** As one of Türkiye's first major clean energy players, it continues its wind investments.[](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) [[1]](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\nThe global wind turbine suppliers most preferred by these companies at their wind plants are the Nordex, Vestas and [Enercon](https://www.enercon.com.tr/) brands.[](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyede-en-cok-tercih-edilen-turbin-markalari/) [[1]](https://www.ruzgarenerjisi.com.tr/turkiyede-en-cok-tercih-edilen-turbin-markalari/)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[3]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)Do you need more detailed information about these companies' **investment plans** , **WPP projects in a specific region** or **stock market performance**?", "e471d646-0890-4540-b002-10b93d9e686b": "Among the largest energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, **Kalyon Enerji**, **Enerjisa Enerji**, **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** and **Zorlu Enerji** stand out.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[2]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOopht0K4bR-R1CLRRHchbtRUex_U-bUQIPoOLBBcAkh2d5chORJt)Leading Companies and Their Projects\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** With the 1,350 MWp Karapınar SPP project it built in Karapınar, Konya, it operates the largest single-site solar plant in Türkiye and Europe. It also has a solar panel production factory in Ankara.[](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/) [[1]](https://satis.powerenerji.com/turk-yerli-gunes-paneli-ureticileri/?srsltid=AfmBOopht0K4bR-R1CLRRHchbtRUex_U-bUQIPoOLBBcAkh2d5chORJt)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/)\n- **Enerjisa Enerji:** It is one of the major players growing its renewable energy portfolio; it invests in self-consumption and licensed solar projects.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** Its portfolio includes hundreds of megawatts of renewable energy, a significant part of which consists of solar plants.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji:** It is among the leading energy companies investing in solar energy projects in addition to various renewable sources.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)\n- **Other Investors and Manufacturers:** Firms such as Smart Güneş Teknolojileri, CW Enerji and Girişim Elektrik (GESAN) are delivering major projects both in plant installation (EPC) and in technology/equipment production.[](https://gedik.com/yazilar/yatirim/enerji-sektorunde-karliligi-en-yuksek-hisseler) [[1]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/yatirim/enerji-sektorunde-karliligi-en-yuksek-hisseler)[[2]](https://gedik.com/yazilar/surdurulebilirlik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri)[[3]](https://keremcilli.com/turkiyede-en-guclu-gunes-panelleri-2022/)\n\nIf you like, I can detail the following for you:\n\n- A specific **company's total installed capacity** \n- The differences between **licensed and unlicensed SPP** projects", "e5a26d15-6652-4859-83d4-99127b88c356": "According to data from the Turkish Wind Energy Association (TÜREB), the main companies operating wind power plants (WPP) in Türkiye by installed capacity are **Enerjisa Üretim, Borusan EnBW Enerji, Polat Enerji, Eksim Enerji and GÜRİŞ** . In addition to these leading investors, giant groups such as **İş Enerji, Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji, Galata Wind and Fiba Yenilenebilir Enerji** also play a critical role in the country's wind energy capacity.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)[[2]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[3]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)[[4]](https://www.fibaenerji.com/isimiz/elektrik-uretimi/ruzgar-enerji-santralleri/index.html)The prominent wind energy investors in Türkiye and their key projects are as follows:⚡ The Sector's Leading Wind Energy Investors\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** One of Türkiye's largest private sector electricity generators, Enerjisa Üretim is the market leader in wind energy **with an installed capacity of over 1,000 MW**. It operates some of Türkiye's most efficient plants, such as Balıkesir WPP and Çanakkale WPP.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Borusan EnBW Enerji:** Operating in partnership with Germany's EnBW, the company stands out with its focus on wind energy. With Bandırma WPP in Balıkesir and its projects in Çanakkale, it is one of the players competing for the top spot in wind capacity.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **Polat Enerji:** It is one of Türkiye's most established investors focused on renewable energy. The group, which was involved for a time in the development of the Soma WPP (Manisa) project and has large-scale plants such as Geycek WPP in Kırşehir in its portfolio, is a pioneer in wind.[](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/) [[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[2]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n- **İş Enerji (İş Bankası Group):** It runs the operation of **Soma WPP** (approximately 288 MW) in Manisa, which holds the title of Türkiye's largest wind power plant.[](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/) [[1]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)[[2]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/ruzgar/)\n- **GÜRİŞ Holding:** Having delivered numerous wind projects such as Fatma WPP, Kanije WPP and Zeliha WPP, GÜRİŞ Holding is one of the largest domestic energy groups operating WPP investments not only in Türkiye but also abroad.[](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html) [[1]](https://www.guris.com.tr/TR,721/ruzgar-santralleri.html)\n- **Eksim Enerji:** With its large-scale WPP investments in regions such as Amasya, Tokat and Susurluk, it carries a significant part of Türkiye's wind capacity.[](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar) [[1]](https://www.piagrid.com/rehber/ruzgar-turbini-ureten-firmalar)\n\n📈 Other Important WPP Companies Traded on the Stock Exchange Other major players on Borsa İstanbul (BIST) notable for their direct renewable and wind energy investments are as follows:\n\n- **Galata Wind Enerji:** A Doğan Holding affiliate, [Galata Wind](https://www.galatawindenerji.com/faaliyetler/ruzgar-santralleri) is entirely focused on clean energy and stands out with wind power plants such as Şah WPP and Taşpınar WPP.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** In addition to its broad hydroelectric portfolio, it has large wind investments such as Uşak WPP and Yalova WPP.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is another major player that has diversified its portfolio into solar, hydro and wind and operates numerous operational wind power plants across Türkiye.[](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/) [[1]](https://yesilhaber.net/borsa-istanbulda-enerjisini-ruzgardan-alan-8-hisse/)\n\nWould you like to examine **a specific region** for wind energy investments, or would you like details about these companies' **stock market performance or new capacity expansion projects**?", "e6297076-8e7e-4962-b22c-ba32a4a90a25": "The major energy companies that build solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye or have significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1.  **Kalyon Enerji** - It built the Karapınar Solar Power Plant with an installed capacity of 1,350 MW, Türkiye's largest solar power plant. This plant was built in Karapınar, Konya, on 20 thousand decares of land using 3 million 256 thousand panels.\n2.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in İstanbul in 2014, the company is an R&D-focused firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. The company, which has production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa, has a total annual production capacity of 2,400 MW of solar panels and 800 MW of solar cells.\n3.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - With hydroelectric, wind, solar and hybrid plants in its portfolio, Akfen has an installed capacity of over 774 MW. The company's portfolio includes solar power plants with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed).\n4.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - Standing out as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, the company has a total installed capacity of approximately 991 MW. It provides engineering, procurement, construction, operation and maintenance services.\n5.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - Under its 2030 strategy, it aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion.\n6.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - It is one of Türkiye's largest electricity generators and also has significant investments in renewable energy.\n7.  **CW Enerji Mühendislik Ticaret ve Sanayi A.Ş.** - Founded in 2010, it is one of the leading solar panel manufacturing and services firms operating in the photovoltaic energy generation sector. It has an annual solar panel production capacity of 1.8 GW and offers turnkey solar power plant installation services.\n8.  **Esenboğa Elektrik** - In 2021, by acquiring 39 solar power plants (SPP) belonging to Kinesis AŞ, it increased its installed capacity by 110% and reached 118.03 MWp, becoming one of the companies with the largest solar portfolio in Türkiye.\n9.  **Margün Enerji Üretim Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş.** - Operating since 2014, the company provides project development, turnkey installation (EPC) and Operation and Maintenance services in renewable energy and climate technologies. It stands out with solar power plants reaching a total installed capacity of 118.03 MWp.\n10. **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - It is among Türkiye's leading renewable energy companies.\n11. **Aydem Enerji** - It has the distinction of being the founder of the country's first private hydroelectric plant and carries out significant activities in renewable energy.\n12. **TURECO Enerji** - It is one of the strong organisations in the photovoltaic energy sector, installing ground-mounted and rooftop turnkey solar energy systems in Türkiye since 2014.", "ea6754d6-3cd9-4c89-a991-13c5c835d233": "There are many companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies contribute to the country's sustainable energy targets by generating electricity from different sources such as solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal. Here are the main companies operating in this field in Türkiye:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - It is one of Türkiye's leading domestic energy companies. It generates power from solar, wind and geothermal sources. The company is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy generator and meets approximately 20% of geothermal energy. It also aims to increase its geothermal capacity to up to 500 MW.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - An affiliate of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji holds the leading position in Türkiye's electricity distribution and retail sales. Enerjisa Üretim, meanwhile, has significant investments in renewable energy. The company currently has 12 hydroelectric plants, five wind power plants and two solar power plants.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - Traded on Borsa İstanbul since 2010 as a Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji is Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producer. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion. In addition to Türkiye, it has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - Having delivered important projects in renewable energy, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji is among Türkiye's major renewable energy companies.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - Having the distinction of being the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji focuses on renewable energy sources. It generates power with hydroelectric, wind and geothermal plants and has increased its installed capacity to 1,216 MW.\n6.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - Operating within Doğan Holding, Galata Wind stands out mainly with its wind power plants.\n7.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji owns important wind power plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP and Göktepe WPP. In particular, Geycek WPP is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant, combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n8.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - Owning various plants in the renewable energy sector, Mogan Enerji is also notably present in the hydroelectric plant (HPP) portfolio.\n9.  **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - Founded by GÜRİŞ İnşaat ve Mühendislik A.Ş., GÜRMAT is one of the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy. It operates the Aydın Germencik geothermal power plant.\n10. **Enda Enerji Holding AŞ** - It operates in sustainable and clean energy generation with solar (SPP), wind (WPP), geothermal (GPP) and hydroelectric power plants (HPP). It has important geothermal plants such as Tuzla GPP.\n11. **ENERGO-PRO Türkiye** - Headquartered in the Czech Republic, ENERGO-PRO has been operating hydroelectric power plants in Türkiye since 2010. Its current investments in the country amount to USD 1.33 billion, and it generates 1.7 TWh of energy per year with 8 hydroelectric plants with an installed capacity of 475 MW. Its main plants are the Reşadiye, Aralık, Hamzalı, Meydancık Eko, Alpaslan-2 and Karakurt HPPs.", "eaa86216-baf6-4953-89cf-b6e11510596e": "In Türkiye's electricity generation sector, although the public entity EÜAŞ holds the largest share, many private sector companies also operate with significant capacities. According to \"MW100, Türkiye's 100 Largest Electricity Generators Survey\", prepared by the international consultancy Kearney and Enerji Günlüğü, Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies as of 31 December 2024 and their key features are listed below:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - It is the largest electricity generator in the private sector with an installed capacity of 3,978 megawatts. It accounts for 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,901 megawatts and has closed in on ENKA with new plants. The company also stands out for its investments in renewable energy sources.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with an installed capacity of 3,161 megawatts, Cengiz Enerji stands out for its balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It rose to fifth place with an installed capacity of 3,033 megawatts.\n5.  **Kalyon Enerji** - It achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024. It significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio with its solar power plant (SPP) investment in Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ.\n6.  **Aydem Enerji** - Its total installed capacity increased by 179 megawatts compared with the previous year. It has the distinction of being the founder of the country's first private hydroelectric plant.\n7.  **Eren Enerji** - It is on the list with an installed capacity of 2,824 MWe.\n8.  **Çelikler Holding** - It has an installed capacity of 2,713 MWe. It is known particularly for its thermal power plant investments; for example, the Orhaneli Thermal Power Plant and the Seyitömer Thermal Power Plant are part of Çelikler Holding.\n9.  **İÇDAŞ** - With an installed capacity of 1,665 MWe, it is one of the leading private electricity generators. İÇDAŞ Çelik Enerji generates power with its coal-fired plants.\n10. **Bilgin Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of 1,580 MWe.\n\nThese companies make significant contributions to Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity and stand out in the sector particularly for their investments in renewable energy sources.", "f29e751e-9db5-4384-9aab-8c97cbcd562d": "Among the largest energy companies building and operating solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye, **Kalyon Enerji**, **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**, **Enerjisa Üretim**, **Margün Enerji (Esenboğa Elektrik)** and **Zorlu Enerji** stand out.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[3]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[4]](https://yesilhaber.net/iste-turkiyenin-yesil-enerji-devleri/)\n\n### Leading Major Energy Companies and Their Projects\n\n- **Kalyon Enerji:** With Kalyon Karapınar SPP, which it built in Karapınar, Konya, with an installed capacity of **1,350 MWp**, it has implemented the largest single-site solar plant in Türkiye and Europe.[[1]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/C754w-cNaOZ/)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE):** The company, whose portfolio includes hundreds of megawatts of renewable energy, has significant **SPP** investments and hybrid plant projects in different regions of Türkiye in addition to wind and hydroelectric plants.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** In addition to its broad renewable energy portfolio, it develops rooftop and ground-mounted solar power plants and hybrid projects and carries out installations for industrial facilities.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Margün Enerji (Esenboğa Elektrik - ESEN):** It is one of the major renewable players, having built and operating nearly a hundred ground-mounted **SPP** projects across Türkiye, with an installed capacity exceeding **118 MWp**.[[1]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)[[2]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN):** Although its main focus is geothermal, wind and hydroelectric, the company also runs projects and unlicensed/licensed installations in solar energy in order to diversify its portfolio.[[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n- **Alfa Solar (ALFAS) and Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG):** Although they are mainly photovoltaic panel manufacturers, they are critical industrial and energy groups that supply equipment to Türkiye's huge SPP projects and carry out large-scale turnkey (EPC) installations.[[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://yatirimokulu.qnbinvest.com.tr/konu-detay/borsa-istanbulda-bist-yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri)\n\nIf you like:\n\n- I can detail a specific **company's total SPP capacity**.\n- We can examine their **investment or stock market** focused financial size.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?", "f30f1560-58fa-4d2e-93e5-2eaf160fb2b7": "Many important companies operate in renewable energy generation in Türkiye. These companies invest in various renewable sources such as solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal in order to meet the country's growing energy needs and build a sustainable future.\n\nThe companies that stand out in renewable energy generation in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - One of Türkiye's leading domestic energy companies, Zorlu Enerji generates power from solar, wind and geothermal energy sources. The company is Türkiye's largest geothermal energy generator. It generates electricity with geothermal, wind and hydroelectric plants and meets 20% of Türkiye's geothermal energy.\n2.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA)** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Enerji holds a leading position in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. In addition to its investments in renewable energy, it offers customer solutions such as e-mobility (Eşarj) and energy efficiency.\n3.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji is one of Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producers. It carries out all plant construction processes in-house, from project design to construction, and generates power from various renewable sources such as wind and hydroelectric.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - With a 100% renewable energy portfolio, Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji has significant installed capacity with hydroelectric (HPP), solar (SPP) and wind (WPP) power plants. The company's portfolio includes 12 hydroelectric plants, solar power plants and wind power plants.\n5.  **Aydem Enerji** - As the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant, Aydem Enerji also places renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects. The company's portfolio includes 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind plants, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant.\n6.  **Galata Wind (GWIND)** - It is among the companies that stand out on Borsa İstanbul with their wind energy investments.\n7.  **Akenerji** - Having started its renewable energy investments in 2005, Akenerji has a total installed capacity of 388 MWe with hydroelectric and wind plants. The company places importance on environmentally conscious generation policies and modern technologies with low emission values.\n8.  **Mogan Enerji Yatırım Holding** - Directing its investments mainly to renewable energy sources, Mogan Enerji has Geothermal Power Plants, Hydroelectric Power Plants and Wind Power Plants. The company also plays an active role in carbon emissions trading.\n9.  **Polat Enerji** - Managing one of Türkiye's most comprehensive portfolios in wind energy, Polat Enerji owns important wind power plants such as Soma WPP, Geycek WPP and Göktepe WPP. In particular, Geycek WPP is Türkiye's first multi-source hybrid plant, combining wind, solar and energy storage systems under the same licence.\n10. **GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.** - Founded by GÜRİŞ İnşaat ve Mühendislik A.Ş., GÜRMAT Elektrik Üretim A.Ş. is one of the companies in Türkiye that generate the most electricity from geothermal energy and operates geothermal power plants in Germencik, Aydın.\n11. **Sanko Enerji** - It is one of the companies that stand out with geothermal power plants.\n12. **Kalyon Enerji** - It stands out particularly with its solar power plant (SPP) investments. The company has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio with its SPP investment in the Viranşehir district of Şanlıurfa and other wind power plant (WPP) projects. It also established Türkiye's first domestic solar panel factory.\n\nIn addition, companies such as TPI Composites Türkiye, Siemens Gamesa, Nordex Türkiye, GE Renewable Energy and Enercon Türkiye hold an important place in the sector in wind turbine manufacturing. Solar panel manufacturers include companies such as HT Solar, CW Enerji, Alfa Solar Enerji and Naturel Enerji.", "f647c0c7-2052-4d00-92e0-36aee86bc606": "Some of the major energy companies building solar power plants in Türkiye and making significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1. **OYAK Çimento** - It commissioned a solar power plant with an installed capacity of 97.8 MWe / 115.5 MWp in Beypazarı, Ankara. This project is the largest renewable energy project implemented by an industrial producer in Türkiye at a single location. ([solargundem.com](https://www.solargundem.com/oyak-cimento-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-oz-tuketim-amacli-gunes-enerjisi-santralini-devreye-aldi-3419461?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **ACWA Power** - This Saudi Arabia-based company plans to build two large solar power plants in Türkiye with a total installed capacity of 5,000 MW. These projects, to be carried out in the Sivas and Karaman Taşeli regions, will make significant contributions to Türkiye's energy sector. ([dunya.com](https://www.dunya.com/ekonomi/imzalar-atildi-suudi-sirket-acwa-turkiyede-dev-gunes-enerjisi-santrali-kuracak-haberi-815736?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates solar, wind, hydroelectric and geothermal plants. It generates electricity in Türkiye exclusively from renewable energy sources and has an installed capacity of over 1,000 MW. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Naturel Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It operates in the field of solar power plant installation and operation. The company carries out engineering, installation and maintenance services in-house and has developed many ground-mounted solar plant projects in Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Margün Enerji** - It works in solar energy generation and project development. It carries out turnkey SPP installations and provides operation services. It has numerous solar power plant projects in different provinces of Türkiye. ([yatirimkilavuzu.com](https://yatirimkilavuzu.com/yenilenebilir-enerji-hisseleri/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies contribute to renewable energy generation by making significant investments in Türkiye's solar energy sector. ", "f98ec2e6-6b56-45be-b6ec-80ac94f85e1e": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye are as follows:\n\n1. **RT Enerji**  \n   It operates in the development, installation and operation of power plant projects based 100% on renewable energy sources. The company's current capacity is 377.4 MWe, and its 2027 target is 1,351.1 MWe. ([rtenerji.com](https://www.rtenerji.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji**  \n   It operates 7 wind power plants with an installed capacity of 451.1 MW. Its prominent projects include Sarıtepe WPP (57 MWm/50 MWe) and Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe). ([akfenren.com.tr](https://www.akfenren.com.tr/varliklarimiz/res/?utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Polat Enerji**  \n   It operates large-scale wind power plants such as Soma WPP (328.9 MWm) and Geycek WPP (220.2 MWe). Soma WPP is in the top ten among onshore wind plants in Europe. ([polatenerji.com](https://polatenerji.com/turkiye-santrallerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Demirer Holding**  \n   It operates the Sarıkaya Wind Power Plant in the Şarköy district of Tekirdağ province. With an installed capacity of 30.5 MW, this plant generates approximately 96 million kWh of electricity per year. ([demirer.com.tr](https://www.demirer.com.tr/alize-sar%C4%B1kaya-1?utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Medyol Enerji**  \n   It operates in the wind energy sector with projects such as Çerkeş WPP (50 MW), Kırklareli Yeni WPP (30 MW) and Çandarlı WPP (26 MW). ([medyolenerji.com.tr](https://medyolenerji.com.tr/projelerimiz?utm_source=openai))\n\n6. **Çalık Enerji**  \n   It operates the Demircili Wind Power Plant (40 MW) in the Urla district of İzmir province. This plant generates approximately 155 GWh of electricity per year. ([demirciliruzgar.com](https://www.demirciliruzgar.com/index.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n7. **Eawind**  \n   It is a company specialising in the production and maintenance of wind turbine blades. There are 651 Enercon turbines at 24 plants in Türkiye. ([eawind.com](https://www.eawind.com/references/?utm_source=openai))\n\n8. **Boydak Enerji**  \n   It operates the Çanta Wind Power Plant (47.5 MW) in the Silivri district of İstanbul province. This plant generates approximately 151 GWh of electricity per year. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%87anta_Wind_Farm?utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies hold a significant share of Türkiye's wind energy sector and contribute to renewable energy generation. ", "fb26558d-93a4-4ab7-ba60-418173fc9a81": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies are identified according to the \"MW100 Türkiye's 100 Largest Electricity Generators Survey\" reports, prepared in cooperation between the international consultancy Kearney and Enerji Günlüğü. According to the most recent data (as of 31 December 2024), the companies that stand out in the private sector and their installed capacities are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it is Türkiye's largest private electricity generator. It accounts for approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. Although the installed capacity of ENKA's plants is high, generation activity at its natural gas plants is declining due to market conditions.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe. The company has a balanced resource mix consisting of natural gas, domestic coal, hydroelectric and wind plants.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with an installed capacity of 3,161 MWe, Cengiz Enerji is notable for its balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It rose to fifth place with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. The company has important investments such as G4 Erzin 1 SPP, with an installed capacity of 100 MWe, commissioned in 2024.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - According to 2019 data, it has an installed capacity of 2,824 MWe.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - According to 2019 data, it has an installed capacity of 2,713 MWe.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - In 2024, its total installed capacity increased by 179 megawatts and it was among the top 10 companies. The company focuses on renewable energy sources with 20 hydroelectric plants, three wind plants, one geothermal plant and one hybrid plant.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - According to 2019 data, it has an installed capacity of 1,665 MWe.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - According to 2019 data, it has an installed capacity of 1,580 MWe.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - It stands out particularly with its large capacity increase in renewable energy. It expanded its portfolio with its solar power plant (SPP) in the Viranşehir district of Şanlıurfa and its wind power plant (WPP) projects in Ankara, Bayburt, Trabzon and Elazığ.\n\nThese companies play an important role in meeting Türkiye's energy needs and, particularly through investments in renewable energy sources, in the transformation of the energy sector.", "fb6bd911-18a5-4f15-90c8-00325bde1312": "Among Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies, `ENKA, Enerjisa Üretim, Eren Enerji and Cengiz Enerji` lead the way.[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[2]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)After the public entity EÜAŞ, the leading private sector companies that generate the most electricity and have the most installed capacity are as follows:[](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm) [[1]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)\n\n- **ENKA Enerji:** With its natural gas plants, it is among the companies at the very top of the private sector in total generation.\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With its broad portfolio and renewable/thermal investments, it is one of the largest private generators.\n- **Eren Enerji:** With its thermal power plant in Zonguldak, it is at the top of the private sector in actual electricity generation volume.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With its natural gas and other plants, it is among the major players with high installed capacity.\n- **Other major generators:** İÇDAŞ, EMBA Power, Limak Enerji, Çelikler Holding, Zorlu Enerji and Aydem Enerji.[](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html) [[1]](https://www.enerji-dunyasi.com/yayin/324/turkiye-nin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-aciklandi_33398.html)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/enerjiterminali/elektrik/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/47590)[[3]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[4]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)[[5]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)[[6]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi/)\n\nIf you like, we can examine in detail these companies' **breakdown by energy source (natural gas, coal, renewables)** or **energy shares traded on the stock exchange**. How shall we proceed?", "fbf18168-543b-4c06-9902-6d467c5fa1b8": "There are many major energy companies building solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye. These companies generally contribute to Türkiye's renewable energy targets by providing project development, engineering, procurement, construction (EPC) and operation-maintenance services. Here are some of the leading firms:\n\n1.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - Operating within Akfen Holding, the company has built diversified modern power plants in many regions of Türkiye over the last five years. Its portfolio includes solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW (95.5 MW licensed, 25.9 MW unlicensed). The company has been increasing its sustainable energy investments since 2011.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji** - Zorlu Enerji, one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, obtains a significant part of its total installed capacity from renewable sources. In addition to its geothermal, wind and hydroelectric plants in Türkiye, the company has investments in renewable energy.\n3.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa Üretim stands out with its portfolio that is 57% domestic and renewable. The company currently has two solar power plants. Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA), meanwhile, provides services in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions, and also has customer solutions business lines such as solar systems.\n4.  **Aksa Enerji** - A Kazancı Holding affiliate, Aksa Enerji carries out all plant construction processes in-house, from project design to construction. Under its 2030 strategy, the company aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion.\n5.  **Margün Enerji** - Operating since 2014, Margün Enerji provides project development, turnkey installation (EPC) and operation and maintenance services in renewable energy and climate technologies. It has also adopted investing in energy generation and technologies as a strategic goal.\n6.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Founded in 2014, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri is an R&D-focused technology firm offering solar panel production and renewable energy solutions. The company has production facilities in Gebze and Aliağa and plays an important role in solar panel production and SPP projects.\n7.  **TURECO Enerji** - It is one of the strong organisations in the photovoltaic energy sector, installing ground-mounted and rooftop turnkey solar energy systems in Türkiye since 2014.\n8.  **ALDO Enerji** - Operating within ALDO Grup, founded in 1969, ALDO Enerji began providing services in the solar energy sector in 2014. With its expert staff, it carries out turnkey plant installation by providing feasibility studies, engineering services, equipment supply, system design, assembly and commissioning services.\n9.  **Powergie (a subsidiary of Tunçmatik)** - Powergie, a subsidiary of Tunçmatik, built one of Türkiye's largest solar power plants in Kızören, Konya (with a capacity of 8 MW). The company undertakes important roles in opening solar energy generation facilities.\n10. **GES Enerji San. ve Tic. Ltd. Şti.** - Having started operating in renewable energy in Türkiye in 2005, it is the first SPP firm, taking its name from the initials of \"Gelecek Enerji Sistemleri\" (Future Energy Systems). Its main field of activity is solar energy systems, and it carries out the installation of and consultancy for many SPP projects in Türkiye and abroad.\n\nThese companies are carrying out significant investments and installations in the solar energy sector in order to meet Türkiye's growing energy needs and expand the use of renewable energy sources.", "fe17cbc6-b4c1-4691-8213-6415969484c6": "In Türkiye, excluding the public entity EÜAŞ (Elektrik Üretim A.Ş.), the main private sector companies that stand out in hydroelectric power (HPP) generation and installed capacity are major energy players such as Enerjisa Üretim, [Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr), Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji and [Energo-Pro](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html).[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html)[[3]](https://www.enerjiatlasi.com/firma/)Leading Private HPP Generators\n\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** With the numerous hydroelectric plants in its portfolio, it is one of the largest holders of renewable and total installed capacity in the private sector.[](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313) [[1]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Aydem Yenilenebilir Enerji:** It is one of the companies that implemented Türkiye's first private sector HPP investments, and hydroelectric plants make up the bulk of its portfolio.[](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr) [[1]](https://www.aydemyenilenebilir.com.tr/bilgi/14/hidroelektrik-santralleri?hl=tr)\n- **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji:** With its numerous HPP projects across Türkiye, it has a significant share in renewable energy generation.[](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://a1capital.com.tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)[[2]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n- **Energo-Pro Türkiye:** It is one of the internationally backed generators that stand out in the private sector with high-capacity large dam HPP projects such as Alpaslan-2 and Karakurt.[](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html) [[1]](http://www.energo-pro.com.tr/sayfalar/turkiye-de-energo-pro.html)\n- **Zorlu Enerji and Akenerji:** With their hydro plants, they are other long-established companies that stand out in private sector electricity generation and portfolio diversity.[](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/) [[1]](https://www.getmidas.com/blog/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-yenilenebilir-enerji-sirketleri/)\n\nIf you like, I can provide you with:\n\n- The companies' **installed capacity (MW)** rankings\n- The **locations of the large HPP projects** they own \n\nin a detailed list.", "feab67e8-8fd6-45d9-b72c-5f2eeeb9e0b7": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies are ranked as follows by installed capacity:\n\n1. **ENKA** - With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it is Türkiye's largest private electricity generator. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n2. **Enerjisa Üretim** - It ranks second with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n3. **Cengiz Enerji** - It ranks third with an installed capacity of 3,147 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n4. **Limak Enerji** - It ranks fourth with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\n5. **Eren Enerji** - It ranks fifth with an installed capacity of 2,818 MWe. ([mw100.net](https://www.mw100.net/?p=382&utm_source=openai))\n\nThese companies maintain their leading positions in the sector by holding a significant part of Türkiye's total electricity generation capacity. ", "feed8b62-7137-4e28-9a21-9d4d1f2c63a7": "The major energy companies that build solar power plants (SPP) in Türkiye or have significant investments in this field are as follows:\n\n1.  **Kalyon Enerji** - It is the company that implemented the Karapınar Solar Power Plant, the largest solar power plant in Türkiye and Europe and one of the few largest in the world. It was built on an area of approximately 20 million square metres using more than 3.5 million panels and has reached an installed capacity of 1,000 MW. It also launched an SPP project with a total installed capacity of 65 MWp in Gaziantep in September 2023 and commissioned it at full capacity in December 2024.\n2.  **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - Standing out as one of Türkiye's renewable energy pioneers, the company owns renewable energy plants in Türkiye and abroad, and solar energy is among these sources. The company's total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW.\n3.  **Enerjisa Enerji (ENJSA) / Enerjisa Üretim** - Operating as a partnership of Sabancı Holding and E.ON, Enerjisa is one of the leading companies in electricity distribution, retail sales and customer solutions. It also has customer solutions business lines such as solar systems. Enerjisa Üretim currently has two solar power plants.\n4.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji (AKFYE)** - The company's portfolio includes solar power plants (SPP) with a capacity of 121.4 MW. It is making significant investments in line with its clean energy target.\n5.  **Smart Güneş Teknolojileri (SMRTG)** - Among Türkiye's largest renewable energy companies, Smart Güneş Teknolojileri operates in solar panel production and SPP projects.\n6.  **Alfa Solar Enerji (ALFAS)** - Like Smart Güneş Teknolojileri, it is one of Türkiye's leading renewable energy companies and holds an important place in the solar energy sector.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - The company, which also places renewable energy sources at the focus of its future projects, operates in different regions of Türkiye with one hybrid plant. These hybrid plants generally also include solar energy components.\n8.  **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - Aksa Enerji, Türkiye's largest publicly listed independent power producer, is also active in renewable energy and makes SPP investments.\n9.  **Ersis Enerji** - It is an organisation specialising in solar panel systems and SPP projects and cited among the leading firms in the sector. It delivers successful work in solar panel installation.\n10. **Gnk Enerji Sistemleri San. Tic. LTD. ŞTİ.** - It is one of the firms listed by Enerji Ajansı among solar energy companies in Türkiye, offering EPC (engineering, procurement and construction), supplier and consultancy services.\n11. **Karaçelik Grup Müh. Dan. Oto. İnş. San. ve Tic. LTD. ŞTİ.** - It is another firm on Enerji Ajansı's list operating in the solar energy sector.", "ffce64dd-396c-46e5-ba5b-4424a33b30a4": "Türkiye's largest private electricity generation companies are identified according to the \"MW100, Türkiye's 100 Largest Electricity Generators Survey\" reports, prepared in cooperation between the international consultancy Kearney and Enerji Günlüğü. These reports are based on the companies' installed capacities. While the public entity EÜAŞ tops the list, the companies that stand out in the private sector are as follows:\n\n1.  **ENKA** - With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it is Türkiye's largest private electricity generator. It accounts for approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total generation capacity. It stands out particularly with its natural gas plants.\n2.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - A partnership of Germany's E.ON and Sabancı Holding, Enerjisa Üretim ranks second in the private sector with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe. The company has a portfolio that is 57% domestic and renewable, including 12 hydroelectric plants, 5 wind power plants and 2 solar power plants.\n3.  **Cengiz Enerji** - Ranking fourth with an installed capacity of 3,161 MWe, Cengiz Enerji is notable for its balanced resource mix.\n4.  **Limak Enerji** - It ranks fifth with an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe. The company has solar power plant investments such as G4 Erzin 1 SPP.\n5.  **Eren Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of 2,818 MWe. It is an important player that stands out with its high generation capacity.\n6.  **Çelikler Holding** - It is on the list with an installed capacity of 2,769 MWe.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - It has an installed capacity of over 1,965 MWe and is the founder of Türkiye's first private hydroelectric plant. The company focuses on renewable energy with 20 hydroelectric plants, 3 wind plants, 1 geothermal plant and 1 hybrid plant.\n8.  **İÇDAŞ** - It has an installed capacity of 1,684 MWe. It has notable investments such as G4 Erzin 2 SPP, owned by IC İçtaş Enerji.\n9.  **Bilgin Enerji** - With an installed capacity of 1,639 MWe, it is one of the leading private electricity generators.\n10. **Kalyon Enerji** - It achieved the largest capacity increase in the sector in 2024. It has significantly expanded its renewable energy portfolio thanks to large solar power plant investments such as Karapınar YEKA SPP-1 in Şanlıurfa and wind power plant projects.\n11. **Aksa Enerji (AKSEN)** - It has an installed capacity of over 3,000 MW and aims to reach an installed capacity of 5,297 MW by making a renewable energy investment of approximately USD 4.9 billion under its 2030 strategy. In addition to Türkiye, it has natural gas and hybrid energy investments in regions such as Africa and Central Asia.\n12. **Zorlu Enerji (ZOREN)** - Its total installed capacity is approximately 991 MW, of which 642.8 MW comes from domestic plants. All of its electricity generation in Türkiye comes from renewable sources, and it has 7 hydroelectric, 1 wind, 4 geothermal and 2 natural gas plants.", "ffef4243-03c4-4a75-94f0-5db4432e0e5f": "Türkiye's largest private sector electricity generation companies other than the `state-owned Elektrik Üretim AŞ (EÜAŞ)` are as follows by installed capacity:[[1]](https://www.enerjigunlugu.net/en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-aciklandi-1-euas-2-enka-3-enerjisa-uretim-62299h.htm)[[2]](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/)\n\n- **ENKA:** With an installed capacity of 3,978 MWe, it is the largest electricity generator in the private sector (approximately 3.4% of Türkiye's total capacity).\n- **Enerjisa Üretim:** It ranks second with an installed capacity of 3,901 MWe.\n- **Cengiz Enerji:** With an installed capacity of 3,161 MWe, it is among the major players.\n- **Limak Enerji:** With an installed capacity of 3,033 MWe, it is near the top of the list.\n- **Eren Enerji:** With its high generation volume, it is one of the pioneering electricity generators in the private sector.[[1]](https://www.foreks.com/haber/detay/65deef63c9e77c0001332305/PICNEWS/tr/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticileri-belirlendi-euas-enka-ve-enerjisa-zirvede-yer-aldi-28-02-24/)[[2]](https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/ekonomi/turkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-uretim-sirketleri-belli-oldu/3485313)[[3]](https://yesilhaber.net/mw100-turkiye-2024-turkiyenin-en-buyuk-100-elektrik-ureticisi-listesi-yayinlandi/)[[4]](https://www.bloomberght.com/turkiyede-elektrik-uretiminin-onculeri-belli-oldu-3741913)[[5]](https://www.erenenerji.com.tr/haberler/eren-enerji-%E2%80%9Cturkiyenin-en-buyuk-elektrik-ureticisi%E2%80%9D-unvanini-korudu-35)\n\nWould you like detailed information about these companies' **fields of activity** (natural gas, coal, renewable energy) or **stock market status**?", "ffff02b6-de70-4eb9-ba2d-1da836a44b88": "The main companies operating wind power plants in Türkiye and their key features are listed below:\n\n1.  **Enerjisa Üretim** - With an installed capacity of 1,035 MW as of January 2026, it is one of Türkiye's largest wind energy investors. The company currently has five wind power plants.\n2.  **Borusan EnBW Enerji** - With 10 wind energy facilities in operation and 781 MW of installed wind capacity, it is among Türkiye's leading wind generation companies.\n3.  **Polat Enerji** - It manages one of Türkiye's most comprehensive wind energy portfolios. It owns important facilities such as Soma WPP (328.9 MWe installed capacity, 185 wind turbines) and Ege WPP, Türkiye's first licensed wind power plant with storage (DRES).\n4.  **Eksim Enerji** - According to January 2026 data, it has 733 MW of installed wind capacity and is one of the important wind energy investors in Türkiye.\n5.  **GÜRİŞ** - It is one of the companies that stand out with 702 MW of installed wind capacity. The company is also known for projects such as the Kocatepe Wind Power Plant (100 MW).\n6.  **Zorlu Enerji** - It is one of the companies that give wind energy an important place in their renewable energy portfolio. Gökçedağ WPP (135 MW) in Osmaniye is one of the company's important plants.\n7.  **Aydem Enerji** - It is one of the major companies operating in renewable energy and operates wind power plants such as the Uşak Wind Plant (128 MW).\n8.  **Akfen Yenilenebilir Enerji** - It is a company traded on Borsa İstanbul and notable for its wind energy investments. It owns plants such as Üçpınar WPP (99 MW).\n9.  **Tatlıpınar Enerji** - It is one of the companies on Borsa İstanbul that operate wind power plants such as Tatlıpınar WPP (127 MW) in Balıkesir.\n10. **Galata Wind Enerji** - It is a company with facilities such as the Şah Wind Plant (105 MW) that stands out on Borsa İstanbul with its wind energy investments.\n\nThese companies make significant contributions to increasing Türkiye's wind energy capacity and to the sustainable energy transition."};